`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"},"9":{"id":"/docs/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`bike-share/1` (share package, `*.bikeshare.zip`) and the customer link"},"10":{"id":"/docs/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"BikePresenter controller API"},"11":{"id":"/docs/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"Embedding on a shop's site"},"12":{"id":"/docs/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"Photo close-ups"},"13":{"id":"/docs/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Open questions (verify on device)"},"14":{"id":"/docs/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."},"15":{"id":"/docs/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools. Exports\n(`Viewer.snapshot` / `recordTurntable`, decisions in `scene/exportMedia.ts`) re-render the model with a\ntransparent clear onto a 2D canvas over the chosen backdrop (CSS gradients redrawn, chroma green, or\nnothing) and optionally the pins (`PinLayer.drawInto`); video goes through `canvas.captureStream` + MediaRecorder."},"16":{"id":"/docs/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path            | Content                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, photos?, imageCount, checklist?: [{ id, label, done }], source?: \"photos\"\\|\"video\", backend? }` (`checklist` is optional and written by iOS; `source`/`backend` only from `tools/reconstruct`) |","table":"table-0"},"17":{"id":"/docs/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path         | Content                                                                                     |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up (`tools/reconstruct` writes `model.glb`, or `.usdz` / `.ply`) |","table":"table-0"},"18":{"id":"/docs/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path         | Content                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16], camera? }] }` (column-major camera→model; `camera: { model, width, height, fx, fy, cx, cy }` in pixels from COLMAP; `width`/`height`/`fx`/`fy` set each photo's field of view in close-up ranking, invalid values are ignored) |","table":"table-0"},"19":{"id":"/docs/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path      | Content                                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos (reconstruction input); `tools/reconstruct`: the JPEG frames |","table":"table-0"},"20":{"id":"/docs/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path      | Content                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/` | optional: JPEG copies of `images/`, same file stems, ≤ 2048 px long edge, EXIF orientation baked into the pixels (orientation 1). Listed as `manifest.photos` |","table":"table-0"},"21":{"id":"/docs/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |","table":"table-0"},"22":{"id":"/docs/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted; when `manifest.photos` names a non-empty folder, its JPEGs are used instead of the HEICs\n(pose `file` names like `IMG_0007.HEIC` match `IMG_0007.jpg` by stem), so no browser needs the\nWASM HEIC decoder. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."},"23":{"id":"/docs/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip-or-toolsreconstruct-package","content":"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."},"24":{"id":"/docs/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"},"25":{"id":"/docs/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."},"26":{"id":"/docs/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."},"27":{"id":"/docs/architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."},"28":{"id":"/docs/architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."},"29":{"id":"/docs/architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."},"30":{"id":"/docs/architecture-28","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."},"31":{"id":"/docs/architecture-29","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."},"32":{"id":"/docs/architecture-30","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"},"33":{"id":"/docs/architecture-31","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."},"34":{"id":"/docs/architecture-32","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."},"35":{"id":"/docs/architecture-33","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, welds the face-varying expansion back into an indexed\nmesh (`../weld.ts`: 2.9M → 0.49M vertices for 1M triangles), waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."},"36":{"id":"/docs/architecture-34","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."},"37":{"id":"/docs/architecture-35","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"Details and measurements: PERFORMANCE.md."},"38":{"id":"/docs/architecture-36","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Render on demand** (`renderScheduler.ts`): the animation loop only runs while something changes.\nViewer methods (`setModel`, `setView`, `applyTransform`, `setBackground`, resize, controls input,\nfly-to) call `viewer.requestRender()`; **code that mutates the three.js scene directly must call it\ntoo**. The shadow map is redrawn only on `requestRender()` (scene changes), never for camera-only\nframes. Frame listeners (`onFrame`, pins) run after drawn frames only."},"39":{"id":"/docs/architecture-37","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Quality** (`quality.ts`): pixel ratio ≤ 2 (1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles),\nMSAA only at 1×, smaller hard shadows on phones; `?quality=low|high` overrides."},"40":{"id":"/docs/architecture-38","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Raycasts** (`bvh.ts`): after the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a\nthree-mesh-bvh hierarchy (built in `bvh.worker.ts` for big meshes, indirect so the GPU index buffer\nis untouched). `viewer.raycastReady` tells the pins when occlusion tests are cheap."},"41":{"id":"/docs/architecture-39","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**Pins** (`pins.ts`): allocation-free projection against a cached viewport size, transform-only\nwrites for pins that moved, `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage,\nocclusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that finish on idle animation frames."},"42":{"id":"/docs/architecture-40","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rendering-and-performance-appswebsrcviewer","content":"**GLB decoders** (`loaders.ts`, `gltfInfo.ts`): `extensionsUsed` decides which of Meshopt, Draco\nand KTX2/Basis is imported; their WASM ships in the build (no CDN)."},"43":{"id":"/docs/architecture-41","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."},"44":{"id":"/docs/architecture-42","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Model transform.** The loader wraps the model so its native bounding box is centered on X/Z\nand rests on y = 0 (`centerOnGround`, deterministic per file); that frame is *model-root space*.\n`model.scale`, `model.rotation` (Euler XYZ, three.js convention) and `model.offset` are then\napplied to the root as `world = offset + R · (scale · p)`. Annotations and hotspot views stay in\nmodel-root space, so re-orienting a capture never detaches a comment. The overview camera is\nframed in world space (camera up is world +Y) and converted back."},"45":{"id":"/docs/architecture-43","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Spec sheet** (`specs?: { label, value }[]`, free text, optional and lenient like the crop: rows\nthat are not two strings are dropped, text is trimmed and capped, at most 40 rows; `scene/specs.ts`).\nRows keep the order staff typed. Present mode shows rows with a value on the first card\n(`PresentView`, so the customer link gets it too); a row with an empty value is kept for staff only."},"46":{"id":"/docs/architecture-44","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Crop box** (`crop?: { min, max, enabled }`, model-root space, optional and lenient: a\nmalformed crop is dropped, swapped corners are reordered). The viewer turns it into six world\nclipping planes on the model's own materials (local clipping, shadows clipped too), recomputed only\nwhen the model transform or the box changes. Raycasts skip hits outside the box (no comments on\ncropped-away parts, no occlusion by them), pins outside it are hidden, and exact bounds (framing,\non-ground, auto-orient samples) only count kept vertices. Edit mode shows the box with one handle\nper face (`viewer/cropBox.ts`): pointer events in the capture phase, so mouse and touch drags never\norbit the camera; the face moves along its axis to the point nearest the pointer ray, clipping\nlive, and the store is updated once on release. \"Fit to bike\" (`scene/crop.ts`, pure) samples\npoints along triangle edges, cuts above the floor slab (a dense, wide band in the lower third of\nthe up axis) and keeps the largest 26-connected voxel cluster with a 2% margin. Area-mode captures\nget that box pre-computed but disabled, a hint in the toast, and auto-orient waits until the crop\nis on. Turning the crop on/off or fitting it re-grounds the visible part."},"47":{"id":"/docs/architecture-45","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"**Auto-orient** (`apps/web/src/scene/orient.ts`, pure, unit-tested). Target frame: +X front,\n+Y up, +Z drive side, tyres on y = 0. Up to 50k strided vertices (≈3 ms for 1M vertices):"},"48":{"id":"/docs/architecture-46","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"PCA: smallest-variance axis = the bike's width, middle axis = candidate up."},"49":{"id":"/docs/architecture-47","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Up sign by votes: the centroid sits below mid-height (wheels), and the top band (handlebar) is\nwider across than the bottom band (two tyre contact patches)."},"50":{"id":"/docs/architecture-48","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Ground line: the longest downward-facing edge of the side-view convex hull (tangent across\nboth tyres) fixes the 5–15° tilt PCA leaves."},"51":{"id":"/docs/architecture-49","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Object Capture output is gravity-aligned, so if that up is within 6° of ±Y, Y is kept exactly\nand only yaw changes (horizontal PCA)."},"52":{"id":"/docs/architecture-50","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"Front sign: the wide handlebar sits ahead of centre (plus a small vote for the drivetrain mass\nbehind it). Drive side follows from the right-handed frame."},"53":{"id":"/docs/architecture-51","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"It runs once when a scene is opened with a non-demo model, no comments and no `model.rotation`\n(`shouldAutoOrient`); the offset is then recomputed from exact bounds so the bike stands on the\nground. Edit → Model exposes the result plus manual rotate/flip/scale/nudge, each one store\nupdate and so one step of the scene's undo history (`SceneStore`: every edit pushes the previous\nscene, edits with the same merge key less than a second apart share a step, `replace` is not a\nstep and a new scene id clears the history; Ctrl/Cmd+Z in Edit mode). Generate tilted test bundles with\n`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --rotate 70,25,-40` (ASCII USD mesh in `model.usdz`)."},"54":{"id":"/docs/architecture-52","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"Share → \"Export share package\" turns a local capture into a self-contained zip\n(`apps/web/src/scene/share.ts`):"},"55":{"id":"/docs/architecture-53","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path              | Content                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-share.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-share/1\", id, name, createdAt, scene, model, photos }` |","table":"table-1"},"56":{"id":"/docs/architecture-54","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path              | Content                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `scene.bike.json` | the `bike-scene/1` scene, model URL rewritten to the packaged file |","table":"table-1"},"57":{"id":"/docs/architecture-55","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path                 | Content      |\n| -------------------- | ------------ |\n| `model.glb\\|usdz\\|…` | the 3D model |","table":"table-1"},"58":{"id":"/docs/architecture-56","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"| Path           | Content                                      |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/*.jpg` | the close-ups referenced by `Hotspot.photos` |","table":"table-1"},"59":{"id":"/docs/architecture-57","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`tools/publish-scene.mjs` validates a package (size limits: zip 300 MB, model 250 MB, JSON 2 MB,\n8 MB × 64 photos; JPEG only; no paths outside the package; `parseScene`) and installs it under\n`apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`. The customer link is\n`…/app/?scene=scenes/<id>/scene.bike.json&view=present` (`kiosk=1&interval=<s>&idle=<s>` for a\nshop screen). Scene, model and photo URLs must be same-origin or https."},"60":{"id":"/docs/architecture-58","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-share1-share-package-bikesharezip-and-the-customer-link","content":"`src/entry.ts` loads only `present/BikePresenter.ts` for `?view=present`, so customers never\ndownload editing code. `&area=<hotspot id or index>` opens the link on an area."},"61":{"id":"/docs/architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"`mountPresenter(container, options)` (`present/BikePresenter.ts`) renders the customer view into\nan element or a shadow root and sizes itself from it. Options: `scene` (a `bike-scene/1` object or\na scene URL, checked by `loadPublishedScene`), `pageHref`, `header`, `share`, `background`,\n`kiosk: { interval, idle, autoplay }`, `autofocus`, `area`. The returned controller:"},"62":{"id":"/docs/architecture-60","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member  |                                                                                     |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ready` | promise, resolves once the model is shown or the error is displayed (never rejects) |","table":"table-2"},"63":{"id":"/docs/architecture-61","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member                                   |                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `scene`, `areas`, `areaIndex`, `playing` | state; `areas[0]` is the whole bike |","table":"table-2"},"64":{"id":"/docs/architecture-62","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member                                                     |                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `goToArea(index \\| hotspotId \\| null)`, `next()`, `prev()` | fly between areas (indexes wrap) |","table":"table-2"},"65":{"id":"/docs/architecture-63","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member              |              |\n| ------------------- | ------------ |\n| `play()`, `pause()` | auto-advance |","table":"table-2"},"66":{"id":"/docs/architecture-64","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member                                   |     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | --- |\n| `setBackground(mode)`, `openComment(id)` |     |","table":"table-2"},"67":{"id":"/docs/architecture-65","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member                        |                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `on(event, fn)` → unsubscribe | `ready {scene}`, `error {message}`, `areachange {index, id, name}`, `commentopen {id, title}` |","table":"table-2"},"68":{"id":"/docs/architecture-66","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"| Member      |                                               |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `destroy()` | stops rendering, frees WebGL, removes the DOM |","table":"table-2"},"69":{"id":"/docs/architecture-67","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bikepresenter-controller-api","content":"It imports no CSS: a page brings `styles.css`, `ui/present.css` and `present/present.css`.\nTheir custom properties are declared on `:root, :host` and every other rule is class-scoped, so\nthe same files work in a shadow root."},"70":{"id":"/docs/architecture-68","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"Two ways, both read-only, both on the published scene's URL rules (same origin as the embed or\nhttps). `embed-demo.html` (`/app/embed-demo.html`) shows both."},"71":{"id":"/docs/architecture-69","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"**iframe** `…/app/embed.html?scene=<url>[&area=…][&kiosk=1…][&origin=https://shop.example]`:\nthe customer view (`present/embed.ts` reuses `customer.ts`, without taking focus) plus a\n`postMessage` bridge, protocol `bike-embed/1` (`scene/embed.ts`):"},"72":{"id":"/docs/architecture-70","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"Parent → embed: `{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", cmd, … }` with `cmd` one of `next`, `prev`, `play`,\n`pause`, `getState`, `goToArea` (`area`: integer index, hotspot id or `null`), `setBackground`\n(`background`: a background mode), `openComment` (`id`). `parseEmbedCommand` validates every\nmessage; anything else is ignored (never evaluated)."},"73":{"id":"/docs/architecture-71","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"Embed → parent: `{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", event, detail }` for `ready` and `state`\n(`{ index, areas, playing, id, name }`), `areachange`, `commentopen` and `error` (the\npresenter's details)."},"74":{"id":"/docs/architecture-72","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"Only messages whose `source` is the framing window are read. With `?origin=` the embed accepts\ncommands only from that origin and posts events only to it; an origin that does not parse\nmatches nothing. Without it, any framing page may drive the bike and events are posted to `*`\n(they only carry the public scene's names and ids)."},"75":{"id":"/docs/architecture-73","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#embedding-on-a-shops-site","content":"**Custom element** `<script type=\"module\" src=\"…/app/bike-viewer.js\">` (a fixed-name build entry,\n`present/element.ts`) then `<bike-viewer src=\"…/scene.bike.json\" area=\"hs-fork\" kiosk>`. It\nrenders in an open shadow root with its own copy of the CSS (Vite `?inline`), so neither page\nleaks styles into the other; the host is `display: block; height: 480px` by default (style it\nfrom the page). `src` (required; changing it reloads), `area` and `kiosk` are observed attributes;\nthe presenter's events are re-dispatched as DOM `CustomEvent`s on the element; `element.presenter`\nis the controller above. Share is off (it would link the shop's page with our query string)."},"76":{"id":"/docs/architecture-74","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."},"77":{"id":"/docs/architecture-75","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."},"78":{"id":"/docs/architecture-76","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(per-sample `camera` intrinsics when present, else an assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."},"79":{"id":"/docs/architecture-77","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."},"80":{"id":"/docs/architecture-78","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"},"81":{"id":"/docs/architecture-79","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."},"82":{"id":"/docs/architecture-80","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."},"83":{"id":"/docs/architecture-81","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"},"84":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"page","content":"Bun migration plan","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration"},"85":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-0","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#what-stays-on-node","content":"What stays on Node"},"86":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-1","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Local changes"},"87":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-2","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"GitHub Actions"},"88":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-3","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#inventory-of-npmnode-assumptions","content":"Inventory of npm/Node assumptions"},"89":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-4","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"Rollout"},"90":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-5","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#risks-and-rollback","content":"Risks and rollback"},"91":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-6","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-migration#open-questions-for-owner","content":"Open questions for owner"},"92":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-7","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration","content":"Decision: adopt Bun 1.4.4 as the package manager; keep Node 22 as the runtime for now. Trial evidence is in BUN-TRIAL.md. Bun migrated both npm locks with matching tested package versions, `--frozen-lockfile` was stable, package builds passed, and warm installs were faster in this single local sample. Vitest under Bun runtime failed in three errors including `ReferenceError: ProgressEvent is not defined` in three.js. Browser E2E passed with Bun as script runner and Node/Playwright binaries; actual Playwright runtime support remains unverified."},"93":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-8","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#what-stays-on-node","content":"Keep Node 22 installed and on PATH for Playwright, npm scripts' explicit `node` calls, `node --test`, docs scripts and Next/MDX until each is intentionally moved and verified. The trial's successful `bun --bun run docs:build` is one result, not enough evidence to remove Node from all environments."},"94":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-9","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#what-stays-on-node","content":"Keep `bun run` as the script entry point, but note scripts with `node` commands and shebang binaries still dispatch Node. Use Node explicitly for runtime-sensitive tests until Bun runtime is independently green."},"95":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-10","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#what-stays-on-node","content":"`apps/web/playwright.config.ts:61-64` invokes `npx vite build`/`npx vite preview`. Replace with `bunx` or direct local binaries in its own verified edit; otherwise this keeps npm/npx on PATH. `tools/bench/bench.mjs:33-36` and `tools/optimize-glb.mjs:73` similarly use npx."},"96":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-11","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Pin Bun with `\"packageManager\": \"bun@1.4.4\"` in root `package.json` and `apps/docs/package.json`; keep `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=22.12\"}` while Node scripts remain."},"97":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-12","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Generate and commit text `bun.lock` at root and `apps/docs/bun.lock` from the current manifests. Remove `package-lock.json` and `apps/docs/package-lock.json` in the lockfile cutover PR; don't maintain two authoritative locks. Trial locks are generated from the current npm locks, with tested versions matching."},"98":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-13","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Run `bun install --frozen-lockfile` at root and `bun install --cwd apps/docs --frozen-lockfile` for docs. Use `bun pm untrusted` to audit scripts. Trial output showed no untrusted scripts; root npm had fsevents (optional) and docs had esbuild postinstall. Confirm Bun's trust behavior on CI and add `trustedDependencies` only for packages whose required install scripts demonstrably need it; validate esbuild and Next after any trust policy change."},"99":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-14","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Convert nested npm calls so `bun run` doesn't silently invoke npm: root `package.json:25-26` (`docs:dev`, `docs:build`); `apps/docs/package.json:8-11` (`dev`, `build`, `typecheck`); the Playwright `webServer` command in `apps/web/playwright.config.ts:61-64`; `tools/publish-pages.sh:78-83`; and optionally npx invocations in `tools/bench/bench.mjs:33-36`, `tools/optimize-glb.mjs:73`. Use `bun run --cwd apps/docs ...` / `bunx` or local executable paths and keep Node commands that are runtime-specific."},"100":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-15","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Change `orca.yaml:4` worktree bootstrap to `bun install --frozen-lockfile`; update onboarding and commands listed below."},"101":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-16","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Onboarding should state Bun 1.4.4 and Node 22 prerequisites, then:"},"102":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-17","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#local-changes","content":"Use `bun run` for scripts but do not set `--bun` globally. Use Node for Vitest runtime-sensitive commands until the `ProgressEvent` failure is fixed and covered."},"103":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-18","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"Use `oven-sh/setup-bun@v2` with `bun-version: 1.4.4` and explicit cache on `~/.bun/install/cache`:"},"104":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-19","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"For docs jobs use key `${{ runner.os }}-bun-docs-${{ hashFiles('apps/docs/bun.lock') }}` and `bun install --cwd apps/docs --frozen-lockfile`. Keep setup-node in the jobs while their scripts/tools use Node. `ci.yml` has a trial-only implementation of this shape; it keeps Node in all jobs for current scripts and changes root/docs package commands."},"105":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-20","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"| Workflow                   | Planned changes                                                                                                                                                                    | Node requirement                                                                      |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Replace npm setup/cache/install/run with setup-bun, cache path above, frozen Bun install, `bun run` and `bunx playwright install`. Docs job uses docs lock/cache and Bun commands. | Retain setup-node for Node-based Playwright, scripts, and coverage-summary `node -e`. |","table":"table-0"},"106":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-21","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"| Workflow                      | Planned changes                                                                                  | Node requirement                                                |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.github/workflows/pages.yml` | Set up Bun + cache both lockfiles; retain Node; frozen installs before `tools/publish-pages.sh`. | `publish-pages.sh` uses npm/node today; retain until converted. |","table":"table-0"},"107":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-22","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"| Workflow                           | Planned changes                                                    | Node requirement                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.github/workflows/pr-preview.yml` | Same setup/cache/install treatment as pages before publish script. | Same publish script reason; `actions/github-script` is an action and unaffected. |","table":"table-0"},"108":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-23","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#github-actions","content":"| Workflow                               | Pla