nventory-of-npmnode-assumptions","content":"| Location                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | References / planned action                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `README.md:10`; `AGENTS.md:27-44,113-139`; `docs/TESTING.md:7-10,20,50,59,69-102,124,154-173`; `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md:36-46,57,76-84`; `docs/GOALS.md:23`; `docs/PERFORMANCE.md:29-49`; `docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md:110,126,133`; `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:184`; `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md:8` | Onboarding/test/reconstruction commands and agent workflow use npm/node; update npm commands and install guidance, preserve Node runtime commands where they remain supported. |","table":"table-1"},"126":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-41","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#inventory-of-npmnode-assumptions","content":"| Location                                                                                                                                             | References / planned action                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.agents/skills/{architect,docs-engineer,junior-engineer,quality-engineer,viewer-engineer,web-engineer}/SKILL.md`; `.claude/agents/claude-runner.md` | Agent command guidance references npm; align with Bun install/run workflow. `.codex/agents/**` has no npm/node references found in this scan. |","table":"table-1"},"127":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-42","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#inventory-of-npmnode-assumptions","content":"No `.nvmrc` or `.node-version` was found. `apps/ios/README.md` has no JS package setup. `apps/web/vite.config.ts` and `apps/docs/next.config.mjs` don't otherwise configure a package manager. Docs build uses Next and should retain Node toolchain pending wider verification."},"128":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-43","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"Two PRs, each green on its own. The lockfile and the workflows switch **together**: committing `bun.lock`\nwhile CI still runs `npm ci` would leave the Bun lock untested and drifting, and two authoritative lockfiles\nis exactly what this plan avoids."},"129":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-44","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"**Cutover PR (atomic, one revert undoes it):**"},"130":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-45","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"commit `bun.lock` and `apps/docs/bun.lock`, regenerated from the current manifests;"},"131":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-46","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"delete both `package-lock.json` files;"},"132":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-47","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"add `packageManager: \"bun@1.4.4\"`;"},"133":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-48","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"convert the nested npm/npx calls (the `docs:*` scripts, `apps/docs` scripts, the Playwright `webServer`, and\n`tools/publish-pages.sh`);"},"134":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-49","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"update `orca.yaml`;"},"135":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-50","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"migrate `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` as in the table above."},"136":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-51","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"Verify:"},"137":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-52","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"a full CI run (web, docs, both E2E shards, merged coverage);"},"138":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-53","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"a PR preview build from this PR;"},"139":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-54","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"`bun install --frozen-lockfile` on a clean clone on macOS."},"140":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-55","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"Optional tool scripts (`tools/bench`, `tools/optimize-glb.mjs`) can keep `npx` for now; it still works when\nNode is installed."},"141":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-56","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"**Docs and agent cleanup PR:** README, AGENTS.md, docs/*.md and the agent skills switch to `bun install` /\n`bun run`, keeping `node` where a command really needs the Node runtime. A final grep for `npm ` and `npx `\nfinds only intentional leftovers, each with a reason."},"142":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-57","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#rollout","content":"Bun as the *runtime* (`--bun`) is a separate, later decision. It is blocked by the Vitest/three.js\n`ProgressEvent` failure and needs its own trial."},"143":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-58","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#risks-and-rollback","content":"Bun may install lifecycle dependencies differently across macOS/Linux or architectures; exercise frozen installs and actual esbuild/Next/Playwright jobs on Ubuntu before lock deletion."},"144":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-59","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#risks-and-rollback","content":"`bunx` may resolve packages differently from npx; Playwright installation and the configured local server must be checked in CI."},"145":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-60","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#risks-and-rollback","content":"A Bun runtime upgrade can expose Node compatibility gaps; keep runtime fixed at Node 22 and pin Bun 1.4.4."},"146":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-61","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#risks-and-rollback","content":"Roll back the package-manager switch by reverting the cutover PR: it restores both `package-lock.json` files, the npm workflow steps and the scripts in one commit. This only works because nothing else ships in that PR."},"147":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-62","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#open-questions-for-owner","content":"Should Bun be pinned at 1.4.4 in `packageManager` and setup-bun, or should CI use a newer version before cutover? Trial used the requested 1.4.4."},"148":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-63","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#open-questions-for-owner","content":"Should lifecycle trust be explicitly allow-listed in `trustedDependencies` after Linux CI proves whether esbuild scripts are required, or left empty when builds pass?"},"149":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-64","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#open-questions-for-owner","content":"Is there a policy preference for pinning GitHub Actions by SHA in addition to version tags?"},"150":{"id":"/docs/bun-migration-65","page_id":"/docs/bun-migration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-migration#open-questions-for-owner","content":"_Source: `docs/BUN-MIGRATION.md`_"},"151":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","type":"page","content":"Bun trial evidence","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-trial"},"152":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-0","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-trial#install-scripts-and-compatibility-failures","content":"Install scripts and compatibility failures"},"153":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-1","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/bun-trial#recommendation","content":"Recommendation"},"154":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-2","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"Trial date: 2026-11-12. Bun 1.4.4 on macOS; existing Node 24.18.0 runtime and warm npm/Bun download caches. Wall times are rounded to seconds from shell wall clock; npm baseline ran before Bun install on a clean `node_modules` for each project. Later Bun operations used Bun-created `node_modules`."},"155":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-3","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step               | npm result/time     | Bun result/time          | Notes                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | ------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Root clean install | `npm ci` exit 0, 4s | `bun install` exit 0, 1s | Bun said `migrated lockfile from package-lock.json`; installed listed versions exactly matching root npm resolution. `bun.lock` created as text. |","table":"table-0"},"156":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-4","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step               | npm result/time                         | Bun result/time                            | Notes                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs clean install | `npm --prefix apps/docs ci` exit 0, 10s | `(cd apps/docs && bun install)` exit 0, 2s | Bun migrated docs package-lock; exact direct versions matched. These are single warm-cache measurements, not a benchmark. |","table":"table-0"},"157":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-5","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step          | npm result/time                    | Bun result/time                | Notes                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Root versions | `npm ls --all --json`: exit 0, <1s | `bun pm ls --all`: exit 0, <1s | three 0.186.1; vite 8.3.5; vitest 5.0.5; @playwright/test 1.63.0; typescript 7.0.2 in both. `next` absent in root as expected. |","table":"table-0"},"158":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-6","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step          | npm result/time                                       | Bun result/time                                  | Notes                                                           |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs versions | `npm --prefix apps/docs ls --all --json`: exit 0, <1s | `(cd apps/docs && bun pm ls --all)`: exit 0, <1s | next 16.4.3 and typescript 7.0.2 in both; web-only keys absent. |","table":"table-0"},"159":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-7","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step            | npm result/time | Bun result/time                             | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Bun frozen lock | n/a             | `bun install --frozen-lockfile` exit 0, <1s | checked 95 root installs / 165 packages with no changes. Docs frozen install also exit 0, checked 285 / 394 with no changes. A second root install reported no changes. Lock hashes stayed stable. |","table":"table-0"},"160":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-8","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes           |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | --------------- | --------------- |\n| `bun run typecheck` | n/a             | exit 0, 1s      | `tsc --noEmit`. |","table":"table-0"},"161":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-9","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                    | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes                                                    |\n| ----------------------- | --------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bun run test:coverage` | n/a             | exit 0, 5s      | Vitest on Node; statement coverage 98.95%, lines 99.63%. |","table":"table-0"},"162":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-10","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step            | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes              |\n| --------------- | --------------- | --------------- | ------------------ |\n| `bun run build` | n/a             | exit 0, 1s      | TypeScript + Vite. |","table":"table-0"},"163":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-11","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                        | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| --------------------------- | --------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `E2E_PORT=4292 bun run e2e` | n/a             | exit 0, 310s    | 102 Playwright tests passed desktop + mobile. Playwright binary uses Node and Chromium; E2E's webServer invokes `npx vite build` and `npx vite preview`, which fell through to npm/npx from PATH and worked. |","table":"table-0"},"164":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-12","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step               | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes                                                                      |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bun run fixtures` | n/a             | exit 0, <1s     | Script invokes `node tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`; Node worked. |","table":"table-0"},"165":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-13","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                 | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes                                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bun run docs:build` | n/a             | exit 0, 11s     | Script invokes `npm --prefix apps/docs run build`; nested npm then invokes `npm run sync` and Next. Silent migration to npm for the package-manager operations. |","table":"table-0"},"166":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-14","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                                             | npm result/time | Bun result/time     | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `bun run e2e:coverage && bun run coverage:merge` | n/a             | compound exit 1, 1s | E2E coverage did not start: Playwright reported `Error: http://localhost:4190 is already used...`; merge then reported `No E2E coverage: run \\`npm run e2e:coverage\\` first`. Not a Bun compatibility result; full non-coverage E2E passed on isolated 4292. Coverage E2E not retried because the full suite took 5m10s. |","table":"table-0"},"167":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-15","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                 | npm result/time | Bun result/time | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `bun --bun run test` | n/a             | exit 1, 12s     | Vitest running in Bun runtime: 34/35 files and 362/364 tests passed, but 2 tests failed / 3 errors. Key failure: `ReferenceError: ProgressEvent is not defined` from `three/build/three.core.js:45169` in `test/compressed.test.ts`. |","table":"table-0"},"168":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-16","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step               | npm result/time | Bun result/time                                                                          | Notes                 |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| Bun sample fixture | n/a             | `bun tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs --sample /tmp/t.bikecapture.zip` exit 0, <1s | Wrote a 52 KB bundle. |","table":"table-0"},"169":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-17","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                 | npm result/time | Bun result/time                                    | Notes                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Bun reconstruct help | n/a             | `bun tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs --help` exit 0, <1s | Help printed correctly. |","table":"table-0"},"170":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-18","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                  | npm result/time | Bun result/time                  | Notes                                              |\n| --------------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Bun-runtime web build | n/a             | `bun --bun run build` exit 0, 1s | TypeScript/Vite build succeeded under Bun runtime. |","table":"table-0"},"171":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-19","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step                   | npm result/time | Bun result/time                          | Notes                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Bun-runtime Playwright | n/a             | `bun --bun run e2e -- --list` exit 0, 1s | One bounded runtime attempt: Playwright listed 102 tests; did not launch browser or webServer. Full browser E2E was run with Node binaries. |","table":"table-0"},"172":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-20","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial","content":"| Step             | npm result/time | Bun result/time                       | Notes                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Bun-runtime Next | n/a             | `bun --bun run docs:build` exit 0, 4s | One runtime attempt built docs successfully. Nested npm script still starts `npm run sync`; Next build completed. |","table":"table-0"},"173":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-21","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#install-scripts-and-compatibility-failures","content":"npm emitted its local `allow-scripts` policy warnings: root `fsevents@2.3.3` (optional platform package) and docs `esbuild@0.28.2` (`node install.js`). Bun emitted no untrusted-script warning; `bun pm untrusted` reported zero. Bun-created dependencies passed Vite, Next, and docs builds, including esbuild-dependent operations. No `sharp` package exists in either lockfile; the `sharp` mentions in `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` describe an optional install. `package-lock.json` marks only fsevents and docs esbuild with `hasInstallScript`."},"174":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-22","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#install-scripts-and-compatibility-failures","content":"The only runtime failure observed was Vitest + three.js under `bun --bun`: missing global `ProgressEvent`. Keep Vitest and browser/tool execution on Node pending a dedicated runtime fix and full verification."},"175":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-23","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#install-scripts-and-compatibility-failures","content":"`bun run docs:build` succeeds but the root and docs scripts explicitly invoke `npm`; successful output shows `npm --prefix apps/docs run build` then `npm run sync`. This silently retains npm as a script runner for those nested commands. Playwright's configured server explicitly invokes `npx` in `apps/web/playwright.config.ts` and succeeds by resolving npx from PATH. The plan should replace those nested package-manager calls with Bun equivalents or clearly retain npm, not leave an accidental fallback."},"176":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-24","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#install-scripts-and-compatibility-failures","content":"First merged-coverage compound command failed due to unrelated port 4190 occupancy. The requested isolated full E2E on port 4292 passed."},"177":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-25","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#recommendation","content":"Adopt Bun 1.4.4 as package manager only in a staged migration, retaining Node 22 as runtime for CI and browser tooling. Measurements show exact tested versions, deterministic text locks, frozen install success, and about 4x/5x faster warm installs in this one local trial. The runtime trial is mixed: web/docs build and plain Node-compatible tools worked, while Vitest failed on `ProgressEvent`; Playwright runtime was only listed, not browser-executed. This is trial evidence, not a claim of cold-cache or CI performance."},"178":{"id":"/docs/bun-trial-26","page_id":"/docs/bun-trial","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/bun-trial#recommendation","content":"_Source: `docs/BUN-TRIAL.md`_"},"179":{"id":"/docs/changelog","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"page","content":"Changelog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog"},"180":{"id":"/docs/changelog-0","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"Unreleased"},"181":{"id":"/docs/changelog-1","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Added"},"182":{"id":"/docs/changelog-2","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"Fixed"},"183":{"id":"/docs/changelog-3","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."},"184":{"id":"/docs/changelog-4","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Product plan updated with the owner's decisions (`docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md`): new bikes only; the customer page is a showroom (3D, components, upgrades) whose one action is **Talk to a salesperson** by email or SMS, with no hold or checkout; US market first (English, USD, TCPA consent for texts); Leads are now Messages; condition notes, reservations and WhatsApp removed. (#35)"},"185":{"id":"/docs/changelog-5","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Bun migration plan (`docs/BUN-MIGRATION.md`, trial evidence in `docs/BUN-TRIAL.md`): Bun 1.4.4 as the package manager, with Node 22 kept as the runtime; one atomic cutover PR (lockfiles + scripts + `ci.yml`/`pages.yml`/`pr-preview.yml` + `orca.yaml`) followed by a docs and agent cleanup PR. Trial: same package versions, frozen lock stable, 102 E2E passed via `bun run`; Vitest under the Bun runtime fails (`ProgressEvent`). (#34)"},"186":{"id":"/docs/changelog-6","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Product views plan (`docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md`): the commercial screens for bike shops (Studio: Library, Bike workspace, Leads, Captures, Settings; the customer Bike page with Show customer and Window modes; Storefront; Embed; Request form; a later Platform console), with wireframes, navigation, what we will not build, data model, phases 0–3 (phase 1 split into a one-shop pilot slice) and owner decisions; written from two independent drafts (Claude and Codex) and hardened by a Codex red-team (privacy roles, structured condition claims, low-bandwidth budget, reservation expiry). (#30)"},"187":{"id":"/docs/changelog-7","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Spec sheet on short screens: the Present spec table shows 4 rows with an \"All specs (k)\" / \"Fewer specs\" toggle, in two columns on wide cards; on wide stages the 3D view ends above the card, as it already did on phones, so the bike is no longer covered. (#27)"},"188":{"id":"/docs/changelog-8","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Capture checklist saved: the iOS app keeps each checklist item (id, label, done, pass) in the bike's `record.json`, and exported bundles carry an optional `checklist: [{id, label, done}]` in `manifest.json` (left out when empty). The viewer does not read it yet. Only the iOS CI build checks the Swift code. (#28)"},"189":{"id":"/docs/changelog-9","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Real intrinsics in close-ups: photo ranking uses each sample's own `camera` from `poses.json` (horizontal FOV and aspect from fx, fy, width, height) instead of the 65° iPhone assumption; implausible values fall back to 65°. (#26)"},"190":{"id":"/docs/changelog-10","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"COLMAP binary models: `tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses` reads `cameras.bin`, `images.bin` and `points3D.bin` directly (no `model_converter` step); TXT is preferred when both exist, and a missing or unreadable `points3D` is a warning, not an error. Binary parsing is bounds-checked and tested against the TXT output. (#25)"},"191":{"id":"/docs/changelog-11","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Preview ops: `prune-previews.yml` runs daily and removes the `/pr/<n>/` preview of every closed PR, and squashes gh-pages history once it passes 200 commits (force-with-lease on the base it read); `pr-preview.yml` keeps one sticky comment with the Docs and Viewer links on each PR. (#24)"},"192":{"id":"/docs/changelog-12","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Agent setup: `CLAUDE.md` is now `AGENTS.md` (shared by Claude Code and Codex, `CLAUDE.md` imports it) with a table of which tool runs each role; one persona skill per role in `.agents/skills/` (web, viewer, iOS, quality, docs, security, junior, plus `architect` and `delegation`), platform-prefixed wrappers in `.claude/agents/claude-<role>.md` and `.codex/agents/codex-<role>.toml`, and `orca.yaml` with the worktree setup script. (#23)"},"193":{"id":"/docs/changelog-13","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Test infrastructure: one fixture generator, `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, with one bike geometry and one pose layout (orbit rings + close-ups) for the E2E variants, the rendered-photo bundle (`--photos`) and the Pages sample (`--sample`); `make-test-bundle.mjs` and `make-capture.mjs` are gone. E2E coverage: `npm run e2e:coverage` records V8 coverage in Chromium, `npm run coverage:merge` merges it with the unit report into `coverage-all/` (~97% lines) so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count, with a merged ratchet checked by a new CI `coverage` job. (#21)"},"194":{"id":"/docs/changelog-14","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Reconstruct: `tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses` converts a COLMAP TXT model (`cameras.txt`, `images.txt`, `points3D.txt`) into `bike-poses/1` (world→camera OpenCV → camera→model, −Z forward, +Y up; real intrinsics kept per sample as `camera`), and `cli.mjs package` turns a model (GLB / USDZ / PLY), JPEG frames and poses into a `bike-capture/1` zip with `source: photos|video` and `backend` in the manifest. Verified on synthetic COLMAP output from the fixture's ground-truth cameras and through the viewer's own bundle reader. (#19)"},"195":{"id":"/docs/changelog-15","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Embeddable viewer + share docs: `embed.html` (customer view in an iframe with a validated `bike-embed/1` postMessage bridge, optional `?origin=` lock), a `<bike-viewer src area kiosk>` custom element (`/app/bike-viewer.js`, shadow DOM with its own CSS; `styles.css` variables now on `:root, :host`), the `embed-demo.html` page with copy-paste snippets, `&area=` on customer links; ARCHITECTURE documents `bike-share/1`, the BikePresenter controller API and the embed protocol; `share.spec.ts` and the new `embed.spec.ts` also run on the mobile project. (#20)"},"196":{"id":"/docs/changelog-16","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Snapshot / video export: the **Snapshot** button opens a menu: PNG at 1×, 2× or 4× the stage (shrunk to the GPU limit and 16.7 MP for iOS Safari) on the stage's backdrop, transparent or chroma green, with or without pins; and a 360° turntable video (8 s, WebM, MP4 in browsers that only record that, hidden where `MediaRecorder` cannot record a canvas). The camera, drawing buffer and clear color are restored afterwards. (#22)"},"197":{"id":"/docs/changelog-17","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Undo/redo for the whole scene: one store-level history (`SceneStore.undo/redo`, 100 steps) covers comments, areas, bike details and Edit → Model (whose own stack is gone). ↶ Undo / ↷ Redo buttons at the top of the Edit panel, Ctrl/Cmd+Z, Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z and Ctrl+Y (not while typing in a field); rapid 1 cm nudges merge into one step; opening another scene starts a fresh history. (#18)"},"198":{"id":"/docs/changelog-18","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Spec sheet: Edit mode has a \"Spec sheet\" section (label/value rows, starting from Frame material, Groupset, Weight and Sizes; add, remove, Tab between fields) saved as optional `specs` in `bike-scene/1` (validated on import: malformed rows dropped, text trimmed and capped). Present mode and the customer link show the filled rows as a \"Key specs\" table on the first (whole bike) card; Export and share packages carry them. The published demo has a sheet. (#13)"},"199":{"id":"/docs/changelog-19","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Site follows the stack tip: `pages.yml` republishes whenever the newest ready PR at the top of the stack (or `develop` when none is open) is pushed, so the live site no longer waits for merges. Parallel agents work in `.claude/worktrees/` with their own E2E port; the suite no longer reuses a server it did not start. The session-credits counter is gone from the home page. (#17)"},"200":{"id":"/docs/changelog-20","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos: the capture screen has a checklist (3 orbits at hub height, saddle height and top-down, ticked as Object Capture completes each pass; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur and cockpit; shots per pass; reflective-paint tips, and why a turntable does not work with on-device Object Capture). Exported bundles add `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) listed as `manifest.photos`, and the web viewer uses them instead of decoding HEIC. (#14)"},"201":{"id":"/docs/changelog-21","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"WebKit E2E: the iPhone specs also run in Playwright WebKit (Safari's engine) via `npm run e2e:webkit` (local, on a Mac; CI is a roadmap item). (#16)"},"202":{"id":"/docs/changelog-22","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Auto-publish: every push to `develop` republishes the site (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`), and each open PR from this repo gets a preview at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer), removed when the PR closes (`pr-preview.yml`), listed under \"PR previews\" on the home and Progress pages from `/pr/index.json`. `tools/publish-pages.sh` gains `--pr`, `--title` and `--remove-pr`, only replaces its own part of gh-pages (the main site keeps `/pr/`), and retries on the latest gh-pages when another run pushed first. (#15)"},"203":{"id":"/docs/changelog-23","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Performance: the viewer renders on demand (an idle stage draws 0 frames, the loop pauses in hidden tabs), redraws the shadow map only when the scene changes, caps the pixel ratio per device (`?quality=low|high`), welds USDZ meshes into indexed geometry (2.9M → 0.49M vertices on a 1M-triangle capture), builds a BVH in a worker so picking and pin occlusion cost ~0.05 ms instead of ~200 ms, and updates 50+ pins with budgeted occlusion and transform-only writes. GLBs with Meshopt, Draco or KTX2 load with lazily fetched, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` makes phone-friendly GLBs; `tools/bench/bench.mjs` measures it all. See `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`. (#12)"},"204":{"id":"/docs/changelog-24","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Photos & video → 3D research (`docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`): reconstruction options for bikes, recommendation (Object Capture on macOS by default, COLMAP + OpenMVS as fallback, splats later), photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions; new ROADMAP Milestone 1.5. (#11)"},"205":{"id":"/docs/changelog-25","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Share with customers: read-only `?scene=…&view=present` link served by a standalone presenter (`present/BikePresenter.ts`, no editing code, container-scoped), Share button (share sheet / clipboard / visible link), `bike-share/1` package export + `tools/publish-scene.mjs`, published demo at `scenes/demo/`. Present mode: leader lines, progress dots, swipe, auto-play (`?kiosk=1`), phone bottom sheet; markdown-lite comment bodies (DOM-only renderer); drag / ↑↓ comment reordering. (#8)"},"206":{"id":"/docs/changelog-26","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Crop box: Edit → Model → Crop clips everything outside an axis-aligned box (model-root space, saved as optional `crop` in `bike-scene/1`) with renderer clipping planes; drag the face handles (mouse or touch) or type the corners; \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor slab and background clusters. Cropped-away geometry can't take comments, and comments outside the box are hidden. Area-mode captures get a suggested box and a hint. (#10)"},"207":{"id":"/docs/changelog-27","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Auto-orient captures: a scanned bike is stood upright facing +X (PCA + side-view ground line, bike-shaped sign heuristics) on first load, with a toast; Edit → Model has Auto-orient, rotate ±90° per axis, flip, turn 180°, scale, real length in cm, 1 cm nudges, on-ground, undo and reset. Comments stay attached. `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` generates tilted test bundles. (#9)"},"208":{"id":"/docs/changelog-28","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"},"209":{"id":"/docs/changelog-29","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"},"210":{"id":"/docs/changelog-30","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"},"211":{"id":"/docs/changelog-31","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"},"212":{"id":"/docs/changelog-32","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"USDZ robustness: Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC) loads with textures; fixes three.js r186 crate decoding of inline vectors/halves/negative ints, ~10× faster mesh build for large captures, lazy-loaded USD code, clear fallback to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Synthetic fixture generator `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`. (#3)"},"213":{"id":"/docs/changelog-33","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"},"214":{"id":"/docs/changelog-34","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"},"215":{"id":"/docs/changelog-35","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"Customer link and Present mode in Safari: the card-height update no longer triggers a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error. (#16)"},"216":{"id":"/docs/changelog-36","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"The active comment pin (and the draft pin) drifted away from its point by 25% of its screen position because CSS `scale` also scaled the position transform. (#9)"},"217":{"id":"/docs/changelog-37","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#fixed","content":"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"},"218":{"id":"/docs/goals","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"page","content":"Goals","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals"},"219":{"id":"/docs/goals-0","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"Product"},"220":{"id":"/docs/goals-1","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"Success criteria"},"221":{"id":"/docs/goals-2","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Quality bar for every PR"},"222":{"id":"/docs/goals-3","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Non-goals (for now)"},"223":{"id":"/docs/goals-4","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."},"224":{"id":"/docs/goals-5","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."},"225":{"id":"/docs/goals-6","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."},"226":{"id":"/docs/goals-7","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."},"227":{"id":"/docs/goals-8","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."},"228":{"id":"/docs/goals-9","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."},"229":{"id":"/docs/goals-10","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."},"230":{"id":"/docs/goals-11","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."},"231":{"id":"/docs/goals-12","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."},"232":{"id":"/docs/goals-13","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."},"233":{"id":"/docs/goals-14","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."},"234":{"id":"/docs/goals-15","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."},"235":{"id":"/docs/goals-16","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"},"236":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"237":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."},"238":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."},"239":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."},"240":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."},"241":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**Share** gives customers a read-only link (`?scene=…&view=present`). To put a bike on a shop's own\nsite, use an iframe or the custom element (live demo: `/app/embed-demo.html`):"},"242":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"The iframe takes commands over `postMessage` (`{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", cmd: \"next\" }`); the\nelement exposes `element.presenter` and DOM events. Details in\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md."},"243":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."},"244":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"_Source: `README.md`_"},"245":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","type":"page","content":"Manual steps","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/manual-steps"},"246":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-0","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"Photos & video → 3D"},"247":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-1","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."},"248":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-2","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Customer link on a real phone**: open the published demo link\n(`…/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present`) on an iPhone, check swiping, the\nbottom sheet, pin taps and the share sheet. Real customer captures should be published to a\nhost you control with `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip> --out <folder>`, not committed here."},"249":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-3","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Crop on a real area-mode capture**: capture a bike in area mode, open the bundle, turn on\nEdit → Model → Crop and check \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor and the room. Note scans where the\nbike touches a wall or stand (the box then includes it; drag the faces to fix)."},"250":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-4","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Auto-orient on a real capture** (needs the real-capture test below): open a real `.bikecapture.zip`\nand check the bike stands upright, front to the right (+X), drive side towards the default camera.\nIf not, note which button fixed it (Flip / Turn 180° / rotate) so the heuristics can be tuned."},"251":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-5","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Decide on the HEIC decoder license**: photo close-ups decode HEIC in Chrome/Firefox with\n`libheif-js` (LGPL-3.0), shipped as a separate, lazily loaded worker chunk. Fine for a private\ntool; before a public release, either confirm LGPL compliance (unmodified library in its own\nfile, notice in the about/credits) or remove it once the iOS app exports JPEGs (see ROADMAP)."},"252":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-6","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."},"253":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-7","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"254":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-8","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."},"255":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-9","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Capture guidance + JPEG export on a device** (#14, needs an iPhone with LiDAR): during a capture,\nopen the checklist: each completed orbit ticks the next orbit row and its shot count stays\nfixed after **Another pass**; the top bar counts shots for the current pass only. Export a\nbundle and check (a) export of ~150 photos finishes in reasonable time with the spinner, (b)\n`photos/IMG_*.jpg` are 2048 px on the long edge and **upright** for portrait and landscape\nshots (open a few on the Mac), (c) the zip grew by roughly 0.5 MB per photo, (d) close-ups in\ndesktop Chrome load without the `heic` worker. Note: the iOS app was compile-checked by CI only\n(no Xcode on the agent's Mac); the JPEG writer was verified with ImageIO on macOS."},"256":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-10","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."},"257":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-11","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Let Actions publish the site** (auto-publish on `develop` and PR previews): Settings →\nActions → General → Workflow permissions → **Read and write permissions**, so the\n`GITHUB_TOKEN` of `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` may push to `gh-pages`. If `gh-pages` has a\nbranch protection rule, allow GitHub Actions to push to it. Check after the first run: the\n\"Publish site\" / \"PR preview\" run is green and Settings → Pages shows a new deployment. PRs\nonly get a preview once their branch contains `pr-preview.yml` (it runs from the PR's own\ncode), so PRs below this one in the stack get theirs after they are rebased or merged."},"258":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-12","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"Owner decisions for turning any photo set or video into a model (details in RECONSTRUCTION.md):"},"259":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-13","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Mac for the default path**: is an Apple silicon Mac (macOS 14+) available to run Object Capture\n(`PhotogrammetrySession`) on photo folders? Without one, the fallback is COLMAP + OpenMVS on Linux."},"260":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-14","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**GPU box**: rent (per-hour cloud GPU) or own an NVIDIA machine for COLMAP dense and Gaussian splats? Budget?"},"261":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-15","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Cloud API**: use a paid service (KIRI Engine API, Luma, Polycam…)? Which one, monthly budget,\nand are its data terms acceptable for customer bikes? Needs an account and an API key stored as a secret, never in the repo."},"262":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-16","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Dulling spray**: acceptable on customer bikes, or only polarizer + diffuse light?"},"263":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-17","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"**Test capture**: shoot one bike with the photo protocol and one 4K video with the video protocol,\nso the pipeline can be measured on real input (keep the files out of the repo)."},"264":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-18","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps#photos--video--3d","content":"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"},"265":{"id":"/docs/performance","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"page","content":"Performance","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance"},"266":{"id":"/docs/performance-0","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"What the viewer does"},"267":{"id":"/docs/performance-1","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"Optimizing a capture"},"268":{"id":"/docs/performance-2","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"Measuring"},"269":{"id":"/docs/performance-3","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Results"},"270":{"id":"/docs/performance-4","page_id":"/docs/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Known gaps"},"271":{"id":"/docs/performance-5","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance","content":"Targets (from GOALS.md): first model visible in **< 3 s** on iPhone Safari over 4G for a\n20 MB model, **60 fps** orbiting with **50 pins**, and **low battery use when idle**."},"272":{"id":"/docs/performance-6","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area             | What                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Where                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Render on demand | The animation loop runs only while something changes (controls input and damping, a fly-to, a model / background / pin / size change). An idle stage draws **0 frames**; a hidden tab stops the loop. | `viewer/renderScheduler.ts`, `Viewer.requestRender()` |","table":"table-0"},"273":{"id":"/docs/performance-7","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area           | What                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where                                     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Cached shadows | The sun and the model stand still while the camera orbits, so the shadow map is redrawn only when the scene changes, not for camera frames (that pass re-draws every triangle of the model). | `Viewer` (`shadowMap.autoUpdate = false`) |","table":"table-0"},"274":{"id":"/docs/performance-8","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                        | What                                                                                                                                                                                             | Where    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| No preserved drawing buffer | The canvas keeps its last frame while idle anyway; `screenshot()` and the Snapshot / turntable exports render right before reading. Saves a full-screen copy per frame on tile-based phone GPUs. | `Viewer` |","table":"table-0"},"275":{"id":"/docs/performance-9","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                 | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where               |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Device-aware quality | Pixel ratio ≤ 2 (phones show no gain at 3×, which shades 2.25× the pixels), 1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles; MSAA only at 1× (2× already supersamples); 1024² hard shadows on phones, 2048² soft on desktop. `?quality=low` (1×, 512² shadows) and `?quality=high` (up to 3×, MSAA) override. | `viewer/quality.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"276":{"id":"/docs/performance-10","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area               | What                                                                                                                                                                                 | Where                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| Welded USDZ meshes | three expands face-varying primvars to three vertices per triangle; identical corners are merged back into an indexed mesh (O(n) open-addressing hash over typed arrays, bit-exact). | `viewer/weld.ts`, `usd/usdz.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"277":{"id":"/docs/performance-11","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area         | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Where                                          |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| BVH raycasts | After the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a three-mesh-bvh hierarchy, built in a worker for big meshes (copies, never transfers, so the geometry stays usable; indirect, so the GPU index buffer is untouched). Picking and pin occlusion use it. | `viewer/bvh.ts`, `bvhImpl.ts`, `bvh.worker.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"278":{"id":"/docs/performance-12","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Where            |\n| ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Pins | Projection into a scratch object against a cached viewport size (no layout reads), transform-only writes for pins that moved, an `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage, occlusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that continue on idle animation frames (without re-rendering) until every visible pin is current. Skipped until the BVH exists for big models. | `viewer/pins.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"279":{"id":"/docs/performance-13","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"| Area                       | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Where                                     |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Lazy, self-hosted decoders | A GLB's `extensionsUsed` decides which decoder is imported: Meshopt (~26 KB JS with inline WASM), Draco (glTF build, ~190 KB WASM, workers), KTX2/Basis (~530 KB WASM, workers). three's loaders resolve the files with `new URL(…, import.meta.url)`, so Vite ships them in `dist/assets/`; nothing comes from a CDN. Plain GLBs fetch none. | `viewer/loaders.ts`, `viewer/gltfInfo.ts` |","table":"table-0"},"280":{"id":"/docs/performance-14","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#what-the-viewer-does","content":"Rule for new code: anything that changes what the canvas shows outside the `Viewer` methods\n(a new scene object, a material tweak, clipping planes) must call `viewer.requestRender()`, or the\nchange appears only on the next camera move."},"281":{"id":"/docs/performance-15","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`tools/optimize-glb.mjs` turns a GLB (for a USDZ capture, first `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`) into a\nphone-friendly one with glTF Transform:"},"282":{"id":"/docs/performance-16","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"**Meshopt** (default) decodes fastest and has the smallest decoder; **Draco** compresses geometry\nharder but costs a ~190 KB WASM download and slower decoding."},"283":{"id":"/docs/performance-17","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`--simplify <ratio>` (meshoptimizer's simplifier, `--error` as a fraction of the mesh radius,\ndefault 0.001) is the decimation step for phones: Object Capture's `.full` detail is far more than a\n6\" screen shows."},"284":{"id":"/docs/performance-18","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#optimizing-a-capture","content":"`--textures webp|--max-texture` use sharp (installed with glTF Transform). `ktx2` (ETC1S) keeps\ntextures compressed in GPU memory (a 4096² texture: 64 MB as RGBA8, 8–16 MB transcoded to ETC2, ASTC or BC7), the\nbiggest memory win on phones, and needs `toktx` on PATH."},"285":{"id":"/docs/performance-19","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"The script serves `dist/` with `vite preview`, drives Chromium on SwiftShader (like the E2E suite)\nthrough the `?e2e` test hook and prints JSON: boot time, a synchronous **frame cost** (render + a\n1-pixel readback that waits for the GPU), renders while idle and while orbiting with the mouse\n(with and without 50 pins), pin-update time per frame, and for `--model`: time until the first frame\nwith the model, geometry size, JS heap, frame cost and the cost of one `pick()` / `isOccluded()`."},"286":{"id":"/docs/performance-20","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#measuring","content":"SwiftShader renders on the CPU, so absolute numbers are far from a phone GPU and swing with machine\nload: compare runs made back to back on the same machine, and read render counts and per-operation\ncosts rather than fps."},"287":{"id":"/docs/performance-21","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Chromium + SwiftShader, 1280×800 at 1×, on a shared 4-core container under heavy load (other jobs\nrunning): treat absolute times as noisy, compare before/after. `tools/bench/bench.mjs --model big.usdz`\n(synthetic 23 MB USDZ, 972k triangles, 2048² textures), base branch vs. this change:"},"288":{"id":"/docs/performance-22","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                           | Before          | After |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------- | ----- |\n| Demo, idle stage: renders in 3 s | 8 (every frame) | **0** |","table":"table-1"},"289":{"id":"/docs/performance-23","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before | After |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------ | ----- |\n| Demo with 50 pins, idle: renders in 3 s | 5      | **0** |","table":"table-1"},"290":{"id":"/docs/performance-24","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before            | After               |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------- |\n| Big capture: vertices / geometry memory | 2,916,000 / 89 MB | **490,148 / 26 MB** |","table":"table-1"},"291":{"id":"/docs/performance-25","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                          | Before | After          |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | -------------- |\n| Big capture: JS heap after load | 271 MB | **104–123 MB** |","table":"table-1"},"292":{"id":"/docs/performance-26","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                    | Before | After       |\n| ------------------------- | ------ | ----------- |\n| Big capture: one `pick()` | 179 ms | **0.07 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"293":{"id":"/docs/performance-27","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                          | Before | After       |\n| ------------------------------- | ------ | ----------- |\n| Big capture: one `isOccluded()` | 221 ms | **0.02 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"294":{"id":"/docs/performance-28","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                      | Before | After    |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------ | -------- |\n| Big capture: pin update per frame (50 pins) | 873 ms | **2 ms** |","table":"table-1"},"295":{"id":"/docs/performance-29","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                           | Before  | After                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Big capture: full frame cost (render + GPU sync) | 3776 ms | 2978–3038 ms (no shadow pass on camera frames) |","table":"table-1"},"296":{"id":"/docs/performance-30","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"| Metric                                  | Before  | After                                                        |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Big capture: first frame with the model | 3357 ms | 2466–4113 ms (noise; adds weld, BVH moved after first frame) |","table":"table-1"},"297":{"id":"/docs/performance-31","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#results","content":"Weld cost: ~0.2 s for 3M vertices in Node on an idle core (unrolled position/normal/uv path), BVH\nbuild ~1 s, now in a worker. Real-device numbers are still to be taken (see Known gaps)."},"298":{"id":"/docs/performance-32","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Not yet measured on a real iPhone (ROADMAP: \"Measure on a real iPhone\")."},"299":{"id":"/docs/performance-33","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"Parsing and welding a big USDZ still run on the main thread (~1 s together for 1M triangles on a\ndesktop CPU, more on a phone); ROADMAP \"Progressive capture loading\"."},"300":{"id":"/docs/performance-34","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"No runtime decimation: phones get the full capture unless it went through `optimize-glb --simplify`."},"301":{"id":"/docs/performance-35","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"The Basis transcoder path is not exercised in CI (the KTX2 fixture is uncompressed RGBA8, since Node\nhas no Basis encoder); its files are built and served like Draco's."},"302":{"id":"/docs/performance-36","page_id":"/docs/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/performance#known-gaps","content":"_Source: `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`_"},"303":{"id":"/docs/product-views","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"page","content":"Product views: bike-3d-brew for bike shops","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views"},"304":{"id":"/docs/product-views-0","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"1. The bet"},"305":{"id":"/docs/product-views-1","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"2. Challenging the three-screen brief"},"306":{"id":"/docs/product-views-2","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"3. People and their jobs"},"307":{"id":"/docs/product-views-3","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#4-the-screens","content":"4. The screens"},"308":{"id":"/docs/product-views-4","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"4.1 Studio: Library"},"309":{"id":"/docs/product-views-5","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"4.2 Studio: Bike workspace"},"310":{"id":"/docs/product-views-6","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"4.3 Bike page (the customer view)"},"311":{"id":"/docs/product-views-7","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"4.4 Show customer and Window mode (the shop floor)"},"312":{"id":"/docs/product-views-8","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"4.5 Storefront"},"313":{"id":"/docs/product-views-9","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"4.6 Embed"},"314":{"id":"/docs/product-views-10","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"4.7 Talk to a salesperson"},"315":{"id":"/docs/product-views-11","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"4.8 Studio: Messages"},"316":{"id":"/docs/product-views-12","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#49-studio-captures","content":"4.9 Studio: Captures"},"317":{"id":"/docs/product-views-13","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"4.10 Studio: Settings"},"318":{"id":"/docs/product-views-14","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#411-platform-console-us-later","content":"4.11 Platform console (us, later)"},"319":{"id":"/docs/product-views-15","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"4.12 iPhone app"},"320":{"id":"/docs/product-views-16","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#5-how-people-move-between-screens","content":"5. How people move between screens"},"321":{"id":"/docs/product-views-17","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"6. What we will not build, and why"},"322":{"id":"/docs/product-views-18","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"7. Data and backend"},"323":{"id":"/docs/product-views-19","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"8. Phases"},"324":{"id":"/docs/product-views-20","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"9. Owner decisions"},"325":{"id":"/docs/product-views-21","page_id":"/docs/product-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"10. Where the two drafts disagreed"},"326":{"id":"/docs/product-views-22","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views","content":"Planning document for the commercial product: who uses it, which screens it has, how they connect, what we\ndeliberately do not build, and in what order. Nothing here is built unless marked **exists**. Owner decisions\nare collected in section 9."},"327":{"id":"/docs/product-views-23","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views","content":"> **Owner decisions, 12 Nov 2026 (these override anything below that disagrees).**\n>\n> - **New bikes only.** No used or consignment bikes, so there are no condition notes, grades or defect lists.\n> - **A showroom, not a sales page.** The customer page informs buyers: see the bike in 3D, explore its\n>   components, and check the upgrades the shop offers. It has no checkout, hold, reservation or \"buy\" flow. Its\n>   one action is **Talk to a salesperson**.\n> - **US market first.** English, USD (`$4,299`), and contact by email or SMS (a text message), plus a call\n>   button. No WhatsApp.\n> - **Bun 1.4.4** as the package manager, with Node 22 as the runtime, an empty trusted-scripts list, and\n>   GitHub Actions on version tags (see BUN-MIGRATION.md)."},"328":{"id":"/docs/product-views-24","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views","content":"How it was written: Claude and Codex each drafted a proposal independently from the same inputs. The drafts\nwere merged and the disagreements settled (section 10). A Codex red-team\nthen attacked the merged plan as a shop owner, a customer on a cheap Android and the phase 1 engineer, and its\ntwelve findings are applied here."},"329":{"id":"/docs/product-views-25","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"A shop does not buy \"3D\". It buys **customers who arrive already understanding the bike**: which groupset,\nwhich wheels, what the upgrade path costs, and why this model and not the one below it. That makes floor time\nshorter and the conversation better. Every view is judged by one question: does it help a customer understand\na specific bike, or help a salesperson explain it?"},"330":{"id":"/docs/product-views-26","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"What follows from that:"},"331":{"id":"/docs/product-views-27","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"**New bikes, explained part by part.** A 2026 road bike has forty brand photos, but no page lets a customer\nlook at *this shop's build* up close, tap the rear derailleur and read what it is, or see that the wheels can be\nupgraded for $600. The 3D model with **component pins** and **upgrade pins** is the advantage. Because a model is\nsold many times, one capture serves every unit of that model, and later every dealer if a brand supplies it."},"332":{"id":"/docs/product-views-28","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"**Inform, then hand over to a person.** The page sells nothing by itself. Its one action, **Talk to a\nsalesperson**, sends a short message by email or SMS with the bike and the parts the customer asked about."},"333":{"id":"/docs/product-views-29","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"**The customer never \"uses an app\".** They tap a link (the shop's site, Instagram, a QR on the floor bike's\ntag, a text from staff). Specs and the contact button never wait for the model to load."},"334":{"id":"/docs/product-views-30","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"**Staff have one hand and 30 seconds.** Floor tools are big buttons, no setup, task words (\"Show customer\",\n\"Preview\"), never \"Edit mode\" or \"Present mode\"."},"335":{"id":"/docs/product-views-31","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#1-the-bet","content":"**3D is the differentiator, not a gate.** A model can be listed with photos and specs first and get its 3D\ncapture later."},"336":{"id":"/docs/product-views-32","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"The brief asked for an admin screen, a shop screen and a client screen. Each name hides two different things:"},"337":{"id":"/docs/product-views-33","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"| Brief | Problem                                                                                                                     | Plan                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Admin | Mixes the **shop owner** (bikes, staff, branding, messages) with **us**, the platform (tenants, storage, billing, support). | **Studio** for the shop. A thin **Platform console** for us, not before about ten active shops; until then, audited database operations and scripts. |","table":"table-0"},"338":{"id":"/docs/product-views-34","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"| Brief | Problem                                                                     | Plan                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Shop  | The back office and the shop floor are different jobs on different devices. | Back office lives in **Studio**. The floor gets **Show customer**: the bike page in an assisted, big-button variant on a shared tablet, and **Window mode** for a dedicated shop-window screen. These are modes of the bike page, not a separate app. |","table":"table-0"},"339":{"id":"/docs/product-views-35","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"| Brief  | Problem                             | Plan                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Client | A viewer is not what a buyer needs. | A **Bike page** (one bike: decide and act) and a **Storefront** (the shop's catalog). Both public, no customer login. The **Embed** on the shop's own site is the main way customers reach it. |","table":"table-0"},"340":{"id":"/docs/product-views-36","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"Plus two screens the brief did not name, which a shop will ask for in week one:"},"341":{"id":"/docs/product-views-37","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Messages** (in Studio): \"Talk to a salesperson\" messages from bike pages (sizing, upgrades, test rides). Without\nthem the customer page has no purpose."},"342":{"id":"/docs/product-views-38","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Captures** (in Studio): uploads from the iPhone app, and later photo/video reconstruction jobs, waiting to\nbecome bikes. This replaces today's \"AirDrop a zip to a laptop and drop it on the viewer\"."},"343":{"id":"/docs/product-views-39","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"The resulting screens:"},"344":{"id":"/docs/product-views-40","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Studio**: Library, Bike workspace, Messages, Captures, Settings."},"345":{"id":"/docs/product-views-41","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Bike page**, with the Show customer and Window modes."},"346":{"id":"/docs/product-views-42","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Storefront** and **Embed**."},"347":{"id":"/docs/product-views-43","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Talk to a salesperson** (contact sheet)."},"348":{"id":"/docs/product-views-44","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**Platform console**, later."},"349":{"id":"/docs/product-views-45","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#2-challenging-the-three-screen-brief","content":"**iPhone app**, which exists and gains \"Upload\"."},"350":{"id":"/docs/product-views-46","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person              | Device       | Jobs                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Owner / manager** | laptop, iPad | list bikes, set prices, choose what is public, brand the pages, see which bikes and links bring requests, invite staff, pay us |","table":"table-1"},"351":{"id":"/docs/product-views-47","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person                                        | Device              | Jobs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Staff who capture** (mechanic, salesperson) | iPhone, shared iPad | list a bike between repair jobs: photos and specs first, a 3D capture when there is time, then areas, component and upgrade pins and reused snippets; save a draft. Mechanics know the components; salespeople own the customer wording. How long each step really takes is measured with the pilot shop before any target is promised |","table":"table-1"},"352":{"id":"/docs/product-views-48","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person                       | Device               | Jobs                                                                                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Salesperson on the floor** | shared iPad, shop TV | show a bike, or two side by side, at the area the customer asks about; hand off a link; reset for the next customer |","table":"table-1"},"353":{"id":"/docs/product-views-49","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person               | Device               | Jobs                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Customer at home** | phone, often over 4G | understand the bike before visiting: components, upgrade options, sizes, close-ups; message a salesperson |","table":"table-1"},"354":{"id":"/docs/product-views-50","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person                | Device                  | Jobs                                              |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Customer in store** | their own phone, via QR | look again later, send it to a partner, come back |","table":"table-1"},"355":{"id":"/docs/product-views-51","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person        | Device | Jobs                                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Brand rep** | any    | look at a dealer's demo bike. The public bike page covers this; no rep portal until a brand pays for it |","table":"table-1"},"356":{"id":"/docs/product-views-52","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#3-people-and-their-jobs","content":"| Person            | Device | Jobs                                                                                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Us (platform)** | laptop | onboard shops, fix failed uploads, watch storage and limits, suspend abuse; never browse shop data by default |","table":"table-1"},"357":{"id":"/docs/product-views-53","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Who**: owner and staff."},"358":{"id":"/docs/product-views-54","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Entry**: `/studio`, the default after sign-in."},"359":{"id":"/docs/product-views-55","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Devices**: laptop and iPad landscape; usable on a phone."},"360":{"id":"/docs/product-views-56","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Exists**: no. Today there is one scene at a time in browser storage."},"361":{"id":"/docs/product-views-57","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**States**: Draft → Live → Archived, plus **Unavailable** (no Reserved or Sold: the page lists a *model*\nthe shop carries, not one physical unit)."},"362":{"id":"/docs/product-views-58","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Unavailable**: the model is out of stock or discontinued. The page stays up and says \"Ask us about\navailability\", so old links still inform."},"363":{"id":"/docs/product-views-59","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"Archived models leave the public site."},"364":{"id":"/docs/product-views-60","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"Each card shows the one number that matters in its state: views or messages when live, readiness when draft."},"365":{"id":"/docs/product-views-61","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#41-studio-library","content":"**Add bike** starts a bike from a capture in the inbox, a `.bikecapture.zip`, a GLB, or just photos and specs."},"366":{"id":"/docs/product-views-62","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Who**: staff and owner."},"367":{"id":"/docs/product-views-63","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Entry**: `/studio/bikes/:id`."},"368":{"id":"/docs/product-views-64","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Exists, partly**: today's Edit mode, with areas, comments, spec sheet, model panel, crop and undo, becomes\nthe tool area of this page. Missing today: shop identity, cloud save, stock fields, publish state and the\nreadiness check."},"369":{"id":"/docs/product-views-65","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Upgrades are structured**: each Upgrade pin names the stock part, the upgrade part, its price difference\n(\"+$600\") and an optional note (\"ask about fitting time\"). Upgrade prices show as add-ons to the model price,\nnever as a configurator total."},"370":{"id":"/docs/product-views-66","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Pin kinds**:"},"371":{"id":"/docs/product-views-67","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Component**: what a part is and why it matters (\"Shimano 105 Di2: wireless electronic shifting\")."},"372":{"id":"/docs/product-views-68","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Upgrade**: what the shop can swap or add, with the price difference."},"373":{"id":"/docs/product-views-69","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Customers can filter by kind on the bike page."},"374":{"id":"/docs/product-views-70","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Snippets**: a shop-wide library of reusable comments, keyed by component (\"Shimano 105 Di2\", \"tubeless ready\").\nWriting copy is the real cost of each listing, and snippets cut it to minutes."},"375":{"id":"/docs/product-views-71","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Readiness check**:"},"376":{"id":"/docs/product-views-72","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Encodes what a good listing needs."},"377":{"id":"/docs/product-views-73","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Uses the capture checklist the iPhone app already saves, so it can say \"no derailleur close-up\"."},"378":{"id":"/docs/product-views-74","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Warns, but never blocks: a single-person shop can always publish."},"379":{"id":"/docs/product-views-75","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Publishing is versioned**:"},"380":{"id":"/docs/product-views-76","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Publish creates a public snapshot."},"381":{"id":"/docs/product-views-77","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Later edits stay in the draft until the shop publishes again, so customers never see half-finished work."},"382":{"id":"/docs/product-views-78","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"Shops can roll back to the previous version."},"383":{"id":"/docs/product-views-79","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#42-studio-bike-workspace","content":"**Photos only on a phone**: on a phone this page shows the checklist and status. 3D editing waits for a\nbigger screen."},"384":{"id":"/docs/product-views-80","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Who**: customers at home and in store."},"385":{"id":"/docs/product-views-81","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Entry**: `/s/:shop/:bike`. QR codes, social links and embeds all lead here, and today's `?scene=` links\nkeep working."},"386":{"id":"/docs/product-views-82","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Device**: a phone, over 4G."},"387":{"id":"/docs/product-views-83","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Exists, partly**: the share link opens a read-only Present mode, with area deep links, the spec sheet,\nclose-up photos and kiosk mode. This is the most important screen."},"388":{"id":"/docs/product-views-84","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**The still image comes first**, within a byte budget:"},"389":{"id":"/docs/product-views-85","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"The page with its facts and poster stays under about 300 KB, with the poster image under about 150 KB."},"390":{"id":"/docs/product-views-86","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"Model bytes load only when the visitor taps \"View in 3D\" when the phone signals Save-Data, a slow connection\nor low memory; otherwise they load once the page is idle."},"391":{"id":"/docs/product-views-87","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"The 3D view shows download progress, a timeout with **Retry**, and a plain failure message that leaves the\nrest of the page working."},"392":{"id":"/docs/product-views-88","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"Pages are generated as static HTML with Open Graph tags, so link previews in texts and social apps look right."},"393":{"id":"/docs/product-views-89","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Components and upgrades are the content**: two lists that mirror the pins. Tapping a row flies the 3D view\nto that part and opens its card. The guided tour (today's Present mode) walks the areas in order."},"394":{"id":"/docs/product-views-90","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Price is optional**: the shop chooses whether to show \"from $4,299\" and upgrade price differences. It is\ninformation, not a cart: there is no total, no checkout and no hold."},"395":{"id":"/docs/product-views-91","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**One action: Talk to a salesperson.** It opens the contact sheet (4.7). On phones it is sticky at the bottom."},"396":{"id":"/docs/product-views-92","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#43-bike-page-the-customer-view","content":"**Fit line**: \"Sizes 49–61; ask us to find yours\" from the model's size table, never a guarantee."},"397":{"id":"/docs/product-views-93","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Who**: a salesperson with a customer, and the shop-window screen."},"398":{"id":"/docs/product-views-94","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Entry**:"},"399":{"id":"/docs/product-views-95","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"Studio → **Show customer**;"},"400":{"id":"/docs/product-views-96","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"`/s/:shop/:bike?mode=store` on the shared iPad;"},"401":{"id":"/docs/product-views-97","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"`/s/:shop/window` on a dedicated screen."},"402":{"id":"/docs/product-views-98","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Exists, partly**: Present mode, area stepping and kiosk auto-advance."},"403":{"id":"/docs/product-views-99","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Compare**:"},"404":{"id":"/docs/product-views-100","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"Shows two bikes with a synced camera and the same area on both, matched by area name."},"405":{"id":"/docs/product-views-101","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"This is the conversation salespeople have all day: \"why is this one $2,400 more?\""},"406":{"id":"/docs/product-views-102","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"It is phase 2, and we confirm with the pilot shop that they actually use it before polishing it."},"407":{"id":"/docs/product-views-103","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**QR hand-off**: the customer scans the code and gets the bike page on their phone. The shop's numbers show\n\"taken home from the floor\"."},"408":{"id":"/docs/product-views-104","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Done ↺**: resets the shared iPad for the next customer and clears anything they typed."},"409":{"id":"/docs/product-views-105","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"**Window mode**: a locked kiosk loop across every live bike, for a dedicated display only. Exiting needs a\nPIN. On the shared iPad, Show customer is not a kiosk."},"410":{"id":"/docs/product-views-106","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"It refreshes the bike list every few minutes and drops any bike that is no longer Live, so the window never\nshows a sold or held bike as available."},"411":{"id":"/docs/product-views-107","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"If the network or a model fails, it falls back to that bike's poster with its price, then to a shop slide\n(logo, hours, \"Ask inside\"). It recovers on its own when the network returns."},"412":{"id":"/docs/product-views-108","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#44-show-customer-and-window-mode-the-shop-floor","content":"It keeps the screen awake through the Wake Lock API, and the setup guide covers the display's own sleep settings."},"413":{"id":"/docs/product-views-109","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"**Who**: customers."},"414":{"id":"/docs/product-views-110","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"**Entry**: `/s/:shop`."},"415":{"id":"/docs/product-views-111","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"**Exists**: no. This is the roadmap's \"Catalog page\"."},"416":{"id":"/docs/product-views-112","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"It shows:"},"417":{"id":"/docs/product-views-113","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"a grid of live bikes with turntable thumbnails;"},"418":{"id":"/docs/product-views-114","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"filters for type, brand, size and price;"},"419":{"id":"/docs/product-views-115","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"a \"Recently sold\" row."},"420":{"id":"/docs/product-views-116","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#45-storefront","content":"It is deliberately thin. Most shops already have a website, so the **Embed is the main way customers arrive**,\nand the storefront serves shops without a site and Instagram bio links."},"421":{"id":"/docs/product-views-117","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"**Exists**: the `embed.html` iframe and `<bike-viewer>`."},"422":{"id":"/docs/product-views-118","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"**What it needs for commercial use**:"},"423":{"id":"/docs/product-views-119","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"\"Copy embed\" for each bike in Studio;"},"424":{"id":"/docs/product-views-120","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"a whole-catalog embed (the storefront grid in an iframe);"},"425":{"id":"/docs/product-views-121","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"copy-paste guides for Shopify, WooCommerce and Squarespace."},"426":{"id":"/docs/product-views-122","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#46-embed","content":"The embed is for discovering and looking at bikes. Its actions open the bike page or Talk to a salesperson, so\nevery lead ends up in one inbox."},"427":{"id":"/docs/product-views-123","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**Who**: customers."},"428":{"id":"/docs/product-views-124","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**Exists**: no."},"429":{"id":"/docs/product-views-125","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**Opens as**: a sheet over the bike page, with the bike filled in."},"430":{"id":"/docs/product-views-126","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**Short form**: a name and one contact method, and how the customer wants the reply (email or text).\nTopic chips are optional. If the customer tapped an upgrade before opening the sheet, it is named in the message."},"431":{"id":"/docs/product-views-127","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**SMS consent**: choosing \"Text message\" shows one line of consent copy and \"Reply STOP to opt out\" (TCPA and\ncarrier rules). Email needs no extra consent."},"432":{"id":"/docs/product-views-128","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**After sending**: a confirmation with what happens next and the shop's phone number. A double tap or a resend\nwithin a few minutes does not create a second message."},"433":{"id":"/docs/product-views-129","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**Abuse and delivery**: a honeypot field, per-IP and per-bike rate limits, retried notifications, and a red\n\"undelivered\" alert in Studio if a message cannot be delivered."},"434":{"id":"/docs/product-views-130","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#47-talk-to-a-salesperson","content":"**No browsing history on messages.** A message holds only what the customer typed and the bike."},"435":{"id":"/docs/product-views-131","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"**Who**: owner and salespeople."},"436":{"id":"/docs/product-views-132","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"**What it shows**: requests per bike, with type, contact, source (Instagram, QR, embed, direct), time and status."},"437":{"id":"/docs/product-views-133","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"Statuses: New, Contacted, Test ride booked, Won, Lost."},"438":{"id":"/docs/product-views-134","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"Notifications by email, and SMS for the shop if it wants, for each new message."},"439":{"id":"/docs/product-views-135","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"**Scope**: assign a lead to someone and export CSV. This is not a CRM."},"440":{"id":"/docs/product-views-136","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#48-studio-messages","content":"**Privacy tools**: delete a lead, export one person's data, and delete messages automatically after the shop's\nretention period (12 months by default)."},"441":{"id":"/docs/product-views-137","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#49-studio-captures","content":"Incoming uploads from the iPhone app (roadmap: Upload to viewer), and later photo/video reconstruction jobs\n(Milestone 1.5)."},"442":{"id":"/docs/product-views-138","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#49-studio-captures","content":"**Statuses**: uploading, processing, ready, and failed with what to do next."},"443":{"id":"/docs/product-views-139","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#49-studio-captures","content":"**Create bike**: opens the workspace with auto-orient and crop already applied, and the checklist carried over."},"444":{"id":"/docs/product-views-140","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Shop**: profile (name, address, hours, phone, SMS number) and branding (logo and accent color first; fonts later)."},"445":{"id":"/docs/product-views-141","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Domains**: a subdomain or path now, custom domains later."},"446":{"id":"/docs/product-views-142","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Staff and roles**:"},"447":{"id":"/docs/product-views-143","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Owner**: everything, including billing."},"448":{"id":"/docs/product-views-144","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Editor**: publish and answer messages."},"449":{"id":"/docs/product-views-145","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Contributor**: capture and save drafts only."},"450":{"id":"/docs/product-views-146","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"One person can belong to several shops."},"451":{"id":"/docs/product-views-147","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Content**: request actions, snippets and size tables."},"452":{"id":"/docs/product-views-148","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#410-studio-settings","content":"**Billing**: plan and payment."},"453":{"id":"/docs/product-views-149","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#411-platform-console-us-later","content":"**Shows**: shops, plan, live bikes, storage, upload failures, last activity and suspension."},"454":{"id":"/docs/product-views-150","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#411-platform-console-us-later","content":"**Support access**: per shop, time-limited and logged. It never shows bike content in the overview."},"455":{"id":"/docs/product-views-151","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#411-platform-console-us-later","content":"**When**: not before about ten active shops. Until then, the database dashboard and scripts are the console."},"456":{"id":"/docs/product-views-152","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"**Exists**: capture, checklist and bundle export."},"457":{"id":"/docs/product-views-153","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"**Commercial changes**:"},"458":{"id":"/docs/product-views-154","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"sign in with the shop account;"},"459":{"id":"/docs/product-views-155","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"**Upload** to Captures instead of AirDrop;"},"460":{"id":"/docs/product-views-156","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"a \"my drafts\" list."},"461":{"id":"/docs/product-views-157","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#412-iphone-app","content":"The in-app 3D viewer (roadmap M4) is worth less than Show customer on an iPad; it moves down."},"462":{"id":"/docs/product-views-158","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#5-how-people-move-between-screens","content":"Every link carries its source (QR, Instagram, embed), so Messages and the Library know which channel works."},"463":{"id":"/docs/product-views-159","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**Checkout, carts or deposits in phases 1–2.** They touch payment, tax, stock races and each shop's own policy,\nand bikes over $1k sell in person after a test ride. Requests plus a human reply come first. Deposits only come\nonce a shop asks and picks a system of record."},"464":{"id":"/docs/product-views-160","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**Customer accounts.** No login to look at, share or ask about a bike."},"465":{"id":"/docs/product-views-161","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**POS or inventory sync in phases 1–2.** We only own the listing state and keep an optional external ID. The page\nnever claims live availability we do not sync."},"466":{"id":"/docs/product-views-162","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**Real-time collaborative editing** (the roadmap's \"Collaborative comments\"). One to three people edit per shop,\nso last-write-wins, undo history and \"edited by\" are enough."},"467":{"id":"/docs/product-views-163","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**A separate tablet app.** Show customer is a web mode that can be installed as a PWA."},"468":{"id":"/docs/product-views-164","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**AR \"bike in your room\", AI-written descriptions, rep portals, session replay.** They are demos, extra\nmaintenance or privacy cost, and none of them answer what the bike is made of or how it fits."},"469":{"id":"/docs/product-views-165","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#6-what-we-will-not-build-and-why","content":"**A bespoke platform admin as an early milestone.**"},"470":{"id":"/docs/product-views-166","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Every row has a shop**: tenant key `shopId` on everything. Access is never granted by an unguessable URL alone."},"471":{"id":"/docs/product-views-167","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Tables**:"},"472":{"id":"/docs/product-views-168","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Shop`: slug, profile, branding, request actions, plan."},"473":{"id":"/docs/product-views-169","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Member`: user, shop, role."},"474":{"id":"/docs/product-views-170","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Bike`: shop, slug, state, price (optional), currency, sizes, type, brand, model year, external ID, published version, draft version."},"475":{"id":"/docs/product-views-171","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`BikeVersion`: a frozen `bike-scene/1` scene, poster, model and photo object IDs, published by, published at."},"476":{"id":"/docs/product-views-172","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Capture`: shop, bundle object, status, error."},"477":{"id":"/docs/product-views-173","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Lead`: shop, bike, type, contact, time window, status, assignee, source, consent notice version, delete-after date."},"478":{"id":"/docs/product-views-174","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Snippet`: shop, component key, markdown."},"479":{"id":"/docs/product-views-175","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"`Event`: shop, bike, kind, source, day-scoped session hash."},"480":{"id":"/docs/product-views-176","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Stock stays out of the scene**: price and availability change often, so they live in `Bike`.\n`bike-scene/1` grows only by optional, presentation-only fields:"},"481":{"id":"/docs/product-views-177","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"pin `kind` (component, upgrade), and for upgrades the part names and price difference;"},"482":{"id":"/docs/product-views-178","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"a `poster`;"},"483":{"id":"/docs/product-views-179","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"a branding reference."},"484":{"id":"/docs/product-views-180","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Following AGENTS.md, that contract change ships first and alone. `bike-share/1` stays a portable package; it is\nnot a permission model."},"485":{"id":"/docs/product-views-181","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Files**:"},"486":{"id":"/docs/product-views-182","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Models and photos are 5–30 MB objects with stable IDs, uploaded through signed URLs."},"487":{"id":"/docs/product-views-183","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Drafts are private. Published versions are public and cacheable."},"488":{"id":"/docs/product-views-184","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Analytics**:"},"489":{"id":"/docs/product-views-185","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Events: page view, model ready or failed, area opened, component or upgrade opened, contact button tapped, message\nsent, QR or campaign source."},"490":{"id":"/docs/product-views-186","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Only aggregate counters per bike, per day and per source. Phase 1 has no session hash and no device storage.\nIP addresses are not stored with events, and server logs are kept for 30 days for operations only."},"491":{"id":"/docs/product-views-187","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Without identifiers or device storage, no consent banner is expected. Before launch, check that against the\nePrivacy rules of the pilot market, and add a hash only if the aggregate counts prove insufficient. A hash\nwould count as pseudonymous personal data."},"492":{"id":"/docs/product-views-188","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Privacy roles (US first; GDPR-ready)**: the US launch needs a privacy notice at collection (CCPA/CPRA style),\nTCPA consent for texts, and deletion on request. The roles below also make an EU launch possible later:"},"493":{"id":"/docs/product-views-189","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"The **shop is the controller** of its messages, and **we are the processor**, under a data processing agreement\nin the terms of service."},"494":{"id":"/docs/product-views-190","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"The lawful basis for a request is steps taken at the customer's request before a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))."},"495":{"id":"/docs/product-views-191","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"The form shows a collection notice (Art. 13): who, why, how long, and how to delete. The shop configures it;\nwe provide the default."},"496":{"id":"/docs/product-views-192","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"Retention defaults to 12 months. Messages can be deleted or exported, staff only see their own shop's messages, and\na breach procedure is documented before the first real lead."},"497":{"id":"/docs/product-views-193","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#7-data-and-backend","content":"**Consumer claims**: component names and upgrade prices are the shop's own statements; the page dates them\n(\"specs checked <date>\") and says upgrade prices are confirmed in store."},"498":{"id":"/docs/product-views-194","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"**Phase 0: clickable prototype (no backend).**"},"499":{"id":"/docs/product-views-195","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"A `/app/proto/` page on the PR preview with tabs: Studio · Bike workspace · Bike page · Show customer · Storefront ·\nTalk to a salesperson."},"500":{"id":"/docs/product-views-196","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"It uses the demo bike and made-up data, so the owner can try each screen on a laptop, an iPad and a phone."},"501":{"id":"/docs/product-views-197","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"It also runs the hosting cost spike."},"502":{"id":"/docs/product-views-198","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"*Done when*: the owner has clicked through every screen and settled the decisions in section 9."},"503":{"id":"/docs/product-views-199","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"**Phase 1a: the pilot slice (one shop, operated by us).**"},"504":{"id":"/docs/product-views-200","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"One shop's hosted listings. There is no signup; we create the shop and its staff logins."},"505":{"id":"/docs/product-views-201","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Private drafts and published snapshots."},"506":{"id":"/docs/product-views-202","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Today's editor, saving to the hosted draft instead of browser storage, with photos-only listings allowed."},"507":{"id":"/docs/product-views-203","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"The bike page within its byte budget, with component and upgrade lists and Talk to a salesperson → email or SMS."},"508":{"id":"/docs/product-views-204","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Each bike page is generated as static HTML when it is published, with Open Graph tags, so texts and\nInstagram previews work without a page server."},"509":{"id":"/docs/product-views-205","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"The privacy notice, retention and deletion from section 7."},"510":{"id":"/docs/product-views-206","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Measure how long listing one bike takes, step by step, with the shop's staff."},"511":{"id":"/docs/product-views-207","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"*Done when*: the pilot shop lists bikes it chose (photos first, 3D where it helps), shares them, and a customer\nrequest reaches the shop and gets answered. The listing-time target is set from what was measured."},"512":{"id":"/docs/product-views-208","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"**Phase 1b: what 1a proved is needed.**"},"513":{"id":"/docs/product-views-209","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"The Library with states, logo and accent color, pin kinds, QR codes, and the embed pointed\nat the new URLs."},"514":{"id":"/docs/product-views-210","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Shop accounts and roles, the step that turns this into a product for more than one shop."},"515":{"id":"/docs/product-views-211","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Phase 1b only starts once a real request has come in through phase 1a."},"516":{"id":"/docs/product-views-212","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"**Phase 2: the shop floor and the shop's own site.**"},"517":{"id":"/docs/product-views-213","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Show customer (Done ↺, QR hand-off), Compare (once the pilot confirms they use it) and Window mode."},"518":{"id":"/docs/product-views-214","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"The Storefront, per-bike and catalog embeds, and snippets."},"519":{"id":"/docs/product-views-215","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"iPhone Upload → Captures, the readiness check fed by the capture checklist."},"520":{"id":"/docs/product-views-216","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Roles, lead assignment and source reports."},"521":{"id":"/docs/product-views-217","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"*Done when*: a three-person shop keeps dozens of listings current, splits capturing from selling, and knows which\nlinks bring requests."},"522":{"id":"/docs/product-views-218","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"**Phase 3: many shops, and the systems they already use.**"},"523":{"id":"/docs/product-views-219","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Self-serve signup, billing, the Platform console and custom domains."},"524":{"id":"/docs/product-views-220","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Calendar-backed test rides, and optional deposits where a shop asks for them."},"525":{"id":"/docs/product-views-221","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Inventory or POS import where demand is proven."},"526":{"id":"/docs/product-views-222","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"Brand scans of new-bike models shared across their dealers."},"527":{"id":"/docs/product-views-223","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#8-phases","content":"*Done when*: a shop we have never met signs itself up and publishes a bike."},"528":{"id":"/docs/product-views-224","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"Decided on 12 Nov 2026:"},"529":{"id":"/docs/product-views-225","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"| Question                     | Decision                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Which shops and bikes first? | **New bikes only**: shops showing their current-season models. No used bikes, so no condition notes. |","table":"table-2"},"530":{"id":"/docs/product-views-226","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"| Question                       | Decision                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| What is the customer page for? | **Informing, not selling**: 3D, components, upgrades. Its one action is **Talk to a salesperson**. No hold, reservation or checkout. |","table":"table-2"},"531":{"id":"/docs/product-views-227","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"| Question      | Decision                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Launch market | **US**: English, USD, email or SMS replies, plus a call button. Privacy section adapted: CCPA/CPRA-style notice, and TCPA consent for texts. |","table":"table-2"},"532":{"id":"/docs/product-views-228","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"| Question | Decision                                                                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Bun      | 1.4.4 pinned, empty trusted-scripts list, GitHub Actions on version tags. |","table":"table-2"},"533":{"id":"/docs/product-views-229","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"Still open; none of these block the prototype:"},"534":{"id":"/docs/product-views-230","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"**Hosting**: decided by the phase 0 cost spike (Cloudflare R2/Workers/D1 vs Supabase)."},"535":{"id":"/docs/product-views-231","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"**Product name and domain.**"},"536":{"id":"/docs/product-views-232","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"**Pilot shop**: one US shop with a few current-season models."},"537":{"id":"/docs/product-views-233","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"**Pricing**: per shop per month with a cap on live models (recommended) vs per model."},"538":{"id":"/docs/product-views-234","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#9-owner-decisions","content":"**Who captures**: shop staff by default, or brands supply one scan per model for every dealer. New bikes make\nbrand scans more valuable than before."},"539":{"id":"/docs/product-views-235","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic                   | Claude draft        | Codex draft                                | Settled                                                                                                                               |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Is 3D required to list? | yes, 3D is the hero | no, photos and specs are enough to publish | Listing with photos is allowed and comes first in the pilot; 3D stays the differentiator, and its real cost in staff time is measured |","table":"table-3"},"540":{"id":"/docs/product-views-236","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic                | Claude draft                      | Codex draft       | Settled                                                          |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Compare on the floor | phase 2, the floor's main feature | phase 3, unproven | Phase 2, polished only after the pilot shop confirms they use it |","table":"table-3"},"541":{"id":"/docs/product-views-237","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic      | Claude draft  | Codex draft                           | Settled           |\n| ---------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| Publishing | edits go live | versioned snapshots, drafts invisible | Versioned (Codex) |","table":"table-3"},"542":{"id":"/docs/product-views-238","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic        | Claude draft                           | Codex draft       | Settled                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Stock fields | in `Bike`, with pin kinds in the scene | outside the scene | Stock in `Bike`; the scene only gains presentation fields |","table":"table-3"},"543":{"id":"/docs/product-views-239","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic                      | Claude draft | Codex draft                 | Settled                                                                                                     |\n| -------------------------- | ------------ | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Messages show viewed areas | yes          | avoid person-level tracking | No (reversed after the red-team: a checkbox does not make it safe or clear). Per-bike aggregate counts only |","table":"table-3"},"544":{"id":"/docs/product-views-240","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic   | Claude draft           | Codex draft              | Settled                    |\n| ------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| Hosting | Cloudflare, for egress | decide after a prototype | Phase 0 cost spike decides |","table":"table-3"},"545":{"id":"/docs/product-views-241","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic                | Claude draft   | Codex draft                      | Settled                                                     |\n| -------------------- | -------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Shared iPad vs kiosk | one Floor mode | kiosk only on dedicated displays | Show customer (shared, resettable) and Window mode (locked) |","table":"table-3"},"546":{"id":"/docs/product-views-242","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"| Topic | Claude draft | Codex draft           | Settled                                            |\n| ----- | ------------ | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Roles | Owner, Staff | Owner, Editor, Viewer | Owner, Editor, Contributor (capturers save drafts) |","table":"table-3"},"547":{"id":"/docs/product-views-243","page_id":"/docs/product-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/product-views#10-where-the-two-drafts-disagreed","content":"_Source: `docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md`_"},"548":{"id":"/docs/progress","page_id":"/docs/progress","type":"page","content":"Progress","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/progress"},"549":{"id":"/docs/progress-0","page_id":"/docs/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/progress","content":"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."},"550":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"page","content":"Photos & video → 3D: reconstruction options for bikes","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction"},"551":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-0","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"Why bikes are hard"},"552":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-1","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Options"},"553":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-2","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"Recommendation"},"554":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-3","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Capture protocol (photos)"},"555":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-4","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"Capture protocol (video)"},"556":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-5","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"Pipeline (`tools/reconstruct/`)"},"557":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-6","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"Owner decisions"},"558":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-7","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"> \"We can have the best 3D experience, but if it doesn't come from a collection of photos and\n> videos of a bike, it's not useful.\" (owner)"},"559":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-8","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"Goal: **any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) → a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer\nopens**: a model (GLB preferred), `poses.json`, `images/` and `manifest.json`. Today the only\nproducer is the iOS Object Capture app."},"560":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-9","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction","content":"**Status of the facts below (2026-10-27).** This first pass comes from the author's own knowledge\nof these tools. It was **not** re-checked against vendor pages in this session because the budget\nwas cut short. Prices, limits and terms of cloud services change often: check each `verify:` item\nbefore anyone commits money or customer photos. What was checked in the sandbox: Ubuntu 24.04\nships `colmap 3.9.1` in `universe` (`apt-get install colmap` works, CPU build without CUDA). There\nis no Docker daemon and no GPU here, so OpenMVS and dense reconstruction were not run."},"561":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-10","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                                 | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                                                  | Mitigation                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Thin parts (spokes ~2 mm, cables, chain) | Few pixels wide, so few features. Dense MVS fills them in or drops them. Meshes come out with webbed wheels or no spokes. | Close passes at the wheels; accept \"disc\" wheels or model spokes procedurally later; splats handle them better than meshes. |","table":"table-0"},"562":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-11","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                       | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Glossy / metallic paint, chrome | Highlights move with the viewpoint, which breaks feature matching and creates holes and bumps. | Diffuse, overcast-like light (softboxes, cloudy day, shade); polarizer; dulling / 3D-scanning spray (AESUB Blue vanishes in about 4 h) on matte-safe parts only, never without the shop's OK. |","table":"table-0"},"563":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-12","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                  | Effect on photogrammetry      | Mitigation                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Black tyres, black carbon | Low texture, so few features. | More light; textured backdrop and floor so the camera poses still solve. |","table":"table-0"},"564":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-13","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                               | Mitigation                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Size ~1.7 × 1 m, open structure | Background visible through the frame; masking matters. | Plain backdrop or a turntable; object masking (Object Capture does it, COLMAP does not). |","table":"table-0"},"565":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-14","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#why-bikes-are-hard","content":"| Property        | Effect on photogrammetry                       | Mitigation                                                    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Symmetric sides | Matching can confuse the left and right sides. | Overlapping rings, top-down ring, markers/props on the floor. |","table":"table-0"},"566":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-15","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                         | Input                                                                                   | Runs on                                                                                                     | Thin parts                     | Gloss | Output                                                                                     | Cost            | Verdict     |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ----------- |\n| **Apple Object Capture** (`PhotogrammetrySession`, RealityKit) | Any folder of JPEG/HEIC/PNG (not only iPhone photos); depth and gravity help if present | macOS 12+ (detail levels `.reduced` … `.raw`; Apple silicon or a Mac with a capable GPU), iOS 17+ on device | Fair; better with close passes | Fair  | USDZ (textured), poses via `.poses` request (macOS 14 / iOS 17+), automatic object masking | Free with a Mac | **Default** |","table":"table-1"},"567":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-16","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                | Input                        | Runs on                                                                                                                                             | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output                                                      | Cost                          | Verdict                              |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **COLMAP** (SfM + MVS) + **OpenMVS** (densify, mesh, refine, texture) | Any images; video via frames | Linux/macOS/Windows; Docker; SfM fine on CPU; COLMAP dense *needs* CUDA, OpenMVS dense runs on CPU (slow: tens of minutes to hours for 150 × 12 MP) | Poor to fair | Poor  | PLY/OBJ + texture; camera poses (`cameras/images/points3D`) | Free (BSD / AGPL for OpenMVS) | **Fallback** (Linux, server, no Mac) |","table":"table-1"},"568":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-17","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                     | Input  | Runs on                                   | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output        | Cost        | Verdict                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Meshroom / AliceVision** | Images | Linux/Windows, CUDA needed for depth maps | Poor to fair | Poor  | OBJ + texture | Free (MPL2) | Worse than COLMAP + OpenMVS for automation; skip |","table":"table-1"},"569":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-18","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                           | Input                                    | Runs on                                                                                    | Thin parts                               | Gloss                           | Output                                | Cost                           | Verdict                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Gaussian splatting** (nerfstudio `splatfacto`, gsplat, Postshot; apps: Polycam, Luma, Scaniverse, KIRI Engine) | Video or images, plus SfM poses (COLMAP) | NVIDIA GPU for training (minutes); phone apps do it in the cloud or on device (Scaniverse) | **Good** (looks right, not a clean mesh) | **Good** (view-dependent color) | `.ply` / `.spz` splats; no clean mesh | Free (open source) / app plans | **Photoreal option**: needs splat viewer support (ROADMAP M6) |","table":"table-1"},"570":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-19","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                                                                     | Input               | Runs on                        | Thin parts | Gloss  | Output           | Cost                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Verdict                                                          |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------- | ------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Cloud photogrammetry APIs**: KIRI Engine API (photo scan + 3DGS), Luma API, Polycam, RealityCapture / RealityScan (Epic) | Upload photos/video | Vendor cloud / Windows desktop | Varies     | Varies | GLB/OBJ/USDZ/PLY | Per-scan credits or seat plans. verify: current price per model, upload limits (images, video length, resolution), commercial-use and data-retention terms, whether customer photos may train their models | Good for \"no Mac, no GPU\"; needs account + budget + terms review |","table":"table-1"},"571":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-20","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"| Option                                                                              | Input      | Runs on                   | Thin parts           | Gloss   | Output | Cost                | Verdict                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------ | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **AI image-to-3D**: TRELLIS (Microsoft, MIT), Hunyuan3D 2.x (Tencent), Tripo, Meshy | 1–4 photos | GPU (open models) or SaaS | **Invents** geometry | Invents | GLB    | Free / SaaS credits | Not for a sales model of *this* bike. OK for placeholders, catalog thumbnails or \"illustrative\" models clearly labeled as such |","table":"table-1"},"572":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-21","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Notes:"},"573":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-22","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Object Capture is the only option with **automatic object masking** built in, which matters for\nthe \"background-free\" goal. With COLMAP the bundle needs masking (rembg / U²-Net on the\nphotos before MVS, or cropping the mesh to the dominant cluster after)."},"574":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-23","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"`PhotogrammetrySession` takes a folder URL of images from any camera. EXIF focal length helps.\nDepth and gravity metadata (iPhone LiDAR HEIC) improve scale and orientation. Without them the\nscale is arbitrary and the model may come out tilted, so auto-orient (ROADMAP M2) becomes required."},"575":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-24","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"COLMAP poses are world→camera with OpenCV axes (+X right, +Y down, +Z forward). The viewer\nwants camera→model with camera looking down -Z, +Y up. So:\n`T_c2w = inverse([R|t]) = [Rᵀ | -Rᵀt]`, then flip the camera's Y and Z axes:\n`pose = T_c2w · diag(1, -1, -1, 1)`. COLMAP quaternions are `QW QX QY QZ` (Hamilton,\nworld→camera)."},"576":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-25","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#options","content":"Splats need a viewer path (Spark / `@sparkjsdev/spark`) and a crop box; pins and areas still work\nbecause they only need a surface to raycast against (a proxy mesh or splat-depth picking)."},"577":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-26","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Default: Object Capture on a Mac** (`tools/reconstruct/macos/` Swift CLI over an image folder,\nthen package to `bike-capture/1` with `poses.json` from the `.poses` request). It is free, gives the\nbest masked, textured mesh for this object class, and works with photos from any camera and\nwith frames pulled from a video. Detail `.full` for the web (then GLB + decimate), `.raw` only for archiving."},"578":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-27","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Fallback: COLMAP + OpenMVS in Docker** (Linux / CI / a rented GPU box) for when no Mac is\navailable: same `ingest` → `reconstruct` → `package` flow, plus mesh cropping to the bike.\nExpect worse wheels and paint."},"579":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-28","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Photoreal later: Gaussian splats** from the same video (COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio, or\nPolycam/Luma/Scaniverse export) once the viewer loads `.spz`/`.ply` splats."},"580":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-29","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**Cloud API** only after the owner picks a vendor, a budget and accepts its data terms."},"581":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-30","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#recommendation","content":"**AI image-to-3D**: never as \"the bike\". Only for placeholders, clearly labeled."},"582":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-31","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Setup**: bike on a stand or a turntable, wheels off the ground or the kickstand hidden; plain\nmatte backdrop that differs from the paint; textured floor or newspaper so the poses solve;\nsoft, even light (two softboxes at 45°, or overcast outdoors), no direct sun, no flash."},"583":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-32","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Camera**: any camera ≥ 12 MP; fixed zoom (no zooming between shots); f/8–f/11 for depth of\nfield; ISO as low as possible; shutter ≥ 1/125 s handheld (tripod: anything); lock focus and\nexposure per ring; RAW+JPEG or high-quality JPEG; no portrait mode or beauty filters."},"584":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-33","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Shots: 120–200** total, 70–80 % overlap between neighbors:"},"585":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-34","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 1, hub height (~0.35 m), distance ~1.5–2 m: 36–48 shots (every 7.5–10°)."},"586":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-35","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 2, saddle height (~0.9 m), looking slightly down: 36–48 shots."},"587":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-36","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Ring 3, high (~1.6 m), looking down at 45°: 24–36 shots."},"588":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-37","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"Close-ups (0.4–0.6 m), 4–6 shots each, overlapping each other: drivetrain (both sides of the\nrear derailleur, chainring), fork crown and dropouts, cockpit (bar, stem, shifters), saddle and\nseat clamp, each wheel hub and a sector of spokes from both sides."},"589":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-38","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Turntable vs walk-around**: turntable with a fixed camera is fastest and steadiest, but the\nbackground must stay out of frame or be masked (static background + rotating bike confuses SfM).\nWalk-around works anywhere and is better for the floor features. Object Capture handles both."},"590":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-39","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-photos","content":"**Reflective paint**: polarizer on the lens (and ideally on the lights), more diffuse light, or a\nremovable dulling spray if the shop agrees. Record which one you used in the manifest notes."},"591":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-40","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**4K (3840×2160) at 30 fps**, or 60 fps if the light allows a fast shutter; HEVC or H.264,\n**not** HDR / Dolby Vision (tone mapping varies between decoders); lock exposure and focus;\nstabilization on; no zooming."},"592":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-41","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**Shutter speed ≥ 1/250 s** (set it in a pro camera app such as Blackmagic Camera; the stock iOS app\npicks it automatically), otherwise motion blur kills features on spokes and cables."},"593":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-42","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"**Slow orbit**: about 60–90 s per ring (≈ 4–6°/s), three rings as above, then slow passes over\nthe close-up areas. 3–5 minutes of footage in total."},"594":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-43","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#capture-protocol-video","content":"The `ingest` step extracts frames, keeps the sharpest frame per short time window (variance of the\nLaplacian) and only adds a frame when the view has changed enough, aiming for 80–200 frames."},"595":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-44","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"**Built so far** (`node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs --help`):"},"596":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-45","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"`poses --colmap <sparse_model> [-o poses.json]` (`colmap.mjs`): reads COLMAP's TXT or binary model directly (TXT wins when both are present; no `model_converter` step needed) and writes\n`bike-poses/1`. Samples are ordered by image name, `file` is the image basename, and each sample\nkeeps the real intrinsics as `camera` (pixels; `SIMPLE_*`/`RADIAL*` models give fx = fy = f;\ndistortion is not kept). The model frame is COLMAP's world frame (arbitrary scale and up), which\nOpenMVS keeps for the mesh, so the viewer's auto-orient stands the bike up."},"597":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-46","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"`package --model <glb|usdz|ply> --images <frames> (--colmap <dir> | --poses <file>) --source photos|video --backend <b> [--name] [-o]`\n(`package.mjs`): flat zip with `manifest.json`, `model.<ext>`, `poses.json`, `images/*.jpg`\n(stored, not deflated). It refuses non-JPEG frames, duplicate names and poses whose image is missing."},"598":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-47","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"Tests (`apps/web/test/reconstruct.test.ts`): COLMAP text synthesized from the fixture's ground-truth\ncameras (via COLMAP's own `x = R·X + t` definition, with shuffled image ids and sign-flipped\nquaternions) must convert back to the same transforms, project points to the same pixels in the\nconverted three.js camera, and package into a zip that the viewer's `readCaptureBundle` opens with\nevery pose matched to its photo."},"599":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-48","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"Status and the next steps are in ROADMAP.md (Milestone 1.5). For the commands to try\nCOLMAP on Linux today (a CPU-only sparse model, enough to check the poses):"},"600":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-49","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#pipeline-toolsreconstruct","content":"For a dense textured mesh use OpenMVS (`InterfaceCOLMAP` → `DensifyPointCloud` → `ReconstructMesh`\n→ `RefineMesh` → `TextureMesh`) from its Docker image, or COLMAP's dense steps on a CUDA machine."},"601":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-50","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"See MANUAL-STEPS.md. In short: a Mac (Apple silicon) for the default path;\nwhether to pay for a cloud API (which vendor, monthly budget, OK with its data terms for\ncustomer bikes); a GPU box (rented or owned) for COLMAP dense / splats; whether dulling spray is\nacceptable on customer bikes."},"602":{"id":"/docs/reconstruction-51","page_id":"/docs/reconstruction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reconstruction#owner-decisions","content":"_Source: `docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`_"},"603":{"id":"/docs/roadmap","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"page","content":"Roadmap","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap"},"604":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-0","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"Milestone 0: Project ops"},"605":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-1","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"},"606":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-2","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"Milestone 1.5: Photos & video → 3D"},"607":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-3","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"},"608":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-4","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"Milestone 3: Sales experience"},"609":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-5","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"},"610":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-6","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"},"611":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-7","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"Milestone 6: Quality"},"612":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-8","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Ideas parking lot"},"613":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-9","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in AGENTS.md."},"614":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-10","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."},"615":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-11","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."},"616":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-12","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."},"617":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-13","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."},"618":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-14","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Prune stale previews**: a scheduled job that removes `/pr/<n>/` for PRs that are no longer open (a missed or failed close run leaves them behind), and squashes gh-pages history once it grows large (each preview adds a full site copy to the branch). Done: `prune-previews.yml` runs daily and removes the preview of every closed PR; when gh-pages passes 200 commits it squashes the history, pushing with `--force-with-lease` on the base it read."},"619":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-15","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Preview link on the PR**: comment (or update one sticky comment) on each PR with its preview URL, so the owner can open it from the GitHub app. Done: `pr-preview.yml` keeps one sticky comment (marker ``) with the Docs and Viewer links on each PR."},"620":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-16","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[ ] **Bun as package manager**: pinned Bun 1.4.4 installs (frozen `bun.lock`, root and `apps/docs`) locally, in `orca.yaml` and in GitHub Actions; Node 22 stays the runtime. Plan and trial: docs/BUN-MIGRATION.md."},"621":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-17","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / dark)"},"622":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-18","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"},"623":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-19","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"},"624":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-20","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"},"625":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-21","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"},"626":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-22","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"},"627":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-23","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"Top priority: any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) must become a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer opens. Research and recommendation: docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md."},"628":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-24","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **Reconstruction research**: options for bikes (Object Capture on macOS, COLMAP + OpenMVS, Meshroom, Gaussian splats, cloud APIs, AI image-to-3D), recommendation, photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md). Vendor prices/terms still to verify against current pages."},"629":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-25","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`ingest` CLI** (`tools/reconstruct/`, Node/TS + ffmpeg): photos and videos → sharp, deduplicated, EXIF-upright JPEG frames (variance-of-Laplacian sharpness + novelty selection, 80–200 frames), HEIC → JPEG, coverage report; unit-tested scoring."},"630":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-26","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **COLMAP → `bike-poses/1` conversion**: parse `cameras.txt`/`images.txt`/`points3D.txt`, world→camera OpenCV axes → camera→model −Z/+Y, with tests on synthetic COLMAP output generated from ground truth. Done: `tools/reconstruct/colmap.mjs` (`cli.mjs poses`), round-trip + reprojection tests in `apps/web/test/reconstruct.test.ts`; each sample also carries the COLMAP intrinsics as `camera`."},"631":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-27","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **COLMAP binary models**: read `cameras.bin`/`images.bin`/`points3D.bin` directly (skip `model_converter`); TXT wins when both exist; points are optional and a missing or bad `points3D` gives a warning, not a failure. Done: `tools/reconstruct/colmap.mjs` reads the binary records with bounds checks, `apps/web/test/reconstruct.test.ts` checks that binary and TXT give the same poses and rejects truncated records."},"632":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-28","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Real COLMAP run**: check the converter on a real `colmap automatic_reconstructor` run over rendered fixture photos (part of the synthetic end-to-end eval)."},"633":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-29","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **Real intrinsics in close-ups**: use `poses.json` `samples[].camera` (fx, fy, width, height) in `scene/photos.ts` ranking instead of the 65° iPhone assumption when present. Done: `sampleIntrinsics()` gives each sample its own horizontal FOV and aspect, bounds-checked (bad values fall back to 65°); the halo/frame test per photo uses that sample's diagonal. Tested in `apps/web/test/photos.test.ts`."},"634":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-30","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend colmap`**: COLMAP + OpenMVS via `tools/reconstruct/docker/` (and native), dense mesh + texture, crop the mesh to the dominant object, optional photo masking (rembg)."},"635":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-31","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend object-capture`**: Swift CLI `tools/reconstruct/macos/` (`PhotogrammetrySession` over an image folder → `model.usdz` + poses), built by a path-filtered macos-latest CI job."},"636":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-32","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[x] **`package`**: result → `bike-capture/1` zip (GLB model, `poses.json`, `images/*.jpg`, manifest with `source: photos|video` and `backend`). Done: `tools/reconstruct/package.mjs` (`cli.mjs package`), the zip is checked through the viewer's own `readCaptureBundle` in a unit test; the web manifest parser keeps `source`/`backend`."},"637":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-33","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **`package` polish**: convert OpenMVS OBJ/PLY to GLB (gltf-transform) and decimate for the web (`tools/optimize-glb.mjs`), crop the mesh to the dominant object, resize frames to ≤ 2048 px; show `source`/`backend` in the viewer's capture info."},"638":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-34","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Synthetic end-to-end eval**: render the fixture bike with texture + textured floor from 60–120 posed cameras and as an orbit video (`tools/fixtures/render-photos.mjs`), run ingest → reconstruct → package, measure pose error after similarity alignment, Chamfer distance / completeness vs ground truth and close-up ranking; report in `docs/RECONSTRUCTION-EVAL.md`."},"639":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-35","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Web upload flow**: drop a folder of photos or a video on the viewer, send it to a reconstruction backend, open the result."},"640":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-36","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Cloud backend**: one paid API behind `reconstruct --backend <vendor>` once the owner picks a vendor and budget."},"641":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-37","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-15-photos--video--3d","content":"[ ] **Splats from video**: COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio → `.spz`, opened through the M6 splat support."},"642":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-38","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."},"643":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-39","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."},"644":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-40","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."},"645":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-41","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."},"646":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-42","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **USDZ robustness**: three r186 reads binary USDC; `apps/web/src/viewer/usd/` fixes its inline-value decoding, speeds up large meshes ~10×, waits for packed textures and falls back to a `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` hint. Synthetic Object-Capture-like fixtures from `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"647":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-43","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Verify a real Object Capture USDZ**: load a real `model.usdz` (owner's iPhone, see docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md), compare against Quick Look; turn anything off into a fixture-based test (synthetic re-creation, never the capture itself)."},"648":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-44","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Weld USDZ meshes**: three expands face-varying meshes to 3 vertices per triangle (~3M vertices for a 1M-triangle capture); identical corners are merged into an indexed geometry (hash-based, typed arrays, O(n)): 2.9M → 0.49M vertices, 89 → 26 MB of geometry on the 1M-triangle fixture. Decimation stays offline (`tools/optimize-glb.mjs --simplify`). See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."},"649":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-45","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."},"650":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-46","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Auto-orient on real scans**: check the up/front heuristics (`scene/orient.ts`) against real Object Capture bikes (flat bars, kids' bikes, e-bikes with a battery, kickstands); tune the vote weights and add the cases as generated test fixtures."},"651":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-47","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."},"652":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-48","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Crop polish**: a rotatable (oriented) crop box for scans whose model-root axes are tilted; a floor-height handle that also re-grounds; show how many comments the crop hides."},"653":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-49","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."},"654":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-50","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **iOS JPEG photo export**: write `images/*.jpg` (or a `photos/` folder of 2048 px JPEGs) next to the HEICs in the bundle so Chrome/Firefox skip the 2 MB WASM HEIC decoder and decoding is instant; the web side already prefers whatever decodes natively. Done: `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) + `manifest.photos`; the web reader uses them when present."},"655":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-51","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Drop the WASM HEIC decoder**: once every exported bundle has `photos/`, remove `libheif-js` (LGPL) or keep it only for old bundles; also check the exported zip size growth (~0.5 MB per photo) on a real capture."},"656":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-52","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait captures, EXIF rotation); read real intrinsics if the iOS app can export them."},"657":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-53","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Portrait captures in close-ups**: test and handle rotated/portrait sample cameras in `scene/photos.ts` ranking (the horizontal FOV comes from `width` and `fx`; a portrait frame may need its axes swapped)."},"658":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-54","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Flag missing close-ups**: read the bundle manifest `checklist` in the viewer and warn about unticked close-ups (e.g. \"no derailleur photos\")."},"659":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-55","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."},"660":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-56","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."},"661":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-57","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."},"662":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-58","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."},"663":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-59","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Embeddable viewer** (was also listed as *Embed packaging*): an `embed.html` page + `postMessage` bridge and a `<bike-viewer>` custom element around `mountPresenter` (`present/BikePresenter.ts`), so shops can put a bike on their own site; scope the `styles.css` base rules first so it works inside Shadow DOM."},"664":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-60","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Share docs**: ARCHITECTURE (`bike-share/1`, BikePresenter controller API for the embed), TESTING-GUIDE (try the customer link on a phone), README; mobile E2E run of `share.spec.ts`."},"665":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-61","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Cross-origin embed check**: an E2E run that loads `bike-viewer.js` and `embed.html` from a second origin (two preview ports) to prove CORS module loading, the `?origin=` lock end to end, and the BVH build falling back to the main thread when the worker cannot start cross-origin (shop pages); add `interval`/`idle` attributes to `<bike-viewer>`."},"666":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-62","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."},"667":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-63","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."},"668":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-64","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Spec sheet on short screens**: with 6+ rows the first Present card covers the lower half of the bike on a laptop; collapse the table to a few rows with \"All specs\" (or a two-column layout on wide cards). Done: 4 rows plus an \"All specs (k)\" toggle, two columns on cards ≥ 500 px, and on wide stages the viewport ends above the card (as on phones) so the bike is never behind it."},"669":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-65","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] _(in progress)_ **Area views with depth + long specs** (owner review): Set view gives no feedback and the camera always orbits and zooms around the bike's center, so close-ups of a part cannot be framed; zoom toward the cursor, double-click to orbit around a point, confirm Set view; spec values longer than one line wrap in the editor and are clamped in Present."},"670":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-66","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Present backdrop under the card**: on wide stages the viewport now ends above the card, so the bike renders smaller and a dark band shows behind the card; extend the stage backdrop under the card or let the card sit beside the bike on landscape screens."},"671":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-67","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."},"672":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-68","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts. Done: **Snapshot** menu in the top bar (1× / 2× / 4× the stage, capped by the GPU and 16.7 MP; as shown / transparent / chroma green; pins on or off), 8 s turntable in WebM (MP4 where only that records, hidden where neither does)."},"673":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-69","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Square / vertical video formats**: the turntable records the stage's aspect; offer 1:1 and 9:16 framings (refit the camera to the bike) and a duration choice for Reels/Stories."},"674":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-70","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Turntable in WebKit E2E**: check the MP4 path (Safari's MediaRecorder) in `npm run e2e:webkit`; the Chromium suite only covers WebM."},"675":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-71","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[x] **Undo/redo for the whole scene**: Edit → Model has its own undo stack; extend it to comments and areas (store-level history, Ctrl/Cmd+Z)."},"676":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-72","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."},"677":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-73","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."},"678":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-74","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[x] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support. Done: checklist in the capture screen (orbits ticked by Object Capture's pass detection, close-ups ticked by hand, shots per pass). Turntable: not possible with `ObjectCaptureSession` (ARKit world tracking needs the object still); documented in the app and README."},"679":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-75","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Turntable capture via the Mac**: a fixed-camera photo mode (plain `AVCapturePhotoOutput` shots while the bike spins on a turntable) reconstructed by `PhotogrammetrySession` on the Mac (see Mac high-detail reconstruction), which accepts turntable sets."},"680":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-76","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[x] **Save the capture checklist**: store ticked close-ups and shots per pass in `record.json` / the manifest so the web side can flag missing close-ups (e.g. \"no derailleur photos\"). Done: the app keeps each checklist item (`id`, `label`, `done`, `pass`) in the bike's `record.json`; the exported manifest gets an optional `checklist: [{id, label, done}]` (left out when empty). Simulator build checked by iOS CI only."},"681":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-77","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."},"682":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-78","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."},"683":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-79","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."},"684":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-80","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"Commercial plan (screens for shops, the shop floor and customers; phases; owner decisions): docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md."},"685":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-81","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[x] **Product views plan**: Studio, Bike page, Show customer / Window mode, Storefront, Embed, Request form, Leads, Captures, Platform console; wireframes, data model, phases 0–3, owner decisions."},"686":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-82","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] _(in progress)_ **Clickable prototype (phase 0)**: `/app/proto/` with tabs Studio · Bike workspace · Bike page · Show customer · Storefront · Talk to a salesperson, for **new bikes** in the **US** (English, USD, email/SMS): components and upgrades on the demo bike with made-up data, no checkout or holds; checked on laptop, iPad and phone sizes."},"687":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-83","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Hosting cost spike**: tenant auth, signed upload, public reads and the cost of 1,000 views of a 20 MB model on Cloudflare (R2/Workers/D1) vs Supabase; result in docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md section 9."},"688":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-84","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."},"689":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-85","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."},"690":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-86","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."},"691":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-87","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."},"692":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-88","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins. Lazily loaded, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs`; BVH picking/occlusion in a worker; budgeted pin updates; device-aware quality (`?quality=low|high`); `tools/bench/` benchmark. See docs/PERFORMANCE.md."},"693":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-89","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Measure on a real iPhone**: first model visible, fps while orbiting with 50 pins and idle CPU in iPhone Safari over 4G (Web Inspector timeline), for a real 20 MB capture and its `optimize-glb` output; record them in docs/PERFORMANCE.md next to the SwiftShader numbers."},"694":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-90","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Runtime decimation for phones**: lazy-load meshoptimizer's simplifier (in a worker) and simplify captures above ~500k triangles on handhelds behind the quality setting, if real-device numbers show the GPU, not fill rate, is the limit."},"695":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-91","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **KTX2/Basis E2E**: an ETC1S/UASTC fixture (needs a Basis encoder in Node, e.g. a WASM build) so the transcoder path is exercised in CI, not only raw KTX2."},"696":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-92","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Progressive capture loading**: show a coarse proxy (or the GLB's first LOD) while a big USDZ parses, and parse/weld it in a worker so the page stays responsive on phones."},"697":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-93","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **E2E tests**: Playwright suite (desktop + iPhone viewport, SwiftShader WebGL) covering view, edit, present, export/import, capture-bundle drop and re-drop, stored captures (reload, Open menu, forget), photo close-ups and lightbox, binary USDC with textures, error toasts, blocked storage, snapshot; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures; unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds; sharded CI job. See docs/TESTING.md."},"698":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-94","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **E2E coverage for app code**: collect V8 coverage from Chromium during the Playwright run (`page.coverage`) and merge it with the unit report, so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count toward the coverage ratchet."},"699":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-95","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Raise app.ts coverage**: the merged report has `ui/app.ts` at ~87% lines / 79% branches; cover its untested paths (see `coverage-all/`) and raise the merged thresholds in `tools/coverage/e2e-coverage.mjs`."},"700":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-96","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **E2E coverage of the minified build**: E2E in CI now runs the unminified, source-mapped build (`E2E_COVERAGE`); add a periodic run over the exact production build, or map coverage through the minifier's source maps."},"701":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-97","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **Render on demand**: only render when the camera, model or pins change (idle stage at 0 fps). Saves phone battery and makes the E2E suite much faster on SwiftShader (today every frame costs ~150–250 ms on CPU)."},"702":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-98","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **WebKit E2E project**: run the suite in Playwright WebKit (closest to iPhone Safari) on a macOS runner or with WebKit's Linux deps; the `mobile` project is Chromium with an iPhone viewport today."},"703":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-99","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **WebKit E2E in CI**: on GitHub's macOS runners (no GPU) every WebKit `page.goto` timed out while the same 45 tests pass locally in 17 s; find a WebGL path that works headless there (or a Linux runner with WebKit deps) and add the job back."},"704":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-100","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Real Safari storage in E2E**: WebKit test contexts have no OPFS, so the WebKit project only exercises the IndexedDB capture cache; cover OPFS in Safari on a real device (see the \"Capture cache on real Safari / iOS\" item)."},"705":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-101","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **One fixture generator**: fold `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` (GLB bundle for the Pages sample) and `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (USDZ bundle with photo poses) into `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` as variants, so there is one bike geometry and one pose layout to maintain."},"706":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-102","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Tilted/area bundles from the same generator**: `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` (auto-orient and crop fixtures) still uses the demo bike; make it a `make-capture-bundle.mjs` variant too."},"707":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-103","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."},"708":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-104","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."},"709":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-105","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."},"710":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-106","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Compare two bikes side by side."},"711":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-107","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."},"712":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-108","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."},"713":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-109","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"},"714":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"page","content":"How to test","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide"},"715":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-0","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"On your phone (no setup)"},"716":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-1","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"On a laptop"},"717":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-2","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"Make a synthetic capture bundle"},"718":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-3","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"What each PR adds"},"719":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-4","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide","content":"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."},"720":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-5","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."},"721":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-6","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."},"722":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-7","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."},"723":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-8","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."},"724":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-9","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."},"725":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-10","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."},"726":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-11","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."},"727":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-12","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"Try what a customer gets: open\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present**\non the phone. Only the bike, its name and price, and the Present card: swipe the card or tap\n‹ › to change area, tap a pin or a comment to fly to it, tap **Share** for the share sheet.\nAdd `&area=hs-fork` to open on the fork, or `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play."},"728":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-13","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"Embedding on a shop's site: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/embed-demo.html**\nshows the bike in an iframe driven by the buttons under it, and as a `<bike-viewer>` element."},"729":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-14","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The site is republished automatically on every push to the stack tip (the newest open PR nothing else is stacked on, or `develop` when none is open). Each open PR also gets its\nown copy at `https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (viewer at `/pr/<n>/app/`),\nlisted under **PR previews** on the home and Progress pages, so you can try a PR before\nmerging it. Each PR also gets a comment with Docs and Viewer links; closed previews are removed\ndaily when their PR is no longer open. The home page says which commit and branch it was built from."},"730":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-15","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"},"731":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-16","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."},"732":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-17","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"},"733":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-18","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."},"734":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-19","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"With a real capture: AirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone to the laptop and drop it on\nthe viewer. If the model does not show, note what the viewer says and add it to\nManual steps."},"735":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-20","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |","table":"table-0"},"736":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-21","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |","table":"table-0"},"737":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-22","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |","table":"table-0"},"738":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-23","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |","table":"table-0"},"739":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-24","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #9 Auto-orient | Make a tilted bundle (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out tilted.bikecapture.zip`) and **Open…** it: the bike stands up facing right and the toast says \"Auto-oriented\". In **Edit** try ↶ Undo at the top of the panel (back to lying on its side), then in **Edit → Model**, Auto-orient, the rotate ±90° buttons, Turn 180°, and type a real length in cm. Pin a comment first: it stays on the same spot through every rotation. |","table":"table-0"},"740":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-25","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR           | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #10 Crop box | Make an area-mode bundle with a floor and clutter (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out area.bikecapture.zip --rotate 0,0,0 --offset 0,0,0 --ground --mode area`) and **Open…** it: the toast suggests cropping. In **Edit → Model → Crop** turn the crop on, press **Fit to bike** (floor and crate disappear), then drag a face handle with the mouse or a finger: the camera must not orbit while dragging. Comments can't be pinned on cropped-away parts, and pins outside the box hide. |","table":"table-0"},"741":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-26","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #8 Share with customers | Open the published demo as a customer: `/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present` (on your phone too). Swipe between areas, tap a pin (leader line to its card), add `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play that pauses when you touch it. In the editor, **Share** on a published scene copies the link; on a local capture it exports a `.bikeshare.zip` that `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip>` installs. In Edit mode, drag comments to reorder them and use **bold**, *italic* and `- ` lists in bodies. |","table":"table-0"},"742":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-27","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #12 Performance | Orbit the demo, then let go: the camera glides to a stop and the page goes quiet (DevTools → Performance shows no frames while idle). Pins slide with the bike and dim when the bike is in front of them. On a phone, open a large capture: it appears, then picking a comment point is instant. Add `?quality=low` to the URL for the cheapest rendering. A GLB made with `node tools/optimize-glb.mjs in.glb out.glb` opens like any other. |","table":"table-0"},"743":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-28","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #21 One fixture generator + E2E coverage | Nothing new to click. `npm run fixture:photos` renders the fixture bike from every pose and writes `tools/fixtures/out/fixture-photos.bikecapture.zip`: **Open…** it, save an area and the close-ups show the bike from each camera. `npm run test:coverage && npm run e2e:coverage && npm run coverage:merge`, then open `coverage-all/index.html`: `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` are in the report. On a PR, the CI `coverage` job's summary has the merged numbers. |","table":"table-0"},"744":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-29","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                     | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #14 iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist**: orbits tick themselves after each completed pass, close-ups tick on tap, the top bar shows shots for the current pass. Export a bundle: the zip has `photos/*.jpg` next to `images/*.HEIC` and `manifest.json` has `\"photos\": \"photos/\"`. Open it in desktop Chrome: close-up photos appear without the HEIC decoder (no `heic` worker request in DevTools → Network). Web side alone: `npm test` (capture.test.ts covers the `photos/` preference). |","table":"table-0"},"745":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-30","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #16 WebKit E2E | Nothing new to click. On a Mac: `npx playwright install webkit && npm run e2e:webkit` runs the iPhone flows in Safari's engine (45 tests). Open the customer link in Safari on your phone: no console error when the Present card changes height. |","table":"table-0"},"746":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-31","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                        | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #19 Reconstruct: COLMAP → poses + package | Nothing to click yet. `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs --help`; with a COLMAP sparse model in TXT (`colmap model_converter … --output_type TXT`): `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs package --model model.glb --images frames --colmap sparse_txt --source video --backend colmap --name \"My bike\"`, then drop `My-bike.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer: the model loads and the close-up filmstrip shows the frames. `npm test` runs `reconstruct.test.ts` (round-trip and reprojection checks). |","table":"table-0"},"747":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-32","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                          | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #22 Snapshot / video export | Click **Snapshot**: pick 4×, Transparent, Show pins, **Save PNG**: the file opens with a see-through background and numbered pins. Chroma green gives a solid key color with no floor shadow. **Record 360° WebM** turns the camera once around the bike (8 s) and downloads a video; the view returns to where it was. In Safari the button says MP4. |","table":"table-0"},"748":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-33","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #13 Spec sheet | In **Edit**, the **Spec sheet** section lists the demo's specs: change a value, remove a row, **+ Add spec** and Tab from the name to the value. Clear a value: that row disappears from **Present** but stays in the editor. **Present** shows a \"Key specs\" table on the first card only; **Export** has a `specs` array. The customer link (`?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present`) shows it too, on a phone as part of the bottom sheet. |","table":"table-0"},"749":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-34","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #24 Prune stale previews + preview link | Open the PR on GitHub: a sticky comment (one per PR, updated on each push) links to its Docs and Viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/`. Nothing else to click: the daily **Prune previews** run (Actions → \"Prune PR previews\", or *Run workflow*) removes previews of closed PRs; close a PR and check that `/pr/<n>/` is gone after the next run. |","table":"table-0"},"750":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-35","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #25 COLMAP binary models | Nothing to click in the viewer. Locally, with a COLMAP sparse model in binary form (`cameras.bin`, `images.bin`, no `model_converter` step): `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses --colmap sparse_bin -o poses.json` writes the same poses as the TXT model. `npm test` runs `reconstruct.test.ts` on both formats, including truncated binary files. |","table":"table-0"},"751":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-36","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                               | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #26 Real intrinsics in close-ups | Nothing new to click. Close-up ranking now uses each photo's own `camera` from `poses.json`, so a bundle packaged from a COLMAP model (`cli.mjs poses` then `package`) ranks with its real focal length. Bundles without `camera` keep the 65° iPhone default. `npm test` runs `photos.test.ts`, including the fallback for bad camera values. |","table":"table-0"},"752":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-37","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #28 Save the capture checklist | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist** and tick a few close-ups, then export the bundle. In the zip, `manifest.json` has `\"checklist\": [{ \"id\", \"label\", \"done\" }]` with your ticks; it is left out when the bike has no checklist items. The viewer does not read it yet. The app itself is only compiled by the iOS CI check (no simulator run here). |","table":"table-0"},"753":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-38","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #27 Spec sheet on short screens | Open the preview viewer, add 6+ rows in Edit → Spec sheet, switch to Present on a laptop-size window: the first card shows 4 specs in two columns and **All specs (k)**; the bike sits fully above the card. On a phone the card is a bottom sheet as before. |","table":"table-0"},"754":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-39","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #15 Auto-publish + PR previews | Open the home page: **PR previews** lists open PRs with Viewer and Docs links; open `/bike-3d-brew/pr/15/app/` and the demo bike loads. Push to a PR and its preview updates a few minutes later (Actions → \"PR preview\"); close it and it disappears from the list. Merging into `develop` updates the main site (Actions → \"Publish site\"). |","table":"table-0"},"755":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-40","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #17 Site follows the stack tip | The home page has no credits box any more. Push to the top PR of the stack (or press *Run workflow* on Actions → \"Publish site\" from it): the main site shows that branch a few minutes later (the footer names it). Pushes to other branches skip publishing. |","table":"table-0"},"756":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-41","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                 | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #20 Embeddable viewer + share docs | Open `/bike-3d-brew/app/embed-demo.html` (also on the phone): the top bike is an iframe; **Next ›**, **Drivetrain**, **Green screen**, **Get state** drive it and the events show up in the log. The bottom one is a `<bike-viewer>` element opening on the Cockpit: it looks the same as the customer link while the page around it keeps its own serif font. Copy a snippet from the page into any HTML file to embed on another site. Customer links now take `&area=hs-fork`. |","table":"table-0"},"757":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-42","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                                | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #18 Undo/redo for the whole scene | In **Edit**, add a comment, move it with ↑, delete it, save a view as an area, then press Ctrl/Cmd+Z (or ↶ Undo at the top of the panel) step by step: each change comes back in order; Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z, Ctrl+Y or ↷ Redo replays them. Ctrl/Cmd+Z inside a text field only undoes your typing. Click the 1 cm nudge buttons quickly: one Undo puts them all back. Reload: the scene is as you left it (the history itself starts fresh). |","table":"table-0"},"758":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-43","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"},"759":{"id":"/docs/testing","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing"},"760":{"id":"/docs/testing-0","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Unit tests"},"761":{"id":"/docs/testing-1","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"What is not unit-tested, and why"},"762":{"id":"/docs/testing-2","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"Coverage"},"763":{"id":"/docs/testing-3","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"E2E coverage"},"764":{"id":"/docs/testing-4","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Fixtures"},"765":{"id":"/docs/testing-5","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"},"766":{"id":"/docs/testing-6","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"Rendered-photo bundle"},"767":{"id":"/docs/testing-7","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"End-to-end tests"},"768":{"id":"/docs/testing-8","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"The `window.__bike` test hook"},"769":{"id":"/docs/testing-9","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Writing reliable E2E tests"},"770":{"id":"/docs/testing-10","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"What the suite covers"},"771":{"id":"/docs/testing-11","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."},"772":{"id":"/docs/testing-12","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer | Where                     | Runs in                                        | Command    |\n| ----- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Unit  | `apps/web/test/*.test.ts` | Vitest, Node (happy-dom per file where needed) | `npm test` |","table":"table-0"},"773":{"id":"/docs/testing-13","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer    | Where                   | Runs in | Command                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| Coverage | same tests, V8 coverage | Vitest  | `npm run test:coverage` |","table":"table-0"},"774":{"id":"/docs/testing-14","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer      | Where                    | Runs in                                  | Command       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| End-to-end | `apps/web/e2e/*.spec.ts` | Playwright, Chromium + SwiftShader WebGL | `npm run e2e` |","table":"table-0"},"775":{"id":"/docs/testing-15","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer           | Where                  | Runs in                                        | Command                                          |\n| --------------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Merged coverage | unit + E2E V8 coverage | Playwright + `tools/coverage/e2e-coverage.mjs` | `npm run e2e:coverage && npm run coverage:merge` |","table":"table-0"},"776":{"id":"/docs/testing-16","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."},"777":{"id":"/docs/testing-17","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."},"778":{"id":"/docs/testing-18","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."},"779":{"id":"/docs/testing-19","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."},"780":{"id":"/docs/testing-20","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."},"781":{"id":"/docs/testing-21","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Zip parsing: `zipIndex.test.ts` hand-builds zips byte by byte (zip64 records and extra fields,\nforeign extras, odd methods, lying sizes), branches fflate never writes."},"782":{"id":"/docs/testing-22","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"USD: `usdz.test.ts` loads the committed binary USDC fixtures (`apps/web/test/fixtures/`, made\nby `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` with Pixar USD); `usd-units.test.ts` drives the crate\ndecoders and composer fast paths directly for encodings the fixtures do not contain."},"783":{"id":"/docs/testing-23","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"Excluded from unit coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead\n(and counted in the merged report, see \"E2E coverage\" below):"},"784":{"id":"/docs/testing-24","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File          | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.ts` | page bootstrap: the whole DOM plus WebGL |","table":"table-1"},"785":{"id":"/docs/testing-25","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/app.ts` | UI controller driving the WebGL `Viewer` |","table":"table-1"},"786":{"id":"/docs/testing-26","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                   | Why it cannot run in Node                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/viewer/Viewer.ts` | `WebGLRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, `ResizeObserver` |","table":"table-1"},"787":{"id":"/docs/testing-27","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                    | Why it cannot run in Node         |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/heic.worker.ts` | a Web Worker running libheif WASM |","table":"table-1"},"788":{"id":"/docs/testing-28","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `src/**/*.d.ts` | type declarations only    |","table":"table-1"},"789":{"id":"/docs/testing-29","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."},"790":{"id":"/docs/testing-30","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"`E2E_COVERAGE=1` (`npm run e2e:coverage`) makes the suite measure what the browser runs:"},"791":{"id":"/docs/testing-31","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"the build keeps source maps and skips minification (`apps/web/vite.config.ts`), so coverage\nmaps back to `src/` line by line;"},"792":{"id":"/docs/testing-32","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"every Chromium test starts `page.coverage` (`apps/web/e2e/test.ts`, the `test` all specs import;\nWebKit has no V8 coverage and is skipped); each worker merges its tests' V8 data and writes one\nfile to `coverage-e2e/raw/`;"},"793":{"id":"/docs/testing-33","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"the global teardown converts it with `ast-v8-to-istanbul` (the converter Vitest uses) to\n`coverage-e2e/coverage-final.json`, `src/` files only."},"794":{"id":"/docs/testing-34","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"`npm run coverage:merge` then merges `coverage/coverage-final.json` (unit, needs\n`npm run test:coverage` first) with every `coverage-e2e/**/coverage-final.json` into\n`coverage-all/` (text summary, HTML, `coverage-summary.json`). For files both runs measure, the\nE2E counts are kept only on the statements, functions and branches the unit report has: the\nproduction bundler and Vitest's transform place a few of them differently, and unmatched\nlocations would count twice. Files only the browser runs (`ui/app.ts`, `viewer/Viewer.ts`,\n`main.ts`, `entry.ts`, the customer presenter) come from E2E alone. At the time of writing:\nlines 97.3%, statements 95.9%, functions 92.9%, branches 90.5% (`ui/app.ts` 87% lines,\n`Viewer.ts` 96%). `THRESHOLDS` in `tools/coverage/e2e-coverage.mjs` is the merged ratchet, set\njust under those; same rule as the unit thresholds. Code that gets tree-shaken out of the build\nis absent from the E2E data rather than counted as uncovered, and the Web Worker\n(`heic.worker.ts`) is not measured."},"795":{"id":"/docs/testing-35","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#e2e-coverage","content":"CI runs both E2E shards with `E2E_COVERAGE`, uploads each shard's `coverage-final.json`, and a\n`coverage` job merges them with a fresh unit run, checks the merged thresholds, prints the totals\n(and `app.ts` / `Viewer.ts` / `main.ts`) in its step summary and uploads `coverage-all/`. So CI's\nE2E runs the unminified build; a local `npm run e2e` still tests the minified production build."},"796":{"id":"/docs/testing-36","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."},"797":{"id":"/docs/testing-37","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                                | Output                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Used by                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` | one bike geometry and one pose layout, as: the bundle variants below (USDZ, GLB, flat, broken…); the photo bundle (`--photos`, `buildPhotoBundle()`); the Pages sample (`--sample`, `buildSampleBundle()`). Deterministic | E2E (global setup), `fixtures.test.ts`, `photos.test.ts`, `capture.test.ts`, `viewer-node.test.ts`, `npm run fixtures`, `tools/publish-pages.sh` |","table":"table-2"},"798":{"id":"/docs/testing-38","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                          | Output                                                         | Used by                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/render-photos.mjs` | JPEG renders of the photo bundle's bike from each of its poses | E2E photo close-ups (`bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`), `npm run fixture:photos` |","table":"table-2"},"799":{"id":"/docs/testing-39","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                              | Output                                        | Used by                                               |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` | tilted and area-mode bundles of the demo bike | E2E auto-orient and crop (`tilted-bike`, `area-bike`) |","table":"table-2"},"800":{"id":"/docs/testing-40","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                     | Output                                                                       | Used by                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` | binary USDC (crate) packages in `apps/web/test/fixtures/` (committed, small) | `usdz.test.ts`, E2E \"binary USDC loads textured\"; needs Pixar USD to regenerate |","table":"table-2"},"801":{"id":"/docs/testing-41","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"},"802":{"id":"/docs/testing-42","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                   | What it exercises                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike.bikecapture.zip` | iOS layout (everything under one folder): manifest, ASCII-USD `model.usdz` of a low-poly vertex-colored bike (wheels, frame tubes, fork, cockpit, saddle, drivetrain as named meshes), `poses.json` with 32 cameras on three rings looking at the bike, 32 tiny placeholder PNG photos, `record.json` |","table":"table-3"},"803":{"id":"/docs/testing-43","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                       | What it exercises                                                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-glb.bikecapture.zip` | same bike as GLB (three's `GLTFExporter` in Node, vertex colors) |","table":"table-3"},"804":{"id":"/docs/testing-44","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-flat.bikecapture.zip` | flat zip with Finder `__MACOSX` junk |","table":"table-3"},"805":{"id":"/docs/testing-45","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                                | What it exercises                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-broken-poses.bikecapture.zip` | invalid `poses.json`: opens with a warning |","table":"table-3"},"806":{"id":"/docs/testing-46","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                            | What it exercises                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `bike-no-model.bikecapture.zip` | capture never reconstructed: error |","table":"table-3"},"807":{"id":"/docs/testing-47","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `not-a-zip.bikecapture.zip` | text with a `.zip` name: error |","table":"table-3"},"808":{"id":"/docs/testing-48","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                    | What it exercises |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `bike.usdz`, `bike.glb` | bare model files  |","table":"table-3"},"809":{"id":"/docs/testing-49","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."},"810":{"id":"/docs/testing-50","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"Two more variants, written on request:"},"811":{"id":"/docs/testing-51","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`--photos`: the same bike moved off-origin by `MODEL_ORIGIN` (like a real reconstruction, which\nis never centered: the viewer's `centerOnGround` undoes it), the orbit poses plus 8 close-ups\n(fork crown, front hub, chainring, rear hub, cockpit, saddle, and two non-drive-side shots), and\none photo per pose: placeholders, or the files of `--images` in sorted order (40 needed)."},"812":{"id":"/docs/testing-52","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`--sample`: the bike as GLB, the orbit poses and no photos, in a `synthetic-export/` folder;\n`createdAt` comes from `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` when set (`tools/publish-pages.sh` sets the commit\ntime)."},"813":{"id":"/docs/testing-53","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `--photos` variant's bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."},"814":{"id":"/docs/testing-54","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos, share, embed). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."},"815":{"id":"/docs/testing-55","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"A third project, `webkit`, runs the iPhone 14 profile in Playwright's WebKit (the engine of iPhone\nSafari) over the view, edit, present, photos, share and files specs. It is opt-in\n(`npm run e2e:webkit`, after `npx playwright install webkit`; the global setup also needs Chromium, which renders the photo fixtures) and local-only for now: on GitHub's\nGPU-less macOS runners every WebKit page load timed out (WebGL), see ROADMAP. It found two\nSafari-only issues: a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error from the Present card's height update\n(now applied on the next frame), and test contexts without OPFS, where captures use the\nIndexedDB fallback."},"816":{"id":"/docs/testing-56","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."},"817":{"id":"/docs/testing-57","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"},"818":{"id":"/docs/testing-58","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"wait for state instead of sleeping: `ready` (boot finished), a model in `viewer.modelRoot`,\n`viewer.flying` (camera animation running);"},"819":{"id":"/docs/testing-59","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"},"820":{"id":"/docs/testing-60","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."},"821":{"id":"/docs/testing-61","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."},"822":{"id":"/docs/testing-62","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."},"823":{"id":"/docs/testing-63","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."},"824":{"id":"/docs/testing-64","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Use `collectErrors(page)` and assert it is empty where a flow should be clean."},"825":{"id":"/docs/testing-65","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."},"826":{"id":"/docs/testing-66","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."},"827":{"id":"/docs/testing-67","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."},"828":{"id":"/docs/testing-68","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Reset view."},"829":{"id":"/docs/testing-69","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`export.spec.ts`: the Snapshot menu saves a 2× transparent PNG (IHDR size, RGBA, see-through\ncorner, opaque bike) and a 1× chroma-green one, restores the drawing buffer and clear color;\nrecords a turntable WebM (EBML header) and puts the camera back."},"830":{"id":"/docs/testing-70","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."},"831":{"id":"/docs/testing-71","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."},"832":{"id":"/docs/testing-72","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."},"833":{"id":"/docs/testing-73","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."},"834":{"id":"/docs/testing-74","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."},"835":{"id":"/docs/testing-75","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."},"836":{"id":"/docs/testing-76","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`specs.spec.ts`: edit the spec sheet (change, remove, add a row, Tab between fields keeps focus), Present shows only\nrows with a value and only on the first card, Export carries them; the customer link shows the published sheet."},"837":{"id":"/docs/testing-77","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."},"838":{"id":"/docs/testing-78","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`share.spec.ts`: the customer link (`?view=present`, `&area=`), Share, the share package →\n`publish-scene` → `?scene` round trip, kiosk and comment polish; on desktop and mobile."},"839":{"id":"/docs/testing-79","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`embed.spec.ts`: on `embed-demo.html`, the iframe's `bike-embed/1` bridge (commands move the\nbike, events come back, malformed messages are ignored) and the `<bike-viewer>` element\n(attributes, events, styles kept inside its shadow root, teardown on removal); desktop and mobile."},"840":{"id":"/docs/testing-80","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`perf.spec.ts`: an idle stage renders 0 frames, orbiting renders and stops again with pins moved, canvas snapshots work without a preserved drawing buffer, and Meshopt / Draco / KTX2 GLBs (from `tools/fixtures/make-compressed-glb.mjs`) open with self-hosted decoders and no foreign requests."},"841":{"id":"/docs/testing-81","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"The viewer renders on demand: to wait for a picture to settle use `viewer.rendering === false`; `viewer.renderCount` counts drawn frames."},"842":{"id":"/docs/testing-82","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"_Source: `docs/TESTING.md`_"}},"count":842},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":518,"2":837,"3":554,"4":279,"5":537,"6":818,"7":718,"8":280,"9":281,"10":524,"11":577,"12":687,"13":671,"14":323,"15":587,"16":398,"17":402,"18":401,"19":404,"20":403,"21":400,"22":610,"23":792,"24":750,"25":256,"26":258,"27":176,"28":116,"29":164,"30":248,"31":662,"32":802,"33":291,"34":290,"35":321,"36":639,"37":565,"38":217,"39":209,"40":211,"41":198,"42":170,"43":734,"44":182,"45":232,"46":134,"47":113,"48":683,"49":815,"50":604,"51":661,"52":599,"53":625,"54":738,"55":396,"56":397,"57":395,"58":399,"59":320,"60":317,"61":303,"62