`docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`_"],[758,"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"],[842,"_Source: `docs/TESTING.md`_"],[244,"_Source: `README.md`_"],[713,"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"],[423,"\"Copy embed\" for each bike in Studio;"],[669,"[ ] _(in progress)_ **Area views with depth + long specs** (owner review): Set view gives no feedback and the camera always orbits and zooms around the bike's center, so close-ups of a part cannot be framed; zoom toward the cursor, double-click to orbit around a point, confirm Set view; spec values longer than one line wrap in the editor and are clamped in Present."],[686,"[ ] _(in progress)_ **Clickable prototype (phase 0)**: `/app/proto/` with tabs Studio · Bike workspace · Bike page · Show customer · Storefront · Talk to a salesperson, for **new bikes** in the **US** (English, USD, email/SMS): components and upgrades on the demo bike with made-up data, no checkout or holds; checked on laptop, iPad and phone sizes."],[629,"[ ] **`ingest` CLI** (`tools/reconstruct/`, Node/TS + ffmpeg): photos and videos → sharp, deduplicated, EXIF-upright JPEG frames (variance-of-Laplacian sharpness + novelty selection, 80–200 frames), HEIC → JPEG, coverage report; unit-tested scoring."],[637,"[ ] **`package` polish**: convert OpenMVS OBJ/PLY to GLB (gltf-transform) and decimate for the web (`tools/optimize-glb.mjs`), crop the mesh to the dominant object, resize frames to ≤ 2048 px; show `source`/`backend` in the viewer's capture info."],[634,"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend colmap`**: COLMAP + OpenMVS via `tools/reconstruct/docker/` (and native), dense mesh + texture, crop the mesh to the dominant object, optional photo masking (rembg)."],[635,"[ ] **`reconstruct --backend object-capture`**: Swift CLI `tools/reconstruct/macos/` (`PhotogrammetrySession` over an image folder → `model.usdz` + poses), built by a path-filtered macos-latest CI job."],[676,"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."],[650,"[ ] **Auto-orient on real scans**: check the up/front heuristics (`scene/orient.ts`) against real Object Capture bikes (flat bars, kids' bikes, e-bikes with a battery, kickstands); tune the vote weights and add the cases as generated test fixtures."],[671,"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."],[620,"[ ] **Bun as package manager**: pinned Bun 1.4.4 installs (frozen `bun.lock`, root and `apps/docs`) locally, in `orca.yaml` and in GitHub Actions; Node 22 stays the runtime. Plan and trial: docs/BUN-MIGRATION.md."],[645,"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."],[644,"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."],[688,"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."],[640,"[ ] **Cloud backend**: one paid API behind `reconstruct --backend <vendor>` once the owner picks a vendor and budget."],[690,"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."],[652,"[ ] **Crop polish**: a rotatable (oriented) crop box for scans whose model-root axes are tilted; a floor-height handle that also re-grounds; show how many comments the crop hides."],[665,"[ ] **Cross-origin embed check**: an E2E run that loads `bike-viewer.js` and `embed.html` from a second origin (two preview ports) to prove CORS module loading, the `?origin=` lock end to end, and the BVH build falling back to the main thread when the worker cannot start cross-origin (shop pages); add `interval`/`idle` attributes to `<bike-viewer>`."],[708,"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."],[655,"[ ] **Drop the WASM HEIC decoder**: once every exported bundle has `photos/`, remove `libheif-js` (LGPL) or keep it only for old bundles; also check the exported zip size growth (~0.5 MB per photo) on a real capture."],[700,"[ ] **E2E coverage of the minified build**: E2E in CI now runs the unminified, source-mapped build (`E2E_COVERAGE`); add a periodic run over the exact production build, or map coverage through the minifier's source maps."],[658,"[ ] **Flag missing close-ups**: read the bundle manifest `checklist` in the viewer and warn about unticked close-ups (e.g. \"no derailleur photos\")."],[691,"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."],[707,"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."],[687,"[ ] **Hosting cost spike**: tenant auth, signed upload, public reads and the cost of 1,000 views of a 20 MB model on Cloudflare (R2/Workers/D1) vs Supabase; result in docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md section 9."],[666,"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."],[677,"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."],[695,"[ ] **KTX2/Basis E2E**: an ETC1S/UASTC fixture (needs a Basis encoder in Node, e.g. a WASM build) so the transcoder path is exercised in CI, not only raw KTX2."],[681,"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."],[693,"[ ] **Measure on a real iPhone**: first model visible, fps while orbiting with 50 pins and idle CPU in iPhone Safari over 4G (Web Inspector timeline), for a real 20 MB capture and its `optimize-glb` output; record them in docs/PERFORMANCE.md next to the SwiftShader numbers."],[659,"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."],[682,"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."],[660,"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."],[657,"[ ] **Portrait captures in close-ups**: test and handle rotated/portrait sample cameras in `scene/photos.ts` ranking (the horizontal FOV comes from `width` and `fx`; a portrait frame may need its axes swapped)."],[670,"[ ] **Present backdrop under the card**: on wide stages the viewport now ends above the card, so the bike renders smaller and a dark band shows behind the card; extend the stage backdrop under the card or let the card sit beside the bike on landscape screens."],[696,"[ ] **Progressive capture loading**: show a coarse proxy (or the GLB's first LOD) while a big USDZ parses, and parse/weld it in a worker so the page stays responsive on phones."],[699,"[ ] **Raise app.ts coverage**: the merged report has `ui/app.ts` at ~87% lines / 79% branches; cover its untested paths (see `coverage-all/`) and raise the merged thresholds in `tools/coverage/e2e-coverage.mjs`."],[632,"[ ] **Real COLMAP run**: check the converter on a real `colmap automatic_reconstructor` run over rendered fixture photos (part of the synthetic end-to-end eval)."],[704,"[ ] **Real Safari storage in E2E**: WebKit test contexts have no OPFS, so the WebKit project only exercises the IndexedDB capture cache; cover OPFS in Safari on a real device (see the \"Capture cache on real Safari / iOS\" item)."],[694,"[ ] **Runtime decimation for phones**: lazy-load meshoptimizer's simplifier (in a worker) and simplify captures above ~500k triangles on handhelds behind the quality setting, if real-device numbers show the GPU, not fill rate, is the limit."],[641,"[ ] **Splats from video**: COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio → `.spz`, opened through the M6 splat support."],[673,"[ ] **Square / vertical video formats**: the turntable records the stage's aspect; offer 1:1 and 9:16 framings (refit the camera to the bike) and a duration choice for Reels/Stories."],[689,"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."],[638,"[ ] **Synthetic end-to-end eval**: render the fixture bike with texture + textured floor from 60–120 posed cameras and as an orbit video (`tools/fixtures/render-photos.mjs`), run ingest → reconstruct → package, measure pose error after similarity alignment, Chamfer distance / completeness vs ground truth and close-up ranking; report in `docs/RECONSTRUCTION-EVAL.md`."],[706,"[ ] **Tilted/area bundles from the same generator**: `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` (auto-orient and crop fixtures) still uses the demo bike; make it a `make-capture-bundle.mjs` variant too."],[679,"[ ] **Turntable capture via the Mac**: a fixed-camera photo mode (plain `AVCapturePhotoOutput` shots while the bike spins on a turntable) reconstructed by `PhotogrammetrySession` on the Mac (see Mac high-detail reconstruction), which accepts turntable sets."],[674,"[ ] **Turntable in WebKit E2E**: check the MP4 path (Safari's MediaRecorder) in `npm run e2e:webkit`; the Chromium suite only covers WebM."],[683,"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."],[656,"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait c