ield, per-IP and per-bike rate limits, retried notifications, and a red\n\"undelivered\" alert in Studio if a message cannot be delivered."],[365,"**Add bike** starts a bike from a capture in the inbox, a `.bikecapture.zip`, a GLB, or just photos and specs."],[432,"**After sending**: a confirmation with what happens next and the shop's phone number. A double tap or a resend\nwithin a few minutes does not create a second message."],[581,"**AI image-to-3D**: never as \"the bike\". Only for placeholders, clearly labeled."],[488,"**Analytics**:"],[468,"**AR \"bike in your room\", AI-written descriptions, rep portals, session replay.** They are demos, extra\nmaintenance or privacy cost, and none of them answer what the bike is made of or how it fits."],[250,"**Auto-orient on a real capture** (needs the real-capture test below): open a real `.bikecapture.zip`\nand check the bike stands upright, front to the right (+X), drive side towards the default camera.\nIf not, note which button fixed it (Flip / Turn 180° / rotate) so the heuristics can be tuned."],[47,"**Auto-orient** (`apps/web/src/scene/orient.ts`, pure, unit-tested). Target frame: +X front,\n+Y up, +Z drive side, tyres on y = 0. Up to 50k strided vertices (≈3 ms for 1M vertices):"],[345,"**Bike page**, with the Show customer and Window modes."],[452,"**Billing**: plan and payment."],[28,"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."],[595,"**Built so far** (`node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs --help`):"],[583,"**Camera**: any camera ≥ 12 MP; fixed zoom (no zooming between shots); f/8–f/11 for depth of\nfield; ISO as low as possible; shutter ≥ 1/125 s handheld (tripod: anything); lock focus and\nexposure per ring; RAW+JPEG or high-quality JPEG; no portrait mode or beauty filters."],[224,"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."],[255,"**Capture guidance + JPEG export on a device** (#14, needs an iPhone with LiDAR): during a capture,\nopen the checklist: each completed orbit ticks the next orbit row and its shot count stays\nfixed after **Another pass**; the top bar counts shots for the current pass only. Export a\nbundle and check (a) export of ~150 photos finishes in reasonable time with the spinner, (b)\n`photos/IMG_*.jpg` are 2048 px on the long edge and **upright** for portrait and landscape\nshots (open a few on the Mac), (c) the zip grew by roughly 0.5 MB per photo, (d) close-ups in\ndesktop Chrome load without the `heic` worker. Note: the iOS app was compile-checked by CI only\n(no Xcode on the agent's Mac); the JPEG writer was verified with ImageIO on macOS."],[342,"**Captures** (in Studio): uploads from the iPhone app, and later photo/video reconstruction jobs, waiting to\nbecome bikes. This replaces today's \"AirDrop a zip to a laptop and drop it on the viewer\"."],[463,"**Checkout, carts or deposits in phases 1–2.** They touch payment, tax, stock races and each shop's own policy,\nand bikes over $1k sell in person after a test ride. Requests plus a human reply come first. Deposits only come\nonce a shop asks and picks a system of record."],[252,"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."],[580,"**Cloud API** only after the owner picks a vendor, a budget and accepts its data terms."],[261,"**Cloud API**: use a paid service (KIRI Engine API, Luma, Polycam…)? Which one, monthly budget,\nand are its data terms acceptable for customer bikes? Needs an account and an API key stored as a secret, never in the repo."],[457,"**Commercial changes**:"],[403,"**Compare**:"],[371,"**Component**: what a part is and why it matters (\"Shimano 105 Di2: wireless electronic shifting\")."],[393,"**Components and upgrades are the content**: two lists that mirror the pins. Tapping a row flies the 3D view\nto that part and opens its card. The guided tour (today's Present mode) walks the areas in order."],[497,"**Consumer claims**: component names and upgrade prices are the shop's own statements; the page dates them\n(\"specs checked <date>\") and says upgrade prices are confirmed in store."],[451,"**Content**: request actions, snippets and size tables."],[449,"**Contributor**: capture and save drafts only."],[443,"**Create bike**: opens the workspace with auto-orient and crop already applied, and the checklist carried over."],[46,"**Crop box** (`crop?: { min, max, enabled }`, model-root space, optional and lenient: a\nmalformed crop is dropped, swapped corners are reordered). The viewer turns it into six world\nclipping planes on the model's own materials (local clipping, shadows clipped too), recomputed only\nwhen the model transform or the box changes. Raycasts skip hits outside the box (no comments on\ncropped-away parts, no occlusion by them), pins outside it are hidden, and exact bounds (framing,\non-ground, auto-orient samples) only count kept vertices. Edit mode shows the box with one handle\nper face (`viewer/cropBox.ts`): pointer events in the capture phase, so mouse and touch drags never\norbit the camera; the face moves along its axis to the point nearest the pointer ray, clipping\nlive, and the store is updated once on release. \"Fit to bike\" (`scene/crop.ts`, pure) samples\npoints along triangle edges, cuts above the floor slab (a dense, wide band in the lower third of\nthe up axis) and keeps the largest 26-connected voxel cluster with a 2% margin. Area-mode captures\nget that box pre-computed but disabled, a hint in the toast, and auto-orient waits until the crop\nis on. Turning the crop on/off or fitting it re-grounds the visible part."],[249,"**Crop on a real area-mode capture**: capture a bike in area mode, open the bundle, turn on\nEdit → Model → Crop and check