 camera and\nwith frames pulled from a video. Detail `.full` for the web (then GLB + decimate), `.raw` only for archiving."],[386,"**Device**: a phone, over 4G."],[359,"**Devices**: laptop and iPad landscape; usable on a phone."],[141,"**Docs and agent cleanup PR:** README, AGENTS.md, docs/*.md and the agent skills switch to `bun install` /\n`bun run`, keeping `node` where a command really needs the Node runtime. A final grep for `npm ` and `npx `\nfinds only intentional leftovers, each with a reason."],[445,"**Domains**: a subdomain or path now, custom domains later."],[408,"**Done ↺**: resets the shared iPad for the next customer and clears anything they typed."],[262,"**Dulling spray**: acceptable on customer bikes, or only polarizer + diffuse light?"],[723,"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."],[448,"**Editor**: publish and answer messages."],[398,"**Entry**:"],[385,"**Entry**: `/s/:shop/:bike`. QR codes, social links and embeds all lead here, and today's `?scene=` links\nkeep working."],[414,"**Entry**: `/s/:shop`."],[367,"**Entry**: `/studio/bikes/:id`."],[358,"**Entry**: `/studio`, the default after sign-in."],[470,"**Every row has a shop**: tenant key `shopId` on everything. Access is never granted by an unguessable URL alone."],[402,"**Exists, partly**: Present mode, area stepping and kiosk auto-advance."],[387,"**Exists, partly**: the share link opens a read-only Present mode, with area deep links, the spec sheet,\nclose-up photos and kiosk mode. This is the most important screen."],[368,"**Exists, partly**: today's Edit mode, with areas, comments, spec sheet, model panel, crop and undo, becomes\nthe tool area of this page. Missing today: shop identity, cloud save, stock fields, publish state and the\nreadiness check."],[456,"**Exists**: capture, checklist and bundle export."],[428,"**Exists**: no."],[415,"**Exists**: no. This is the roadmap's \"Catalog page\"."],[360,"**Exists**: no. Today there is one scene at a time in browser storage."],[421,"**Exists**: the `embed.html` iframe and `<bike-viewer>`."],[29,"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."],[578,"**Fallback: COLMAP + OpenMVS in Docker** (Linux / CI / a rented GPU box) for when no Mac is\navailable: same `ingest` → `reconstruct` → `package` flow, plus mesh cropping to the bike.\nExpect worse wheels and paint."],[226,"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."],[485,"**Files**:"],[396,"**Fit line**: \"Sizes 49–61; ask us to find yours\" from the model's size table, never a guarantee."],[256,"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."],[42,"**GLB decoders** (`loaders.ts`, `gltfInfo.ts`): `extensionsUsed` decides which of Meshopt, Draco\nand KTX2/Basis is imported; their WASM ships in the build (no CDN)."],[260,"**GPU box**: rent (per-hour cloud GPU) or own an NVIDIA machine for COLMAP dense and Gaussian splats? Budget?"],[534,"**Hosting**: decided by the phase 0 cost spike (Cloudflare R2/Workers/D1 vs Supabase)."],[71,"**iframe** `…/app/embed.html?scene=<url>[&area=…][&kiosk=1…][&origin=https://shop.example]`:\nthe customer view (`present/embed.ts` reuses `customer.ts`, without taking focus) plus a\n`postMessage` bridge, protocol `bike-embed/1` (`scene/embed.ts`):"],[332,"**Inform, then hand over to a person.** The page sells nothing by itself. Its one action, **Talk to a\nsalesperson**, sends a short message by email or SMS with the bike and the parts the customer asked about."],[349,"**iPhone app**, which exists and gains \"Upload\"."],[27,"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."],[257,"**Let Actions publish the site** (auto-publish on `develop` and PR previews): Settings →\nActions → General → Workflow permissions → **Read and write permissions**, so the\n`GITHUB_TOKEN` of `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` may push to `gh-pages`. If `gh-pages` has a\nbranch protection rule, allow GitHub Actions to push to it. Check after the first run: the\n\"Publish site\" / \"PR preview\" run is green and Settings → Pages shows a new deployment. PRs\nonly get a preview once their branch contains `pr-preview.yml` (it runs from the PR's own\ncode), so PRs below this one in the stack get theirs after they are rebased or merged."],[225,"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."],[259,"**Mac for the default path**: is an Apple silicon Mac (macOS 14+) available to run Object Capture\n(`PhotogrammetrySession`) on photo folders? Without one, the fallback is COLMAP + OpenMVS on Linux."],[282,"**Meshopt** (default) decodes fastest and has the smallest decoder; **Draco** compresses geometry\nharder but costs a ~190 KB WASM download and slower decoding."],[341,"**Messages** (in Studio): \"Talk to a salesperson\" messages from bike pages (sizing, upgrades, test rides). Without\nthem the customer page has no purpose."],[44,"**Model transform.** The loader wraps the model so its native bounding box is centered on X/Z\nand rests on y = 0 (`centerOnGround`, deterministic per file); that frame is *model-root space*.\n`model.scale`, `model.rotation` (Euler XYZ, three.js convention) and `model.offset` are then\napplied to the root as `world = offset + R · (scale · p)`. Annotations and hotspot views stay in\nmodel-root space, so re-orienting a capture never detaches a comment. The overview camera is\nframed in world space (camera up is world +Y) and converted back."],[331,"**New bikes, explained part by part.** A 2026 road bike has forty brand photos, but no page lets a customer\nlook at *this shop's build* up close, tap the rear derailleur and read what it is, or see that the wheels can be\nupgraded for $600. The 3D model with **component pins** and **upgrade pins** is the advantage. Because a model is\nsold many times, one capture serves every unit of that model, and later every dealer if a brand supplies it."],[434,"**No browsing history on messages.** A message holds only what the customer typed and the bike."],[395,"**One action: Talk to a salesperson.** It opens the contact sheet (4.7). On phones it is sticky at the bottom."],[429,"**Opens as**: a sheet over the bike page, with the bike filled in."],[447,"**Owner**: everything, including billing."],[498,"**Phase 0: clickable prototype (no backend).**"],[503,"**Phase 1a: the pilot slice (one shop, operated by us).**"],[512,"**Phase 1b: what 1a proved is needed.**"],[516,"**Phase 2: the shop floor and the shop's own site.**"],[522,"**Phase 3: many shops, and the systems they already use.**"],[579,"**Photoreal later: Gaussian splats** from the same video (COLMAP poses + gsplat/nerfstudio, or\nPolycam/Luma/Scaniverse export) once the viewer loads `.spz`/`.ply` splats."],[383,"**Photos only on a phone**: on a phone this page shows the checklist and status. 3D editing waits for a\nbigger screen."],[79,"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."],[536,"**Pilot shop**: one US shop with a few current-season models."],[370,"**Pin kinds**:"],[41,"**Pins** (`pins.ts`): allocation-free projection against a cached viewport size, transform-only\nwrites for pins that moved, `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage,\nocclusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that finish on idle animation frames."],[348,"**Platform console**, later."],[465,"**POS or inventory sync in phases 1–2.** We only own the listing state and keep an optional external ID. The page\nnever claims live availability we do not sync."],[724,"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."],[394,"**Price is optional**: the shop chooses whether to show \"from $4,299\" and upgrade price differences. It is\ninformation, not a cart: there is no total, no checkout and no hold."],[537,"**Pricing**: per shop per month with a cap on live models (recommended) vs per model."],[492,"**Privacy roles (US first; GDPR-ready)**: the US launch needs a privacy notice at collection (CCPA/CPRA style),\nTCPA consent for texts, and deletion on request. The roles below also make an EU launch possible later:"],[440,"**Privacy tools**: delete a lead, export one person's data, and delete messages automatically after the shop's\nretention period (12 months by default)."],[535,"**Product name and domain.**"],[379,"**Publishing is versioned**:"],[407,"**QR hand-off**: the customer scans the code and gets the bike page on their phone. The shop's numbers show\n\"taken home from the floor\"."],[39,"**Quality** (`quality.ts`): pixel ratio ≤ 2 (1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles),\nMSAA only at 1×, smaller hard shadows on phones; `?quality=low|high` overrides."],[78,"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(per-sample `camera` intrinsics when present, else an assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."],[40,"**Raycasts** (`bvh.ts`): after the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a\nthree-mesh-bvh hierarchy (built in `bvh.worker.ts` for big meshes, indirect so the GPU index buffer\nis untouched). `viewer.raycastReady` tells the pins when occlusion tests are cheap."],[375,"**Readiness check**:"],[254,"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."],[253,"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."],[466,"**Real-time collaborative editing** (the roadmap's \"Collaborative comments\"). One to three people edit per shop,\nso last-write-wins, undo history and \"edited by\" are enough."],[590,"**Reflective paint**: polarizer on the lens (and ideally on the lights), more diffuse light, or a\nremovable dulling spray if the shop agrees. Record which one you used in the manifest notes."],[38,"**Render on demand** (`renderScheduler.ts`): the animation loop only runs while something changes.\nViewer methods (`setModel`, `setView`, `applyTransform`, `setBackground`, resize, controls input,\nfly-to) call `viewer.requestRender()`; **code that mutates the three.js scene directly must call it\ntoo**. The shadow map is redrawn only on `requestRender()` (scene changes), never for camera-only\nframes. Frame listeners (`onFrame`, pins) run after drawn frames only."],[228,"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."],[439,"**Scope**: assign a lead to someone and export CSV. This is not a CRM."],[227,"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."],[582,"**Setup**: bike on a stand or a turntable, wheels off the ground or the kickstand hidden; plain\nmatte backdrop that differs from the paint; textured floor or newspaper so the poses solve;\nsoft, even light (two softboxes at 45°, or overcast outdoors), no direct sun, no flash."],[241,"**Share** gives customers a read-only link (`?scene=…&view=present`). To put a bike on a shop's own\nsite, use an iframe or the custom element (live demo: `/app/embed-demo.html`):"],[444,"**Shop**: profile (name, address, hours, phone, SMS number) and branding (logo and accent color first; fonts later)."],[430,"**Short form**: a name and one contact method, and how the customer wants the reply (email or text).\nTopic chips are optional. If the customer tapped an upgrade before opening the sheet, it is named in the message."],[584,"**Shots: 120–200** total, 70–80 % overlap between neighbors:"],[453,"**Shows**: shops, plan, live bikes, storage, upload failures, last activity and suspension."],[592,"**Shutter speed ≥ 1/250 s** (set it in a pro camera app such as Blackmagic Camera; the stock iOS app\npicks it automatically), otherwise motion blur kills features on spokes and cables."],[593,"**Slow orbit**: about 60–90 s per ring (≈ 4–6°/s), three rings as above, then slow passes over\nthe close-up areas. 3–5 minutes of footage in total."],[431,"**SMS consent**: choosing \"Text message\" shows one line of consent copy and \"Reply STOP to opt out\" (TCPA and\ncarrier rules). Email needs no extra consent."],[374,"**Snippets**: a shop-wide library of reusable comments, keyed by component (\"Shimano 105 Di2\", \"tubeless ready\").\nWriting copy is the real cost of each listing, and snippets cut it to minutes."],[77,"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."],[45,"**Spec sheet** (`specs?: { label, value }[]`, free text, optional and lenient like the crop: rows\nthat are not two strings are dropped, text is trimmed and capped, at most 40 rows; `scene/specs.ts`).\nRows keep the order staff typed. Present mode shows rows with a value on the first card\n(`PresentView`, so the customer link gets it too); a row with an empty value is kept for staff only."],[446,"**Staff and roles**:"],[334,"**Staff have one hand and 30 seconds.** Floor tools are big buttons, no setup, task words (\"Show customer\",\n\"Preview\"), never \"Edit mode\" or \"Present mode\"."],[361,"**States**: Draft → Live → Archived, plus **Unavailable** (no Reserved or Sold: the page lists a *model*\nthe shop carries, not one physical unit)."],[560,"**Status of the facts below (2026-10-27).** This first pass comes from the author's own knowledge\nof these tools. It was **not** re-checked against vendor pages in this session because the budget\nwas cut short. Prices, limits and terms of cloud services change often: check each `verify:` item\nbefore anyone commits money or customer photos. What was checked in the sandbox: Ubuntu 24.04\nships `colmap 3.9.1` in `universe` (`apt-get install colmap` works, CPU build without CUDA). There\nis no Docker daemon and no GPU here, so OpenMVS and dense reconstruction were not run."],[442,"**Statuses**: uploading, processing, ready, and failed with what to do next."],[480,"**Stock stays out of the scene**: price and availability change often, so they live in `Bike`.\n`bike-scene/1` grows only by optional, presentation-only fields:"],[346,"**Storefront** and **Embed**."],[344,"**Studio**: Library, Bike workspace, Messages, Captures, Settings."],[454,"**Support access**: per shop, time-limited and logged. It never shows bike content in the overview."],[471,"**Tables**:"],[347,"**Talk to a salesperson** (contact sheet)."],[263,"**Test capture**: shoot one bike with the photo protocol and one 4K video with the video protocol,\nso the pipeline can be measured on real input (keep the files out of the repo)."],[333,"**The customer never \"uses an app\".** They tap a link (the shop's site, Instagram, a QR on the floor bike's\ntag, a text from staff). Specs and the contact button never wait for the model to load."],[388,"**The still image comes first**, within a byte budget:"],[589,"**Turntable vs walk-around**: turntable with a fixed camera is fastest and steadiest, but the\nbackground must stay out of frame or be masked (static background + rotating bike confuses SfM).\nWalk-around works anywhere and is better for the floor features. Object Capture handles both."],[30,"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."],[362,"**Unavailable**: the model is out of stock or discontinued. The page stays up and says \"Ask us about\navailability\", so old links still inform."],[372,"**Upgrade**: what the shop can swap or add, with the price difference."],[369,"**Upgrades are structured**: each Upgrade pin names the stock part, the upgrade part, its price difference\n(\"+$600\") and an optional note (\"ask about fitting time\"). Upgrade prices show as add-ons to the model price,\nnever as a configurator total."],[459,"**Upload** to Captures instead of AirDrop;"],[722,"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."],[422,"**What it needs for commercial use**:"],[436,"**What it shows**: requests per bike, with type, contact, source (Instagram, QR, embed, direct), time and status."],[25,"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."],[455,"**When**: not before about ten active shops. Until then, the database dashboard and scripts are the console."],[26,"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."],[538,"**Who captures**: shop staff by default, or brands supply one scan per model for every dealer. New bikes make\nbrand scans more valuable than before."],[397,"**Who**: a salesperson with a customer, and the shop-window screen."],[384,"**Who**: customers at home and in store."],[413,"**Who**: customers."],[427,"**Who**: customers."],[435,"**Who**: owner and salespeople."],[357,"**Who**: owner and staff."],[366,"**Who**: staff and owner."],[409,"**Window mode**: a locked kiosk loop across every live bike, for a dedicated display only. Exiting needs a\nPIN. On the shared iPad, Show customer is not a kiosk."],[527,"*Done when*: a shop we have never met signs itself up and publishes a bike."],[521,"*Done when*: a three-person shop keeps dozens of listings current, splits capturing from selling, and knows which\nlinks bring requests."],[502,"*Done when*: the owner has clicked through every screen and settled the decisions in section 9."],[511,"*Done when*: the pilot shop lists bikes it chose (photos first, 3D where it helps), shares them, and a customer\nrequest reaches the shop and gets answered. The listing-time target is set from what was measured."],[811,"`--photos`: the same bike moved off-origin by `MODEL_ORIGIN` (like a real reconstruction, which\nis never centered: the viewer's `centerOnGround` undoes it), the orbit poses plus 8 close-ups\n(fork crown, front hub, chainring, rear hub, cockpit, saddle, and two non-drive-side shots), and\none photo per pose: placeholders, or the files of `--images` in sorted order (40 needed)."],[812,"`--sample`: the bike as GLB, the orbit poses and no photos, in a `synthetic-export/` folder;\n`createdAt` comes from `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` when set (`tools/publish-pages.sh` sets the commit\ntime)."],[283,"`--simplify <ratio>` (meshoptimizer's simplifier, `--error` as a fraction of the mesh radius,\ndefault 0.001) is the decimation step for phones: Object Capture's `.full` detail is far more than a\n6\" screen shows."],[284,"`--textures webp|--max-texture` use sharp (installed with glTF Transform). `ktx2` (ETC1S) keeps\ntextures compressed in GPU memory (a 4096² texture: 64 MB as RGBA8, 8–16 MB transcoded to ETC2, ASTC or BC7), the\nbiggest memory win on phones, and needs `toktx` on PATH."],[400,"`/s/:shop/:bike?mode=store` on the shared iPad;"],[401,"`/s/:shop/window` on a dedicated screen."],[95,"`apps/web/playwright.config.ts:61-64` invokes `npx vite build`/`npx vite preview`. Replace with `bunx` or direct local binaries in its own verified edit; otherwise this keeps npm/npx on PATH. `tools/bench/bench.mjs:33-36` and `tools/optimize-glb.mjs:73` similarly use npx."],[4,"`bike-capture/1` (iOS export zip, or `tools/reconstruct` package)"],[8,"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"],[9,"`bike-share/1` (share package, `*.bikeshare.zip`) and the customer link"],[474,"`Bike`: shop, slug, state, price (optional), currency, sizes, type, brand, model year, external ID, published version, draft version."],[475,"`BikeVersion`: a frozen `bike-scene/1` scene, poster, model and photo object IDs, published by, published at."],[801,"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"],[139,"`bun install --frozen-lockfile` on a clean clone on macOS."],[175,"`bun run docs:build` succeeds but the root and docs scripts explicitly invoke `npm`; successful output shows `npm --prefix apps/docs run build` then `npm run sync`. This silently retains npm as a script runner for those nested commands. Playwright's configured server explicitly invokes `npx` in `apps/web/playwright.config.ts` and succeeds by resolving npx from PATH. The plan should replace those nested package-manager calls with Bun equivalents or clearly retain npm, not leave an accidental fallback."],[144,"`bunx` may resolve packages differently from npx; Playwright installation and the configured local server must be checked in CI."],[834,"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."],[476,"`Capture`: shop, bundle object, status, error."],[34,"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."],[33,"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."],[790,"`E2E_COVERAGE=1` (`npm run e2e:coverage`) makes the suite measure what the browser runs:"],[830,"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."],[839,"`embed.spec.ts`: on `embed-demo.html`, the iframe's `bike-embed/1` bridge (commands move the\nbike, events come back, malformed messages are ignored) and the `<bike-viewer>` element\n(attributes, events, styles kept inside its shadow root, teardown on removal); desktop and mobile."],[479,"`Event`: shop, bike, kind, source, day-scoped session hash."],[829,"`export.spec.ts`: the Snapshot menu saves a 2× transparent PNG (IHDR size, RGBA, see-through\ncorner, opaque bike) and a 1× chroma-green one, restores the drawing buffer and clear color;\nrecords a turntable WebM (EBML header) and puts the camera back."],[837,"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."],[832,"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."],[477,"`Lead`: shop, bike, type, contact, time window, status, assignee, source, consent notice version, delete-after date."],[817,"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"],[765,"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"],[473,"`Member`: user, shop, role."],[61,"`mountPresenter(container, options)` (`present/BikePresenter.ts`) renders the customer view into\nan element or a shadow root and sizes itself from it. Options: `scene` (a `bike-scene/1` object or\na scene URL, checked by `loadPublishedScene`), `pageHref`, `header`, `share`, `background`,\n`kiosk: { interval, idle, autoplay }`, `autofocus`, `area`. The returned controller:"],[794,"`npm run coverage:merge` then merges `coverage/coverage-final.json` (unit, needs\n`npm run test:coverage` first) with every `coverage-e2e/**/coverage-final.json` into\n`coverage-all/` (text summary, HTML, `coverage-summary.json`). For files both runs measure, the\nE2E counts are kept only on the statements, functions and branches the unit report has: the\nproduction bundler and Vitest's transform place a few of them differently, and unmatched\nlocations would count twice. Files only the browser runs (`ui/app.ts`, `viewer/Viewer.ts`,\n`main.ts`, `entry.ts`, the customer presenter) come from E2E alone. At the time of writing:\nlines 97.3%, statements 95.9%, functions 92.9%, branches 90.5% (`ui/app.ts` 87% lines,\n`Viewer.ts` 96%). `THRESHOLDS` in `tools/coverage/e2e-coverage.mjs` is the merged ratchet, set\njust under those; same rule as the unit thresholds. Code that gets tree-shaken out of the build\nis absent from the E2E data rather than counted as uncovered, and the Web Worker\n(`heic.worker.ts`) is not measured."],[789,"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."],[230,"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."],[597,"`package --model <glb|usdz|ply> --images <frames> (--colmap <dir> | --poses <file>) --source photos|video --backend <b> [--name] [-o]`\n(`package.mjs`): flat zip with `manifest.json`, `model.<ext>`, `poses.json`, `images/*.jpg`\n(stored, not deflated). It refuses non-JPEG frames, duplicate names and poses whose image is missing."],[840,"`perf.spec.ts`: an idle stage renders 0 frames, orbiting renders and stops again with pins moved, canvas snapshots work without a preserved drawing buffer, and Meshopt / Draco / KTX2 GLBs (from `tools/fixtures/make-compressed-glb.mjs`) open with self-hosted decoders and no foreign requests."],[574,"`PhotogrammetrySession` takes a folder URL of images from any camera. EXIF focal length helps.\nDepth and gravity metadata (iPhone LiDAR HEIC) improve scale and orientation. Without them the\nscale is arbitrary and the model may come out tilted, so auto-orient (ROADMAP M2) becomes required."],[835,"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."],[596,"`poses --colmap <sparse_model> [-o poses.json]` (`colmap.mjs`): reads COLMAP's TXT or binary model directly (TXT wins when both are present; no `model_converter` step needed) and writes\n`bike-poses/1`. Samples are ordered by image name, `file` is the image basename, and each sample\nkeeps the real intrinsics as `camera` (pixels; `SIMPLE_*`/`RADIAL*` models give fx = fy = f;\ndistortion is not kept). The model frame is COLMAP's world frame (arbitrary scale and up), which\nOpenMVS keeps for the mesh, so the viewer's auto-orient stands the bike up."],[831,"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."],[838,"`share.spec.ts`: the customer link (`?view=present`, `&area=`), Share, the share package →\n`publish-scene` → `?scene` round trip, kiosk and comment polish; on desktop and mobile."],[472,"`Shop`: slug, profile, branding, request actions, plan."],[478,"`Snippet`: shop, component key, markdown."],[836,"`specs.spec.ts`: edit the spec sheet (change, remove, add a row, Tab between fields keeps focus), Present shows only\nrows with a value and only on the first card, Export carries them; the customer link shows the published sheet."],[60,"`src/entry.ts` loads only `present/BikePresenter.ts` for `?view=present`, so customers never\ndownload editing code. `&area=<hotspot id or index>` opens the link on an area."],[833,"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."],[281,"`tools/optimize-glb.mjs` turns a GLB (for a USDZ capture, first `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`) into a\nphone-friendly one with glTF Transform:"],[59,"`tools/publish-scene.mjs` validates a package (size limits: zip 300 MB, model 250 MB, JSON 2 MB,\n8 MB × 64 photos; JPEG only; no paths outside the package; `parseScene`) and installs it under\n`apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`. The customer link is\n`…/app/?scene=scenes/<id>/scene.bike.json&view=present` (`kiosk=1&interval=<s>&idle=<s>` for a\nshop screen). Scene, model and photo URLs must be same-origin or https."],[35,"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, welds the face-varying expansion back into an indexed\nmesh (`../weld.ts`: 2.9M → 0.49M vertices for 1M triangles), waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."],[828,"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Reset view."],[14,"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."],[558,"> \"We can have the best 3D experience, but if it doesn't come from a collection of photos and\n> videos of a bike, it's not useful.\" (owner)"],[327,"> **Owner decisions, 12 Nov 2026 (these override anything below that disagrees).**\n>\n> - **New bikes only.** No used or consignment bikes, so there are no condition notes, grades or defect lists.\n> - **A showroom, not a sales page.** The customer page informs buyers: see the bike in 3D, explore its\n>   components, and check the upgrades the shop offers. It has no checkout, hold, reservation or \"buy\" flow. Its\n>   one action is **Talk to a salesperson**.\n> - **US market first.** English, USD (`$4,299`), and contact by email or SMS (a text message), plus a call\n>   button. No WhatsApp.\n> - **Bun 1.4.4** as the package manager, with Node 22 as the runtime, an empty trusted-scripts list, and\n>   GitHub Actions on version tags (see BUN-MIGRATION.md)."],[274,"| Area                        | What                                                                                                                                                                                             | Where    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------- |\n| No preserved drawing buffer | The canvas keeps its last frame while idle anyway; `screenshot()` and the Snapshot / turntable exports render right before reading. Saves a full-screen copy per frame on tile-based phone GPUs. | `Viewer` |"],[279,"| Area                       | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | Where                                     |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Lazy, self-hosted decoders | A GLB's `extensionsUsed` decides which decoder is imported: Meshopt (~26 KB JS with inline WASM), Draco (glTF build, ~190 KB WASM, workers), KTX2/Basis (~530 KB WASM, workers). three's loaders resolve the files with `new URL(…, import.meta.url)`, so Vite ships them in `dist/assets/`; nothing comes from a CDN. Plain GLBs fetch none. | `viewer/loaders.ts`, `viewer/gltfInfo.ts` |"],[275,"| Area                 | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where               |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Device-aware quality | Pixel ratio ≤ 2 (phones show no gain at 3×, which shades 2.25× the pixels), 1.5 on phones for captures over 400k triangles; MSAA only at 1× (2× already supersamples); 1024² hard shadows on phones, 2048² soft on desktop. `?quality=low` (1×, 512² shadows) and `?quality=high` (up to 3×, MSAA) override. | `viewer/quality.ts` |"],[276,"| Area               | What                                                                                                                                                                                 | Where                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| Welded USDZ meshes | three expands face-varying primvars to three vertices per triangle; identical corners are merged back into an indexed mesh (O(n) open-addressing hash over typed arrays, bit-exact). | `viewer/weld.ts`, `usd/usdz.ts` |"],[272,"| Area             | What                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Where                                                 |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Render on demand | The animation loop runs only while something changes (controls input and damping, a fly-to, a model / background / pin / size change). An idle stage draws **0 frames**; a hidden tab stops the loop. | `viewer/renderScheduler.ts`, `Viewer.requestRender()` |"],[273,"| Area           | What                                                                                                                                                                                         | Where                                     |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Cached shadows | The sun and the model stand still while the camera orbits, so the shadow map is redrawn only when the scene changes, not for camera frames (that pass re-draws every triangle of the model). | `Viewer` (`shadowMap.autoUpdate = false`) |"],[277,"| Area         | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Where                                          |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| BVH raycasts | After the first frame of a model, meshes over 5k triangles get a three-mesh-bvh hierarchy, built in a worker for big meshes (copies, never transfers, so the geometry stays usable; indirect, so the GPU index buffer is untouched). Picking and pin occlusion use it. | `viewer/bvh.ts`, `bvhImpl.ts`, `bvh.worker.ts` |"],[278,"| Area | What                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Where            |\n| ---- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Pins | Projection into a scratch object against a cached viewport size (no layout reads), transform-only writes for pins that moved, an `offscreen` class for pins behind the camera or off the stage, occlusion raycasts under a 3 ms per-frame budget that continue on idle animation frames (without re-rendering) until every visible pin is current. Skipped until the BVH exists for big models. | `viewer/pins.ts` |"],[339,"| Brief  | Problem                             | Plan                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Client | A viewer is not what a buyer needs. | A **Bike page** (one bike: decide and act) and a **Storefront** (the shop's catalog). Both public, no customer login. The **Embed** on the shop's own site is the main way customers reach it. |"],[337,"| Brief | Problem                                                                                                                     | Plan                                                                                                                                                 |\n| ----- | -------------------------------------