` splats; no clean mesh | Free (open source) / app plans | **Photoreal option**: needs splat viewer support (ROADMAP M6) |"],[571,"| Option                                                                              | Input      | Runs on                   | Thin parts           | Gloss   | Output | Cost                | Verdict                                                                                                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------- | -------------------- | ------- | ------ | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **AI image-to-3D**: TRELLIS (Microsoft, MIT), Hunyuan3D 2.x (Tencent), Tripo, Meshy | 1–4 photos | GPU (open models) or SaaS | **Invents** geometry | Invents | GLB    | Free / SaaS credits | Not for a sales model of *this* bike. OK for placeholders, catalog thumbnails or \"illustrative\" models clearly labeled as such |"],[567,"| Option                                                                | Input                        | Runs on                                                                                                                                             | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output                                                      | Cost                          | Verdict                              |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **COLMAP** (SfM + MVS) + **OpenMVS** (densify, mesh, refine, texture) | Any images; video via frames | Linux/macOS/Windows; Docker; SfM fine on CPU; COLMAP dense *needs* CUDA, OpenMVS dense runs on CPU (slow: tens of minutes to hours for 150 × 12 MP) | Poor to fair | Poor  | PLY/OBJ + texture; camera poses (`cameras/images/points3D`) | Free (BSD / AGPL for OpenMVS) | **Fallback** (Linux, server, no Mac) |"],[566,"| Option                                                         | Input                                                                                   | Runs on                                                                                                     | Thin parts                     | Gloss | Output                                                                                     | Cost            | Verdict     |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ----------- |\n| **Apple Object Capture** (`PhotogrammetrySession`, RealityKit) | Any folder of JPEG/HEIC/PNG (not only iPhone photos); depth and gravity help if present | macOS 12+ (detail levels `.reduced` … `.raw`; Apple silicon or a Mac with a capable GPU), iOS 17+ on device | Fair; better with close passes | Fair  | USDZ (textured), poses via `.poses` request (macOS 14 / iOS 17+), automatic object masking | Free with a Mac | **Default** |"],[568,"| Option                     | Input  | Runs on                                   | Thin parts   | Gloss | Output        | Cost        | Verdict                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----- | ------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Meshroom / AliceVision** | Images | Linux/Windows, CUDA needed for depth maps | Poor to fair | Poor  | OBJ + texture | Free (MPL2) | Worse than COLMAP + OpenMVS for automation; skip |"],[57,"| Path                 | Content      |\n| -------------------- | ------------ |\n| `model.glb\\|usdz\\|…` | the 3D model |"],[55,"| Path              | Content                                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-share.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-share/1\", id, name, createdAt, scene, model, photos }` |"],[56,"| Path              | Content                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `scene.bike.json` | the `bike-scene/1` scene, model URL rewritten to the packaged file |"],[16,"| Path            | Content                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, photos?, imageCount, checklist?: [{ id, label, done }], source?: \"photos\"\\|\"video\", backend? }` (`checklist` is optional and written by iOS; `source`/`backend` only from `tools/reconstruct`) |"],[58,"| Path           | Content                                      |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/*.jpg` | the close-ups referenced by `Hotspot.photos` |"],[21,"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |"],[18,"| Path         | Content                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16], camera? }] }` (column-major camera→model; `camera: { model, width, height, fx, fy, cx, cy }` in pixels from COLMAP; `width`/`height`/`fx`/`fy` set each photo's field of view in close-up ranking, invalid values are ignored) |"],[17,"| Path         | Content                                                                                     |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up (`tools/reconstruct` writes `model.glb`, or `.usdz` / `.ply`) |"],[20,"| Path      | Content                                                                                                                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `photos/` | optional: JPEG copies of `images/`, same file stems, ≤ 2048 px long edge, EXIF orientation baked into the pixels (orientation 1). Listed as `manifest.photos` |"],[19,"| Path      | Content                                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos (reconstruction input); `tools/reconstruct`: the JPEG frames |"],[351,"| Person                                        | Device              | Jobs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Staff who capture** (mechanic, salesperson) | iPhone, shared iPad | list a bike between repair jobs: photos and specs first, a 3D capture when there is time, then areas, component and upgrade pins and reused snippets; save a draft. Mechanics know the components; salespeople own the customer wording. How long each step really takes is measured with the pilot shop before any target is promised |"],[352,"| Person                       | Device               | Jobs                                                                                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Salesperson on the floor** | shared iPad, shop TV | show a bike, or two side by side, at the area the customer asks about; hand off a link; reset for the next customer |"],[354,"| Person                | Device                  | Jobs                                              |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Customer in store** | their own phone, via QR | look again later, send it to a partner, come back |"],[353,"| Person               | Device               | Jobs                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Customer at home** | phone, often over 4G | understand the bike before visiting: components, upgrade options, sizes, close-ups; message a salesperson |"],[350,"| Person              | Device       | Jobs                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Owner / manager** | laptop, iPad | list bikes, set prices, choose what is public, brand the pages, see which bikes and links bring requests, invite staff, pay us |"],[356,"| Person            | Device | Jobs                                                                                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Us (platform)** | laptop | onboard shops, fix failed uploads, watch storage and limits, suspend abuse; never browse shop data by default |"],[355,"| Person        | Device | Jobs                                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Brand rep** | any    | look at a dealer's demo bike. The public bike page covers this; no rep portal until a brand pays for it |"],[746,"| PR                                        | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #19 Reconstruct: COLMAP → poses + package | Nothing to click yet. `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs --help`; with a COLMAP sparse model in TXT (`colmap model_converter … --output_type TXT`): `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs package --model model.glb --images frames --colmap sparse_txt --source video --backend colmap --name \"My bike\"`, then drop `My-bike.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer: the model loads and the close-up filmstrip shows the frames. `npm test` runs `reconstruct.test.ts` (round-trip and reprojection checks). |"],[743,"| PR                                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #21 One fixture generator + E2E coverage | Nothing new to click. `npm run fixture:photos` renders the fixture bike from every pose and writes `tools/fixtures/out/fixture-photos.bikecapture.zip`: **Open…** it, save an area and the close-ups show the bike from each camera. `npm run test:coverage && npm run e2e:coverage && npm run coverage:merge`, then open `coverage-all/index.html`: `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` are in the report. On a PR, the CI `coverage` job's summary has the merged numbers. |"],[749,"| PR                                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #24 Prune stale previews + preview link | Open the PR on GitHub: a sticky comment (one per PR, updated on each push) links to its Docs and Viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/`. Nothing else to click: the daily **Prune previews** run (Actions → \"Prune PR previews\", or *Run workflow*) removes previews of closed PRs; close a PR and check that `/pr/<n>/` is gone after the next run. |"],[744,"| PR                                     | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #14 iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist**: orbits tick themselves after each completed pass, close-ups tick on tap, the top bar shows shots for the current pass. Export a bundle: the zip has `photos/*.jpg` next to `images/*.HEIC` and `manifest.json` has `\"photos\": \"photos/\"`. Open it in desktop Chrome: close-up photos appear without the HEIC decoder (no `heic` worker request in DevTools → Network). Web side alone: `npm test` (capture.test.ts covers the `photos/` preference). |"],[756,"| PR                                 | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #20 Embeddable viewer + share docs | Open `/bike-3d-brew/app/embed-demo.html` (also on the phone): the top bike is an iframe; **Next ›**, **Drivetrain**, **Green screen**, **Get state** drive it and the events show up in the log. The bottom one is a `<bike-viewer>` element opening on the Cockpit: it looks the same as the customer link while the page around it keeps its own serif font. Copy a snippet from the page into any HTML file to embed on another site. Customer links now take `&area=hs-fork`. |"],[757,"| PR                                | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #18 Undo/redo for the whole scene | In **Edit**, add a comment, move it with ↑, delete it, save a view as an area, then press Ctrl/Cmd+Z (or ↶ Undo at the top of the panel) step by step: each change comes back in order; Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z, Ctrl+Y or ↷ Redo replays them. Ctrl/Cmd+Z inside a text field only undoes your typing. Click the 1 cm nudge buttons quickly: one Undo puts them all back. Reload: the scene is as you left it (the history itself starts fresh). |"],[751,"| PR                               | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #26 Real intrinsics in close-ups | Nothing new to click. Close-up ranking now uses each photo's own `camera` from `poses.json`, so a bundle packaged from a COLMAP model (`cli.mjs poses` then `package`) ranks with its real focal length. Bundles without `camera` keep the 65° iPhone default. `npm test` runs `photos.test.ts`, including the fallback for bad camera values. |"],[753,"| PR                              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #27 Spec sheet on short screens | Open the preview viewer, add 6+ rows in Edit → Spec sheet, switch to Present on a laptop-size window: the first card shows 4 specs in two columns and **All specs (k)**; the bike sits fully above the card. On a phone the card is a bottom sheet as before. |"],[752,"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #28 Save the capture checklist | On the iPhone: during a capture tap **Checklist** and tick a few close-ups, then export the bundle. In the zip, `manifest.json` has `\"checklist\": [{ \"id\", \"label\", \"done\" }]` with your ticks; it is left out when the bike has no checklist items. The viewer does not read it yet. The app itself is only compiled by the iOS CI check (no simulator run here). |"],[754,"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #15 Auto-publish + PR previews | Open the home page: **PR previews** lists open PRs with Viewer and Docs links; open `/bike-3d-brew/pr/15/app/` and the demo bike loads. Push to a PR and its preview updates a few minutes later (Actions → \"PR preview\"); close it and it disappears from the list. Merging into `develop` updates the main site (Actions → \"Publish site\"). |"],[755,"| PR                             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #17 Site follows the stack tip | The home page has no credits box any more. Push to the top PR of the stack (or press *Run workflow* on Actions → \"Publish site\" from it): the main site shows that branch a few minutes later (the footer names it). Pushes to other branches skip publishing. |"],[747,"| PR                          | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #22 Snapshot / video export | Click **Snapshot**: pick 4×, Transparent, Show pins, **Save PNG**: the file opens with a see-through background and numbered pins. Chroma green gives a solid key color with no floor shadow. **Record 360° WebM** turns the camera once around the bike (8 s) and downloads a video; the view returns to where it was. In Safari the button says MP4. |"],[750,"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| #25 COLMAP binary models | Nothing to click in the viewer. Locally, with a COLMAP sparse model in binary form (`cameras.bin`, `images.bin`, no `model_converter` step): `node tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses --colmap sparse_bin -o poses.json` writes the same poses as the TXT model. `npm test` runs `reconstruct.test.ts` on both formats, including truncated binary files. |"],[736,"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |"],[741,"| PR                      | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #8 Share with customers | Open the published demo as a customer: `/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present` (on your phone too). Swipe between areas, tap a pin (leader line to its card), add `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play that pauses when you touch it. In the editor, **Share** on a published scene copies the link; on a local capture it exports a `.bikeshare.zip` that `node tools/publish-scene.mjs <zip>` installs. In Edit mode, drag comments to reorder them and use **bold**, *italic* and `- ` lists in bodies. |"],[742,"| PR              | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #12 Performance | Orbit the demo, then let go: the camera glides to a stop and the page goes quiet (DevTools → Performance shows no frames while idle). Pins slide with the bike and dim when the bike is in front of them. On a phone, open a large capture: it appears, then picking a comment point is instant. Add `?quality=low` to the URL for the cheapest rendering. A GLB made with `node tools/optimize-glb.mjs in.glb out.glb` opens like any other. |"],[748,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #13 Spec sheet | In **Edit**, the **Spec sheet** section lists the demo's specs: change a value, remove a row, **+ Add spec** and Tab from the name to the value. Clear a value: that row disappears from **Present** but stays in the editor. **Present** shows a \"Key specs\" table on the first card only; **Export** has a `specs` array. The customer link (`?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present`) shows it too, on a phone as part of the bottom sheet. |"],[739,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #9 Auto-orient | Make a tilted bundle (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out tilted.bikecapture.zip`) and **Open…** it: the bike stands up facing right and the toast says \"Auto-oriented\". In **Edit** try ↶ Undo at the top of the panel (back to lying on its side), then in **Edit → Model**, Auto-orient, the rotate ±90° buttons, Turn 180°, and type a real length in cm. Pin a comment first: it stays on the same spot through every rotation. |"],[738,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |"],[745,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #16 WebKit E2E | Nothing new to click. On a Mac: `npx playwright install webkit && npm run e2e:webkit` runs the iPhone flows in Safari's engine (45 tests). Open the customer link in Safari on your phone: no console error when the Present card changes height. |"],[735,"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |"],[740,"| PR           | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #10 Crop box | Make an area-mode bundle with a floor and clutter (`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --out area.bikecapture.zip --rotate 0,0,0 --offset 0,0,0 --ground --mode area`) and **Open…** it: the toast suggests cropping. In **Edit → Model → Crop** turn the crop on, press **Fit to bike** (floor and crate disappear), then drag a face handle with the mouse or a finger: the camera must not orbit while dragging. Comments can't be pinned on cropped-away parts, and pins outside the box hide. |"],[737,"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |"],[561,"| Property                                 | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                                                  | Mitigation                                                                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Thin parts (spokes ~2 mm, cables, chain) | Few pixels wide, so few features. Dense MVS fills them in or drops them. Meshes come out with webbed wheels or no spokes. | Close passes at the wheels; accept \"disc\" wheels or model spokes procedurally later; splats handle them better than meshes. |"],[562,"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                                                                       | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Glossy / metallic paint, chrome | Highlights move with the viewpoint, which breaks feature matching and creates holes and bumps. | Diffuse, overcast-like light (softboxes, cloudy day, shade); polarizer; dulling / 3D-scanning spray (AESUB Blue vanishes in about 4 h) on matte-safe parts only, never without the shop's OK. |"],[564,"| Property                        | Effect on photogrammetry                               | Mitigation                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Size ~1.7 × 1 m, open structure | Background visible through the frame; masking matters. | Plain backdrop or a turntable; object masking (Object Capture does it, COLMAP does not). |"],[563,"| Property                  | Effect on photogrammetry      | Mitigation                                                               |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Black tyres, black carbon | Low texture, so few features. | More light; textured backdrop and floor so the camera poses still solve. |"],[565,"| Property        | Effect on photogrammetry                       | Mitigation                                                    |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Symmetric sides | Matching can confuse the left and right sides. | Overlapping rings, top-down ring, markers/props on the floor. |"],[530,"| Question                       | Decision                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| What is the customer page for? | **Informing, not selling**: 3D, components, upgrades. Its one action is **Talk to a salesperson**. No hold, reservation or checkout. |"],[529,"| Question                     | Decision                                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Which shops and bikes first? | **New bikes only**: shops showing their current-season models. No used bikes, so no condition notes. |"],[531,"| Question      | Decision                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Launch market | **US**: English, USD, email or SMS replies, plus a call button. Privacy section adapted: CCPA/CPRA-style notice, and TCPA consent for texts. |"],[532,"| Question | Decision                                                                  |\n| ---