github/workflows/pages.yml` | Set up Bun + cache both lockfiles; retain Node; frozen installs before `tools/publish-pages.sh`. | `publish-pages.sh` uses npm/node today; retain until converted. |"],[109,"| Workflow                    | Planned changes                                                                                        | Node requirement                           |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `.github/workflows/ios.yml` | No package-manager change unless inspection confirms web dependencies; currently Swift/Xcode workflow. | Swift/Xcode toolchain only; no Bun needed. |"],[105,"| Workflow                   | Planned changes                                                                                                                                                                    | Node requirement                                                                      |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Replace npm setup/cache/install/run with setup-bun, cache path above, frozen Bun install, `bun run` and `bunx playwright install`. Docs job uses docs lock/cache and Bun commands. | Retain setup-node for Node-based Playwright, scripts, and coverage-summary `node -e`. |"],[81,"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."],[304,"1. The bet"],[325,"10. Where the two drafts disagreed"],[305,"2. Challenging the three-screen brief"],[306,"3. People and their jobs"],[307,"4. The screens"],[308,"4.1 Studio: Library"],[317,"4.10 Studio: Settings"],[318,"4.11 Platform console (us, later)"],[319,"4.12 iPhone app"],[309,"4.2 Studio: Bike workspace"],[310,"4.3 Bike page (the customer view)"],[311,"4.4 Show customer and Window mode (the shop floor)"],[312,"4.5 Storefront"],[313,"4.6 Embed"],[314,"4.7 Talk to a salesperson"],[315,"4.8 Studio: Messages"],[316,"4.9 Studio: Captures"],[320,"5. How people move between screens"],[321,"6. What we will not build, and why"],[322,"7. Data and backend"],[323,"8. Phases"],[324,"9. Owner decisions"],[460,"a \"my drafts\" list."],[419,"a \"Recently sold\" row."],[499,"A `/app/proto/` page on the PR preview with tabs: Studio · Bike workspace · Bike page · Show customer · Storefront ·\nTalk to a salesperson."],[482,"a `poster`;"],[223,"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."],[483,"a branding reference."],[145,"A Bun runtime upgrade can expose Node compatibility gaps; keep runtime fixed at Node 22 and pin Bun 1.4.4."],[137,"a full CI run (web, docs, both E2E shards, merged coverage);"],[417,"a grid of live bikes with turntable thumbnails;"],[138,"a PR preview build from this PR;"],[329,"A shop does not buy \"3D\". It buys **customers who arrive already understanding the bike**: which groupset,\nwhich wheels, what the upgrade path costs, and why this model and not the one below it. That makes floor time\nshorter and the conversation better. Every view is judged by one question: does it help a customer understand\na specific bike, or help a salesperson explain it?"],[719,"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."],[815,"A third project, `webkit`, runs the iPhone 14 profile in Playwright's WebKit (the engine of iPhone\nSafari) over the view, edit, present, photos, share and files specs. It is opt-in\n(`npm run e2e:webkit`, after `npx playwright install webkit`; the global setup also needs Chromium, which renders the photo fixtures) and local-only for now: on GitHub's\nGPU-less macOS runners every WebKit page load timed out (WebGL), see ROADMAP. It found two\nSafari-only issues: a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error from the Present card's height update\n(now applied on the next frame), and test contexts without OPFS, where captures use the\nIndexedDB fallback."],[424,"a whole-catalog embed (the storefront grid in an iframe);"],[132,"add `packageManager: \"bun@1.4.4\"`;"],[181,"Added"],[177,"Adopt Bun 1.4.4 as package manager only in a staged migration, retaining Node 22 as runtime for CI and browser tooling. Measurements show exact tested versions, deterministic text locks, frozen install success, and about 4x/5x faster warm installs in this one local trial. The runtime trial is mixed: web/docs build and plain Node-compatible tools worked, while Vitest failed on `ProgressEvent`; Playwright runtime was only listed, not browser-executed. This is trial evidence, not a claim of cold-cache or CI performance."],[192,"Agent setup: `CLAUDE.md` is now `AGENTS.md` (shared by Claude Code and Codex, `CLAUDE.md` imports it) with a table of which tool runs each role; one persona skill per role in `.agents/skills/` (web, viewer, iOS, quality, docs, security, junior, plus `architect` and `delegation`), platform-prefixed wrappers in `.claude/agents/claude-<role>.md` and `.codex/agents/codex-<role>.toml`, and `orca.yaml` with the worktree setup script. (#23)"],[796,"All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."],[709,"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."],[1,"Architecture"],[363,"Archived models leave the public site."],[623,"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"],[207,"Auto-orient captures: a scanned bike is stood upright facing +X (PCA + side-view ground line, bike-shaped sign heuristics) on first load, with a toast; Edit → Model has Auto-orient, rotate ±90° per axis, flip, turn 180°, scale, real length in cm, 1 cm nudges, on-ground, undo and reset. Comments stay attached. `tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs` generates tilted test bundles. (#9)"],[202,"Auto-publish: every push to `develop` republishes the site (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`), and each open PR from this repo gets a preview at `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer), removed when the PR closes (`pr-preview.yml`), listed under \"PR previews\" on the home and Progress pages from `/pr/index.json`. `tools/publish-pages.sh` gains `--pr`, `--title` and `--remove-pr`, only replaces its own part of gh-pages (the main site keeps `/pr/`), and retries on the latest gh-pages when another run pushed first. (#15)"],[82,"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."],[10,"BikePresenter controller API"],[526,"Brand scans of new-bike models shared across their dealers."],[816,"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."],[142,"Bun as the *runtime* (`--bun`) is a separate, later decision. It is blocked by the Vitest/three.js\n`ProgressEvent` failure and needs its own trial."],[143,"Bun may install lifecycle dependencies differently across macOS/Linux or architectures; exercise frozen installs and actual esbuild/Next/Playwright jobs on Ubuntu before lock deletion."],[84,"Bun migration plan"],[185,"Bun migration plan (`docs/BUN-MIGRATION.md`, trial evidence in `docs/BUN-TRIAL.md`): Bun 1.4.4 as the package manager, with Node 22 kept as the runtime; one atomic cutover PR (lockfiles + scripts + `ci.yml`/`pages.yml`/`pr-preview.yml` + `orca.yaml`) followed by a docs and agent cleanup PR. Trial: same package versions, frozen lock stable, 102 E2E passed via `bun run`; Vitest under the Bun runtime fails (`ProgressEvent`). (#34)"],[151,"Bun trial evidence"],[110,"Cache keys: include lockfile hash and OS; docs must key its own lock. Never cache `node_modules`. Keep setup-node after setup-bun in jobs where runtime Node is used."],[524,"Calendar-backed test rides, and optional deposits where a shop asks for them."],[823,"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."],[237,"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."],[213,"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"],[5,"Capture cache (browser storage)"],[188,"Capture checklist saved: the iOS app keeps each checklist item (id, label, done, pass) in the bike's `record.json`, and exported bundles carry an optional `checklist: [{id, label, done}]` in `manifest.json` (left out when empty). The viewer does not read it yet. Only the iOS CI build checks the Swift code. (#28)"],[554,"Capture protocol (photos)"],[555,"Capture protocol (video)"],[210,"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"],[100,"Change `orca.yaml:4` worktree bootstrap to `bun install --frozen-lockfile`; update onboarding and commands listed below."],[179,"Changelog"],[730,"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"],[287,"Chromium + SwiftShader, 1280×800 at 1×, on a shared 4-core container under heavy load (other jobs\nrunning): treat absolute times as noisy, compare before/after. `tools/bench/bench.mjs --model big.usdz`\n(synthetic 23 MB USDZ, 972k triangles, 2048² textures), base branch vs. this change:"],[795,"CI runs both E2E shards with `E2E_COVERAGE`, uploads each shard's `coverage-final.json`, and a\n`coverage` job merges them with a fresh unit run, checks the merged thresholds, prints the totals\n(and `app.ts` / `Viewer.ts` / `main.ts`) in its step summary and uploads `coverage-all/`. So CI's\nE2E runs the unminified build; a local `npm run e2e` still tests the minified production build."],[626,"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"],[588,"Close-ups (0.4–0.6 m), 4–6 shots each, overlapping each other: drivetrain (both sides of the\nrear derailleur, chainring), fork crown and dropouts, cockpit (bar, stem, shifters), saddle and\nseat clamp, each wheel hub and a sector of spokes from both sides."],[190,"COLMAP binary models: `tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses` reads `cameras.bin`, `images.bin` and `points3D.bin` directly (no `model_converter` step); TXT is preferred when both exist, and a missing or unreadable `points3D` is a warning, not an error. Binary parsing is bounds-checked and tested against the TXT output. (#25)"],[575,"COLMAP poses are world→camera with OpenCV axes (+X right, +Y down, +Z forward). The viewer\nwants camera→model with camera looking down -Z, +Y up. So:\n`T_c2w = inverse([R|t]) = [Rᵀ | -Rᵀt]`, then flip the camera's Y and Z axes:\n`pose = T_c2w · diag(1, -1, -1, 1)`. COLMAP quaternions are `QW QX QY QZ` (Hamilton,\nworld→camera)."],[684,"Commercial plan (screens for shops, the shop floor and customers; phases; owner decisions): docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md."],[130,"commit `bun.lock` and `apps/docs/bun.lock`, regenerated from the current manifests;"],[710,"Compare two bikes side by side."],[3,"Contracts"],[99,"Convert nested npm calls so `bun run` doesn't silently invoke npm: root `package.json:25-26` (`docs:dev`, `docs:build`); `apps/docs/package.json:8-11` (`dev`, `build`, `typecheck`); the Playwright `webServer` command in `apps/web/playwright.config.ts:61-64`; `tools/publish-pages.sh:78-83`; and optionally npx invocations in `tools/bench/bench.mjs:33-36`, `tools/optimize-glb.mjs:73`. Use `bun run --cwd apps/docs ...` / `bunx` or local executable paths and keep Node commands that are runtime-specific."],[133,"convert the nested npm/npx calls (the `docs:*` scripts, `apps/docs` scripts, the Playwright `webServer`, and\n`tools/publish-pages.sh`);"],[425,"copy-paste guides for Shopify, WooCommerce and Squarespace."],[762,"Coverage"],[206,"Crop box: Edit → Model → Crop clips everything outside an axis-aligned box (model-root space, saved as optional `crop` in `bike-scene/1`) with renderer clipping planes; drag the face handles (mouse or touch) or type the corners; \"Fit to bike\" removes the floor slab and background clusters. Cropped-away geometry can't take comments, and comments outside the box are hidden. Area-mode captures get a suggested box and a hint. (#10)"],[215,"Customer link and Present mode in Safari: the card-height update no longer triggers a \"ResizeObserver loop\" page error. (#16)"],[373,"Customers can filter by kind on the bike page."],[528,"Decided on 12 Nov 2026:"],[92,"Decision: adopt Bun 1.4.4 as the package manager; keep Node 22 as the runtime for now. Trial evidence is in BUN-TRIAL.md. Bun migrated both npm locks with matching tested package versions, `--frozen-lockfile` was stable, package builds passed, and warm installs were faster in this single local sample. Vitest under Bun runtime failed in three errors including `ReferenceError: ProgressEvent is not defined` in three.js. Browser E2E passed with Bun as script runner and Node/Playwright binaries; actual Playwright runtime support remains unverified."],[131,"delete both `package-lock.json` files;"],[37,"Details and measurements: PERFORMANCE.md."],[232,"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."],[211,"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"],[80,"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"],[779,"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."],[487,"Drafts are private. Published versions are public and cacheable."],[240,"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."],[763,"E2E coverage"],[508,"Each bike page is generated as static HTML when it is published, with Open Graph tags, so texts and\nInstagram previews work without a page server."],[364,"Each card shows the one number that matters in its state: views or messages when live, readiness when draft."],[73,"Embed → parent: `{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", event, detail }` for `ready` and `state`\n(`{ index, areas, playing, id, name }`), `areachange`, `commentopen` and `error` (the\npresenter's details)."],[195,"Embeddable viewer + share docs: `embed.html` (customer view in an iframe with a validated `bike-embed/1` postMessage bridge, optional `?origin=` lock), a `<bike-viewer src area kiosk>` custom element (`/app/bike-viewer.js`, shadow DOM with its own CSS; `styles.css` variables now on `:root, :host`), the `embed-demo.html` page with copy-paste snippets, `&area=` on customer links; ARCHITECTURE documents `bike-share/1`, the BikePresenter controller API and the embed protocol; `share.spec.ts` and the new `embed.spec.ts` also run on the mobile project. (#20)"],[11,"Embedding on a shop's site"],[728,"Embedding on a shop's site: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/embed-demo.html**\nshows the bike in an iframe driven by the buttons under it, and as a `<bike-viewer>` element."],[376,"Encodes what a good listing needs."],[767,"End-to-end tests"],[489,"Events: page view, model ready or failed, area opened, component or upgrade opened, contact button tapped, message\nsent, QR or campaign source."],[792,"every Chromium test starts `page.coverage` (`apps/web/e2e/test.ts`, the `test` all specs import;\nWebKit has no V8 coverage and is skipped); each worker merges its tests' V8 data and writes one\nfile to `coverage-e2e/raw/`;"],[462,"Every link carries its source (QR, Instagram, embed), so Messages and the Library know which channel works."],[183,"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."],[821,"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."],[783,"Excluded from unit coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead\n(and counted in the merged report, see \"E2E coverage\" below):"],[15,"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools. Exports\n(`Viewer.snapshot` / `recordTurntable`, decisions in `scene/exportMedia.ts`) re-render the model with a\ntransparent clear onto a 2D canvas over the chosen backdrop (CSS gradients redrawn, chroma green, or\nnothing) and optionally the pins (`PinLayer.drawInto`); video goes through `canvas.captureStream` + MediaRecorder."],[418,"filters for type, brand, size and price;"],[819,"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"],[176,"First merged-coverage compound command failed due to unrelated port 4190 occupancy. The requested isolated full E2E on port 4292 passed."],[182,"Fixed"],[764,"Fixtures"],[776,"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."],[484,"Following AGENTS.md, that contract change ships first and alone. `bike-share/1` stays a portable package; it is\nnot a permission model."],[600,"For a dense textured mesh use OpenMVS (`InterfaceCOLMAP` → `DensifyPointCloud` → `ReconstructMesh`\n→ `RefineMesh` → `TextureMesh`) from its Docker image, or COLMAP's dense steps on a CUDA machine."],[104,"For docs jobs use key `${{ runner.os }}-bun-docs-${{ hashFiles('apps/docs/bun.lock') }}` and `bun install --cwd apps/docs --frozen-lockfile`. Keep setup-node in the jobs while their scripts/tools use Node. `ci.yml` has a trial-only implementation of this shape; it keeps Node in all jobs for current scripts and changes root/docs package commands."],[76,"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."],[214,"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"],[52,"Front sign: the wide handlebar sits ahead of centre (plus a small vote for the drivetrain mass\nbehind it). Drive side follows from the right-handed frame."],[97,"Generate and commit text `bun.lock` at root and `apps/docs/bun.lock` from the current manifests. Remove `package-lock.json` and `apps/docs/package-lock.json` in the lockfile cutover PR; don't maintain two authoritative locks. Trial locks are generated from the current npm locks, with tested versions matching."],[87,"GitHub Actions"],[559,"Goal: **any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) → a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer\nopens**: a model (GLB preferred), `poses.json`, `images/` and `manifest.json`. Today the only\nproducer is the iOS Object Capture app."],[218,"Goals"],[50,"Ground line: the longest downward-facing edge of the side-view convex hull (tangent across\nboth tyres) fixes the 5–15° tilt PCA leaves."],[328,"How it was written: Claude and Codex each drafted a proposal independently from the same inputs. The drafts\nwere merged and the disagreements settled (section 10). A Codex red-team\nthen attacked the merged plan as a shop owner, a customer on a cheap Android and the phase 1 engineer, and its\ntwelve findings are applied here."],[731,"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."],[714,"How to test"],[612,"Ideas parking lot"],[411,"If the network or a model fails, it falls back to that bike's poster with its price, then to a shop slide\n(logo, hours, \"Ask inside\"). It recovers on its own when the network returns."],[22,"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted; when `manifest.photos` names a non-empty folder, its JPEGs are used instead of the HEICs\n(pose `file` names like `IMG_0007.HEIC` match `IMG_0007.jpg` by stem), so no browser needs the\nWASM HEIC decoder. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."],[441,"Incoming uploads from the iPhone app (roadmap: Upload to viewer), and later photo/video reconstruction jobs\n(Milestone 1.5)."],[152,"Install scripts and compatibility failures"],[88,"Inventory of npm/Node assumptions"],[525,"Inventory or POS import where demand is proven."],[625,"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"],[200,"iOS capture guidance + JPEG photos: the capture screen has a checklist (3 orbits at hub height, saddle height and top-down, ticked as Object Capture completes each pass; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur and cockpit; shots per pass; reflective-paint tips, and why a turntable does not work with on-device Object Capture). Exported bundles add `photos/*.jpg` (2048 px, upright) listed as `manifest.photos`, and the web viewer uses them instead of decoding HEIC. (#14)"],[519,"iPhone Upload → Captures, the readiness check fed by the capture checklist."],[149,"Is there a policy preference for pinning GitHub Actions by SHA in addition to version tags?"],[501,"It also runs the hosting cost spike."],[69,"It imports no CSS: a page brings `styles.css`, `ui/present.css` and `present/present.css`.\nTheir custom properties are declared on `:root, :host` and every other rule is class-scoped, so\nthe same files work in a shadow root."],[420,"It is deliberately thin. Most shops already have a website, so the **Embed is the main way customers arrive**,\nand the storefront serves shops without a site and Instagram bio links."],[406,"It is phase 2, and we confirm with the pilot shop that they actually use it before polishing it."],[412,"It keeps the screen awake through the Wake Lock API, and the setup guide covers the display's own sleep settings."],[410,"It refreshes the bike list every few minutes and drops any bike that is no longer Live, so the window never\nshows a sold or held bike as available."],[53,"It runs once when a scene is opened with a non-demo model, no comments and no `model.rotation`\n(`shouldAutoOrient`); the offset is then recomputed from exact bounds so the bike stands on the\nground. Edit → Model exposes the result plus manual rotate/flip/scale/nudge, each one store\nupdate and so one step of the scene's undo history (`SceneStore`: every edit pushes the previous\nscene, edits with the same merge key less than a second apart share a step, `replace` is not a\nstep and a new scene id clears the history; Ctrl/Cmd+Z in Edit mode). Generate tilted test bundles with\n`node tools/fixtures/make-bike-capture.mjs --rotate 70,25,-40` (ASCII USD mesh in `model.usdz`)."],[416,"It shows:"],[500,"It uses the demo bike and made-up data, so the owner can try each screen on a laptop, an iPad and a phone."],[733,"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."],[94,"Keep `bun run` as the script entry point, but note scripts with `node` commands and shebang binaries still dispatch Node. Use Node explicitly for runtime-sensitive tests until Bun runtime is independently green."],[93,"Keep Node 22 installed and on PATH for Playwright, npm scripts' explicit `node` calls, `node --test`, docs scripts and Next/MDX until each is intentionally moved and verified. The trial's successful `bun --bun run docs:build` is one result, not enough evidence to remove Node from all environments."],[270,"Known gaps"],[381,"Later edits stay in the draft until the shop publishes again, so customers never see half-finished work."],[86,"Local changes"],[717,"Make a synthetic capture bundle"],[245,"Manual steps"],[614,"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."],[510,"Measure how long listing one bike takes, step by step, with the shop's staff."],[712,"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."],[36,"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."],[268,"Measuring"],[135,"migrate `ci.yml`, `pages.yml` and `pr-preview.yml` as in the table above."],[604,"Milestone 0: Project ops"],[605,"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"],[606,"Milestone 1.5: Photos & video → 3D"],[607,"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"],[608,"Milestone 3: Sales experience"],[609,"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"],[610,"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"],[611,"Milestone 6: Quality"],[390,"Model bytes load only when the visitor taps \"View in 3D\" when the phone signals Save-Data, a slow connection\nor low memory; otherwise they load once the page is idle."],[486,"Models and photos are 5–30 MB objects with stable IDs, uploaded through signed URLs."],[822,"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."],[127,"No `.nvmrc` or `.node-version` was found. `apps/ios/README.md` has no JS package setup. `apps/web/vite.config.ts` and `apps/docs/next.config.mjs` don't otherwise configure a package manager. Docs build uses Next and should retain Node toolchain pending wider verification."],[300,"No runtime decimation: phones get the full capture unless it went through `optimize-glb --simplify`."],[222,"Non-goals (for now)"],[298,"Not yet measured on a real iPhone (ROADMAP: \"Measure on a real iPhone\")."],[572,"Notes:"],[438,"Notifications by email, and SMS for the shop if it wants, for each new message."],[173,"npm emitted its local `allow-scripts` policy warnings: root `fsevents@2.3.3` (optional platform package) and docs `esbuild@0.28.2` (`node install.js`). Bun emitted no untrusted-script warning; `bun pm untrusted` reported zero. Bun-created dependencies passed Vite, Next, and docs builds, including esbuild-dependent operations. No `sharp` package exists in either lockfile; the `sharp` mentions in `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` describe an optional install. `package-lock.json` marks only fsevents and docs esbuild with `hasInstallScript`."],[573,"Object Capture is the only option with **automatic object masking** built in, which matters for\nthe \"background-free\" goal. With COLMAP the bundle needs masking (rembg / U²-Net on the\nphotos before MVS, or cropping the mesh to the dominant cluster after)."],[51,"Object Capture output is gravity-aligned, so if that up is within 6° of ±Y, Y is kept exactly\nand only yaw changes (horizontal PCA)."],[31,"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."],[716,"On a laptop"],[827,"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."],[715,"On your phone (no setup)"],[101,"Onboarding should state Bun 1.4.4 and Node 22 prerequisites, then:"],[450,"One person can belong to several shops."],[504,"One shop's hosted listings. There is no signup; we create the shop and its staff logins."],[490,"Only aggregate counters per bike, per day and per source. Phase 1 has no session hash and no device storage.\nIP addresses are not stored with events, and server logs are kept for 30 days for operations only."],[74,"Only messages whose `source` is the framing window are read. With `?origin=` the embed accepts\ncommands only from that origin and posts events only to it; an origin that does not parse\nmatches nothing. Without it, any framing page may drive the bike and events are posted to `*`\n(they only carry the public scene's names and ids)."],[13,"Open questions (verify on device)"],[91,"Open questions for owner"],[720,"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."],[267,"Optimizing a capture"],[140,"Optional tool scripts (`tools/bench`, `tools/optimize-glb.mjs`) can keep `npx` for now; it still works when\nNode is installed."],[552,"Options"],[236,"Overview"],[557,"Owner decisions"],[258,"Owner decisions for turning any photo set or video into a model (details in RECONSTRUCTION.md):"],[392,"Pages are generated as static HTML with Open Graph tags, so link previews in texts and social apps look right."],[72,"Parent → embed: `{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", cmd, … }` with `cmd` one of `next`, `prev`, `play`,\n`pause`, `getState`, `goToArea` (`area`: integer index, hotspot id or `null`), `setBackground`\n(`background`: a background mode), `openComment` (`id`). `parseEmbedCommand` validates every\nmessage; anything else is ignored (never evaluated)."],[299,"Parsing and welding a big USDZ still run on the main thread (~1 s together for 1M triangles on a\ndesktop CPU, more on a phone); ROADMAP \"Progressive capture loading\"."],[48,"PCA: smallest-variance axis = the bike's width, middle axis = candidate up."],[265,"Performance"],[203,"Performance: the viewer renders on demand (an idle stage draws 0 frames, the loop pauses in hidden tabs), redraws the shadow map only when the scene changes, caps the pixel ratio per device (`?quality=low|high`), welds USDZ meshes into indexed geometry (2.9M → 0.49M vertices on a 1M-triangle capture), builds a BVH in a worker so picking and pin occlusion cost ~0.05 ms instead of ~200 ms, and updates 50+ pins with budgeted occlusion and transform-only writes. GLBs with Meshopt, Draco or KTX2 load with lazily fetched, self-hosted decoders; `tools/optimize-glb.mjs` makes phone-friendly GLBs; `tools/bench/bench.mjs` measures it all. See `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`. (#12)"],[515,"Phase 1b only starts once a real request has come in through phase 1a."],[12,"Photo close-ups"],[209,"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"],[246,"Photos & video → 3D"],[204,"Photos & video → 3D research (`docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md`): reconstruction options for bikes, recommendation (Object Capture on macOS by default, COLMAP + OpenMVS as fallback, splats later), photo and video capture protocols, owner decisions; new ROADMAP Milestone 1.5. (#11)"],[550,"Photos & video → 3D: reconstruction options for bikes"],[481,"pin `kind` (component, upgrade), and for upgrades the part names and price difference;"],[96,"Pin Bun with `\"packageManager\": \"bun@1.4.4\"` in root `package.json` and `apps/docs/package.json`; keep `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=22.12\"}` while Node scripts remain."],[556,"Pipeline (`tools/reconstruct/`)"],[326,"Planning document for the commercial product: who uses it, which screens it has, how they connect, what we\ndeliberately do not build, and in what order. Nothing here is built unless marked **exists**. Owner decisions\nare collected in section 9."],[814,"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos, share, embed). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."],[340,"Plus two screens the brief did not name, which a shop will ask for in week one:"],[191,"Preview ops: `prune-previews.yml` runs daily and removes the `/pr/<n>/` preview of every closed PR, and squashes gh-pages history once it passes 200 commits (force-with-lease on the base it read); `pr-preview.yml` keeps one sticky comment with the Docs and Viewer links on each PR. (#24)"],[505,"Private drafts and published snapshots."],[624,"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"],[219,"Product"],[184,"Product plan updated with the owner's decisions (`docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md`): new bikes only; the customer page is a showroom (3D, components, upgrades) whose one action is **Talk to a salesperson** by email or SMS, with no hold or checkout; US market first (English, USD, TCPA consent for texts); Leads are now Messages; condition notes, reservations and WhatsApp removed. (#35)"],[186,"Product views plan (`docs/PRODUCT-VIEWS.md`): the commercial screens for bike shops (Studio: Library, Bike workspace, Leads, Captures, Settings; the customer Bike page with Show customer and Window modes; Storefront; Embed; Request form; a later Platform console), with wireframes, navigation, what we will not build, data model, phases 0–3 (phase 1 split into a one-shop pilot slice) and owner decisions; written from two independent drafts (Claude and Codex) and hardened by a Codex red-team (privacy roles, structured condition claims, low-bandwidth budget, reservation expiry). (#30)"],[303,"Product views: bike-3d-brew for bike shops"],[548,"Progress"],[233,"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."],[380,"Publish creates a public snapshot."],[229,"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."],[777,"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."],[221,"Quality bar for every PR"],[820,"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."],[234,"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."],[189,"Real intrinsics in close-ups: photo ranking uses each sample's own `camera` from `poses.json` (horizontal FOV and aspect from fx, fy, width, height) instead of the 65° iPhone assumption; implausible values fall back to 65°. (#26)"],[153,"Recommendation"],[553,"Recommendation"],[194,"Reconstruct: `tools/reconstruct/cli.mjs poses` converts a COLMAP TXT model (`cameras.txt`, `images.txt`, `points3D.txt`) into `bike-poses/1` (world→camera OpenCV → camera→model, −Z forward, +Y up; real intrinsics kept per sample as `camera`), and `cli.mjs package` turns a model (GLB / USDZ / PLY), JPEG frames and poses into a `bike-capture/1` zip with `source: photos|video` and `backend` in the manifest. Verified on synthetic COLMAP output from the fixture's ground-truth cameras and through the viewer's own bundle reader. (#19)"],[766,"Rendered-photo bundle"],[7,"Rendering and performance (`apps/web/src/viewer/`)"],[269,"Results"],[496,"Retention defaults to 12 months. Messages can be deleted or exported, staff only see their own shop's messages, and\na breach procedure is documented before the first real lead."],[585,"Ring 1, hub height (~0.35 m), distance ~1.5–2 m: 36–48 shots (every 7.5–10°)."],[586,"Ring 2, saddle height (~0.9 m), looking slightly down: 36–48 shots."],[587,"Ring 3, high (~1.6 m), looking down at 45°: 24–36 shots."],[90,"Risks and rollback"],[603,"Roadmap"],[549,"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."],[520,"Roles, lead assignment and source reports."],[146,"Roll back the package-manager switch by reverting the cutover PR: it restores both `package-lock.json` files, the npm workflow steps and the scripts in one commit. This only works because nothing else ships in that PR."],[89,"Rollout"],[280,"Rule for new code: anything that changes what the canvas shows outside the `Viewer` methods\n(a new scene object, a material tweak, clipping planes) must call `viewer.requestRender()`, or the\nchange appears only on the next camera move."],[98,"Run `bun install --frozen-lockfile` at root and `bun install --cwd apps/docs --frozen-lockfile` for docs. Use `bun pm untrusted` to audit scripts. Trial output showed no untrusted scripts; root npm had fsevents (optional) and docs had esbuild postinstall. Confirm Bun's trust behavior on CI and add `trustedDependencies` only for packages whose required install scripts demonstrably need it; validate esbuild and Next after any trust policy change."],[622,"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"],[825,"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."],[43,"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."],[243,"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."],[601,"See MANUAL-STEPS.md. In short: a Mac (Apple silicon) for the default path;\nwhether to pay for a cloud API (which vendor, monthly budget, OK with its data terms for\ncustomer bikes); a GPU box (rented or owned) for COLMAP dense / splats; whether dulling spray is\nacceptable on customer bikes."],[523,"Self-serve signup, billing, the Platform console and custom domains."],[54,"Share → \"Export share package\" turns a local capture into a self-contained zip\n(`apps/web/src/scene/share.ts`):"],[205,"Share with customers: read-only `?scene=…&view=present` link served by a standalone presenter (`present/BikePresenter.ts`, no editing code, container-scoped), Share button (share sheet / clipboard / visible link), `bike-share/1` package export + `tools/publish-scene.mjs`, published demo at `scenes/demo/`. Present mode: leader lines, progress dots, swipe, auto-play (`?kiosk=1`), phone bottom sheet; markdown-lite comment bodies (DOM-only renderer); drag / ↑↓ comment reordering. (#8)"],[514,"Shop accounts and roles, the step that turns this into a product for more than one shop."],[382,"Shops can roll back to the previous version."],[147,"Should Bun be pinned at 1.4.4 in `packageManager` and setup-bun, or should CI use a newer version before cutover? Trial used the requested 1.4.4."],[148,"Should lifecycle trust be explicitly allow-listed in `trustedDependencies` after Linux CI proves whether esbuild scripts are required, or left empty when builds pass?"],[517,"Show customer (Done ↺, QR hand-off), Compare (once the pilot confirms they use it) and Window mode."],[404,"Shows two bikes with a synced camera and the same area on both, matched by area name."],[458,"sign in with the shop account;"],[199,"Site follows the stack tip: `pages.yml` republishes whenever the newest ready PR at the top of the stack (or `develop` when none is open) is pushed, so the live site no longer waits for merges. Parallel agents work in `.claude/worktrees/` with their own E2E port; the suite no longer reuses a server it did not start. The session-credits counter is gone from the home page. (#17)"],[711,"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."],[196,"Snapshot / video export: the **Snapshot** button opens a menu: PNG at 1×, 2× or 4× the stage (shrunk to the GPU limit and 16.7 MP for iOS Safari) on the stage's backdrop, transparent or chroma green, with or without pins; and a 360° turntable video (8 s, WebM, MP4 in browsers that only record that, hidden where `MediaRecorder` cannot record a canvas). The camera, drawing buffer and clear color are restored afterwards. (#22)"],[24,"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"],[187,"Spec sheet on short screens: the Present spec table shows 4 rows with an \"All specs (k)\" / \"Fewer specs\" toggle, in two columns on wide cards; on wide stages the 3D view ends above the card, as it already did on phones, so the bike is no longer covered. (#27)"],[198,"Spec sheet: Edit mode has a \"Spec sheet\" section (label/value rows, starting from Frame material, Groupset, Weight and Sizes; add, remove, Tab between fields) saved as optional `specs` in `bike-scene/1` (validated on import: malformed rows dropped, text trimmed and capped). Present mode and the customer link show the filled rows as a \"Key specs\" table on the first (whole bike) card; Export and share packages carry them. The published demo has a sheet. (#13)"],[576,"Splats need a viewer path (Spark / `@sparkjsdev/spark`) and a crop box; pins and areas still work\nbecause they only need a surface to raycast against (a proxy mesh or splat-depth picking)."],[599,"Status and the next steps are in ROADMAP.md (Milestone 1.5). For the commands to try\nCOLMAP on Linux today (a CPU-only sparse model, enough to check the poses):"],[437,"Statuses: New, Contacted, Test ride booked, Won, Lost."],[533,"Still open; none of these block the prototype:"],[780,"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."],[399,"Studio → **Show customer**;"],[220,"Success criteria"],[286,"SwiftShader renders on the CPU, so absolute numbers are far from a phone GPU and swing with machine\nload: compare runs made back to back on the same machine, and read render counts and per-operation\ncosts rather than fps."],[271,"Targets (from GOALS.md): first model visible in **< 3 s** on iPhone Safari over 4G for a\n20 MB model, **60 fps** orbiting with **50 pins**, and **low battery use when idle**."],[193,"Test infrastructure: one fixture generator, `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, with one bike geometry and one pose layout (orbit rings + close-ups) for the E2E variants, the rendered-photo bundle (`--photos`) and the Pages sample (`--sample`); `make-test-bundle.mjs` and `make-capture.mjs` are gone. E2E coverage: `npm run e2e:coverage` records V8 coverage in Chromium, `npm run coverage:merge` merges it with the unit report into `coverage-all/` (~97% lines) so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count, with a merged ratchet checked by a new CI `coverage` job. (#21)"],[208,"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"],[759,"Testing"],[598,"Tests (`apps/web/test/reconstruct.test.ts`): COLMAP text synthesized from the fixture's ground-truth\ncameras (via COLMAP's own `x = R·X + t` definition, with shuffled image ids and sign-flipped\nquaternions) must convert back to the same transforms, project points to the same pixels in the\nconverted three.js camera, and package into a zip that the viewer's `readCaptureBundle` opens with\nevery pose matched to its photo."],[826,"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."],[493,"The **shop is the controller** of its messages, and **we are the processor**, under a data processing agreement\nin the terms of service."],[594,"The `ingest` step extracts frames, keeps the sharpest frame per short time window (variance of the\nLaplacian) and only adds a frame when the view has changed enough, aiming for 80–200 frames."],[768,"The `window.__bike` test hook"],[391,"The 3D view shows download progress, a timeout with **Retry**, and a plain failure message that leaves the\nrest of the page working."],[216,"The active comment pin (and the draft pin) drifted away from its point by 25% of its screen position because CSS `scale` also scaled the position transform. (#9)"],[725,"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."],[613,"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in AGENTS.md."],[301,"The Basis transcoder path is not exercised in CI (the KTX2 fixture is uncompressed RGBA8, since Node\nhas no Basis encoder); its files are built and served like Draco's."],[507,"The bike page within its byte budget, with component and upgrade lists and Talk to a salesperson → email or SMS."],[336,"The brief asked for an admin screen, a shop screen and a client screen. Each name hides two different things:"],[791,"the build keeps source maps and skips minification (`apps/web/vite.config.ts`), so coverage\nmaps back to `src/` line by line;"],[813,"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `--photos` variant's bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."],[426,"The embed is for discovering and looking at bikes. Its actions open the bike page or Talk to a salesperson, so\nevery lead ends up in one inbox."],[495,"The form shows a collection notice (Art. 13): who, why, how long, and how to delete. The shop configures it;\nwe provide the default."],[793,"the global teardown converts it with `ast-v8-to-istanbul` (the converter Vitest uses) to\n`coverage-e2e/coverage-final.json`, `src/` files only."],[242,"The iframe takes commands over `postMessage` (`{ type: \"bike-embed/1\", cmd: \"next\" }`); the\nelement exposes `element.presenter` and DOM events. Details in\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md."],[461,"The in-app 3D viewer (roadmap M4) is worth less than Show customer on an iPad; it moves down."],[732,"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"],[494,"The lawful basis for a request is steps taken at the customer's request before a contract (Art. 6(1)(b))."],[513,"The Library with states, logo and accent color, pin kinds, QR codes, and the embed pointed\nat the new URLs."],[174,"The only runtime failure observed was Vitest + three.js under `bun --bun`: missing global `ProgressEvent`. Keep Vitest and browser/tool execution on Node pending a dedicated runtime fix and full verification."],[389,"The page with its facts and poster stays under about 300 KB, with the poster image under about 150 KB."],[809,"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."],[509,"The privacy notice, retention and deletion from section 7."],[721,"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."],[23,"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."],[343,"The resulting screens:"],[285,"The script serves `dist/` with `vite preview`, drives Chromium on SwiftShader (like the E2E suite)\nthrough the `?e2e` test hook and prints JSON: boot time, a synchronous **frame cost** (render + a\n1-pixel readback that waits for the GPU), renders while idle and while orbiting with the mouse\n(with and without 50 pins), pin-update time per frame, and for `--model`: time until the first frame\nwith the model, geometry size, JS heap, frame cost and the cost of one `pick()` / `isOccluded()`."],[729,"The site is republished automatically on every push to the stack tip (the newest open PR nothing else is stacked on, or `develop` when none is open). Each open PR also gets its\nown copy at `https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (viewer at `/pr/<n>/app/`),\nlisted under **PR previews** on the home and Progress pages, so you can try a PR before\nmerging it. Each PR also gets a comment with Docs and Viewer links; closed previews are removed\ndaily when their PR is no longer open. The home page says which commit and branch it was built from."],[518,"The Storefront, per-bike and catalog embeds, and snippets."],[841,"The viewer renders on demand: to wait for a picture to settle use `viewer.rendering === false`; `viewer.renderCount` counts drawn frames."],[247,"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."],[405,"This is the conversation salespeople have all day: \"why is this one $2,400 more?\""],[771,"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."],[778,"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."],[32,"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"],[726,"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."],[506,"Today's editor, saving to the hosted draft instead of browser storage, with photos-only listings allowed."],[627,"Top priority: any photo set or video of a bike (any camera) must become a `bike-capture/1` bundle the viewer opens. Research and recommendation: docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md."],[154,"Trial date: 2026-11-12. Bun 1.4.4 on macOS; existing Node 24.18.0 runtime and warm npm/Bun download caches. Wall times are rounded to seconds from shell wall clock; npm baseline ran before Bun install on a clean `node_modules` for each project. Later Bun operations used Bun-created `node_modules`."],[727,"Try what a customer gets: open\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/?scene=scenes/demo/scene.bike.json&view=present**\non the phone. Only the bike, its name and price, and the Present card: swipe the card or tap\n‹ › to change area, tap a pin or a comment to fly to it, tap **Share** for the share sheet.\nAdd `&area=hs-fork` to open on the fork, or `&kiosk=1&interval=4` for auto-play."],[810,"Two more variants, written on request:"],[128,"Two PRs, each green on its own. The lockfile and the workflows switch **together**: committing `bun.lock`\nwhile CI still runs `npm ci` would leave the Bun lock untested and drifting, and two authoritative lockfiles\nis exactly what this plan avoids."],[70,"Two ways, both read-only, both on the published scene's URL rules (same origin as the embed or\nhttps). `embed-demo.html` (`/app/embed-demo.html`) shows both."],[231,"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."],[197,"Undo/redo for the whole scene: one store-level history (`SceneStore.undo/redo`, 100 steps) covers comments, areas, bike details and Edit → Model (whose own stack is gone). ↶ Undo / ↷ Redo buttons at the top of the Edit panel, Ctrl/Cmd+Z, Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z and Ctrl+Y (not while typing in a field); rapid 1 cm nudges merge into one step; opening another scene starts a fresh history. (#18)"],[760,"Unit tests"],[180,"Unreleased"],[49,"Up sign by votes: the centroid sits below mid-height (wheels), and the top band (handlebar) is\nwider across than the bottom band (two tyre contact patches)."],[134,"update `orca.yaml`;"],[782,"